window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS=(window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51 | Plans For The Future","paragraphs":["Then, suddenly, an intriguing, dangerous idea appeared in his mind.","Crimson flames burned steadily in his left hand.","Blue lightning crackled violently in his right hand.","What would happen if he tried to combine these two highly destructive elements together?","Slowly, he began to move his hands closer together, bringing the two energies toward the center of his chest.","Instantly—","A powerful, alarming sense of danger rang out within his mind.","Dexter’s expression changed immediately, his face turning slightly pale. His heartbeat accelerated rapidly, his chest heaving.","The closer the two energies became, the more violently unstable they felt. It was as though he was trying to force two violently opposing storms into a single, tiny bottle.","If they actually collided and reacted—","The resulting elemental explosion would probably blow up his entire bedroom, and perhaps even injure him severely despite his enhanced physique.","’ Nop! I’m not dying anytime soon.’","Dexter immediately pulled his hands apart, extinguishing both energies.","The intense warning feeling in his mind disappeared almost instantly.","He let out a slow, shaky breath.","\"That was incredibly dangerous...\" he whispered.","Fortunately, his curiosity had not got him killed tonight. The blue lightning slowly faded away into the dark air.","Then, another thought entered his mind.","If the violent, chaotic thunder could not merge with the crimson flames of the Flame Demon bloodline...","What about the Golden Flames?","\"Whoosh!\"","A pure, bright golden fire erupted above his right palm.","Unlike the violent, blood-red crimson flames, these golden flames felt noble, pure, and incredibly stable, like the light of a divine being.","The bright golden light illuminated every corner of his bedroom, casting warm, clear shadows.","Although the golden flame was highly powerful, its temperature felt noticeably lower and far more controlled than the Ancient Flame Demon’s crimson fire.","Dexter stared at the two distinct flames quietly.","Crimson in his left hand and gold flame in his right hand.","Them slowly, he began bringing them together once more.","However, as Dexter slowly brought the crimson flames and golden flames closer, his internal warning system activated once more.","But this time, the sense of danger was not nearly as overwhelming or terrifying as when he had attempted to combine the lightning and the fire.","Earlier, his instincts had practically screamed at him but this time, the warning felt more like a strong suggestion of caution.","Dexter narrowed his eyes thoughtfully in the golden light.","\"So it can probably be done...\" he murmured.","\"It just isn’t something I shouldn’t try inside the house.\"","The last thing he wanted to do was to accidentally blow up their small bungalow and turn the girls homeless overnight.","He immediately extinguished both flames, returning the room to its natural darkness.","If he was going to experiment with advanced elemental fusion, he would have to find a highly secure, professional facility to do so safely.","Perhaps a Hero Training Facility.","Or one of the public combat testing grounds located in the mid-districts of the city.","Unfortunately...","Dexter still did not possess an official Hero License.","Without a license, he was still technically considered an ordinary, unawakened civilian by the government, despite possessing a personal strength that could easily rival some veterans.","Hero training grounds were heavily regulated, high-security facilities designed specifically for awakened individuals to train and test their highly destructive abilities safely.","Unauthorized civilians were not allowed entry under any circumstances, and trying to sneak in could result in immediate arrest.","Dexter sighed softly.","That was another important task to add to tomorrow’s busy schedule.","His thoughts soon drifted back toward a much more immediate, practical problem.","Money.","Thirty thousand dollars sounded like a massive fortune to someone from the lower districts.","Until one actually started spending it on high-grade necessities.","A new, comfortable bed for himself.","Three proper, supportive beds for the girls.","Decent furniture to replace their chairs.","Basic household necessities.","Ten thousand credits could easily disappear in the blink of an eye.","Then, there were the heavy medical expenses.","Especially Selene’s medication.","Although the frequency and severity of her freezing episodes had decreased significantly recently hte painful attacks still happened at least once every single day.","Fortunately, thanks to his newly acquired Frost Sense, Dexter could usually detect the cold buildup of frost mana within her body nearly a minute before an attack actually began.","That gave him enough time to prepare and inject the expensive suppressant serum beforehand, weakening the outbreak considerably before she had to suffer through the worst of the pain.","But Dexter knew very well that this was not a permanent cure.","More importantly—","Their current supply of the suppressant serum was almost completely gone.","There was only enough serum left in the small medical box for tomorrow’s dose.","After that...","Nothing.","He needed to buy at least another week’s supply from the specialized pharmacies in the mid-districts. Preferably more, just in case of emergencies.","Then, there was the food.","Especially Lyra’s meals.","Dexter could not help but smile helplessly in the dark as he thought about her.","When she had first arrived at the bungalow, she ate enough food for three grown men, which had shocked him.","A few days later, her appetite grew, and she began eating enough for four.","Then five.","Now?","Lyra was regularly eating enough food for six normal adults every single day. Her appetite had become truly terrifying.","Strangely enough, as he observed her daily life, Dexter had started noticing a clear pattern.","The happier and more comfortable she became in the house...","The more she ate.","The safer she felt around him...","The larger her appetite grew.","Although she was still very quiet, withdrawn, and rarely made eye contact, the difference between the current Lyra and the terrifying silent girl who had first entered this house was already enormous.","Her gloomy, defensive expression had softened noticeably. Perhaps fifty percent compared to before. Maybe even more.","That progress alone made the extra food expenses completely worth it.","As for the Diamond Rice...","Dexter had already decided against using it by itself for their daily meals. It was simply too valuable and potent to use constantly.","Instead, he planned to mix it with ordinary, high-quality rice.","Perhaps seventy percent Diamond Rice and thirty percent regular rice."]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52 | Grade 4 Arcane Cuisine!","paragraphs":["The effects would remain excellent and easy to digest, while dramatically increasing the amount of time his limited supply would last.","Still, the more he calculated the upcoming expenses, the more painful the numbers became.","Furniture, medicine, food and high-grade ingredients.","By tomorrow night, the thirty thousand dollars would probably be gone. Completely gone.","Fortunately—","Dexter already knew the solution to his financial worries.","The Hero Association.","Tomorrow, he would officially register as a Hero, complete the testing, and obtain his physical Hero License.","Once that happened, he could finally enter the regulated dungeons around the city.","The thought alone caused a surge of quiet excitement to run through him.","Dungeons meant monsters.","Monsters meant valuable drops and materials he could sell.","Money meant more investments into his wives.","Investments meant powerful returns from the system.","Returns meant rapid increases in his personal strength.","Strength meant better protection for his home.","And protection meant a peaceful, stable future for the girls.","It was a perfect, self-sustaining cycle.","The stronger he became, the more he could invest in them. The more he invested in them, the stronger all of them would become together.","For the first time in his difficult life...","Dexter could actually see a clear, bright path forward. A real future.","After finalizing his plans for tomorrow, Dexter slowly closed his eyes.","His breathing became calm and steady.","The thick mana from the surrounding world immediately began flowing toward his body like rivers returning to the sea.","With his extraordinary SS-Rank Mana Affinity, cultivation no longer felt like a struggle to absorb scarce energy. Instead, it felt as though the physical world itself was willingly offering its power to him.","The Limitless Grand Cosmos Scripture began to circulate automatically through his pathways, guiding the mana smoothly.","Inside the endless darkness of his inner universe, the two brilliant Star Nodes continued to shine quietly like eternal stars.","Meanwhile, the partially awakened Cosmic DNA Helix rested silently between them.","The first segment glowed with brilliant, stable light.","The second shone with equal, warm radiance.","The third segment flickered softly in the dark, only partially illuminated, like a sleeping giant waiting for the right moment to awaken.","Dexter slowly sank deeper into his meditation, searching the vast inner universe of his mind for the location of the third star.","While quietly, in the background, the Buddha Endurance technique transformed the physical pain of the three girls and into raw strength, slowly raising his attributes.","•••","The next morning, Dexter woke up early, just as the first pale light of dawn began to touch the windows of the bungalow.","Today was a special day.","Not only was he planning to visit the Hunter Association later, but he also wanted to try an advanced cooking experiment he had been thinking about all night.","Cooking with actual Heavenly Treasures.","Standing inside the small, clean kitchen, Dexter opened the kitchen window first to let the cool morning air circulate.","He tied his simple fabric apron around his waist and began taking out his ingredients one by one, placing them carefully on the wooden counter.","The Diamond Rice.","The Origin Sun Fruit.","The Star Essence Serum.","The Heavenly Marrow Cleansing Capsule.","The Millennium Blood Ginseng.","The Void Spirit Lotus.","And finally...","The Restoration Pill.","Dexter looked at the small, glowing pill resting in his palm for a long, quiet moment.","Originally, when he first received it, he had intended to keep it safe in his storage. After all, he only possessed one.","If he gave it to only one of the girls, only one of them would have her severely damaged meridians healed, while the other two would remain crippled and in pain. That felt deeply unfair to him. He could not bring himself to choose one over the other.","But now...","A new, highly practical idea had appeared in his mind.","As a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, he possessed the advanced ability to dissolve the concentrated medicinal properties of high-grade treasures and pills directly into a Arcane meal.","By doing this, the healing effect would be slightly weaker than if one person consumed the pill directly, but all three girls would be able to share and benefit from its properties simultaneously.","A gentle smile appeared on his face.","\"Perfect,\" he whispered.","He took out his trusty Type-2 Cooking Pot and placed it on the stove before igniting his Alchemist Flame.","A warm, golden flame immediately rose beneath the dark pot, casting a bright light across the kitchen walls.","Unlike his previous, daily cooking plans, he did not mix any ordinary rice into the pot today. Today, he wanted absolute perfection. He wanted to create the most powerful medicinal dish he could possibly manage with his current skills.","One by one, the extremely rare ingredients entered the pot.","The small kitchen was soon filled with an astonishing, sweet fragrance that began to drift down the hallway.","Dexter controlled the temperature of the golden flames with extreme care, while simultaneously circulating his own mana through his hands and into the pot.","Every single bit of his concentration was focused entirely on the cooking process.","The Diamond Rice slowly began to soften, melting down into a pure, glowing spiritual essence.","The heavy medicinal ingredients dissolved, their distinct properties merging together under his careful guidance.","The fragrance in the kitchen grew richer, more intense, and incredibly heavenly.","Beads of sweat soon appeared on Dexter’s forehead, trickling down his face, but he did not dare to look away. Creating a dish of this caliber was far more difficult and mentally exhausting than anything he had ever cooked before.","He continuously infused his own dense, Superhuman-realm mana into the mixture, carefully balancing the volatile medicinal properties of the treasures to ensure they did not reject each other.","An hour of intense concentration later—","’Buzz!’","A powerful, distinct wave of pure spiritual energy erupted from the pot, rippling through the kitchen.","Dexter’s eyes widened as he looked at the glowing content.","He had actually succeeded.","[Ding! Congratulations, you have successfully created the Celestial Origin Star Rice (Grade 4)]","Originally, given his current level, the meal should have only reached the peak of Grade Three.","However, by using multiple genuine Heavenly Treasures and pouring nearly all of his refined Superhuman mana into the cooking process, he had forcefully elevated the final product to a genuine Grade Four Spiritual Meal.","It was a meal that was fully comparable to a Grade Four Heavenly Treasure!","Even Dexter, with his calm mind, could not help but inhale sharply at the realization.","A Grade Four Heavenly Treasure...","In the entire history of this city, such an item had only appeared a handful of times."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53 | Celestial Origin Star Rice!","paragraphs":["Years ago, when one had been discovered deep within a high-level dungeon, it had been brought to the central auction house. The most powerful and wealthy families in the province had fought desperately for it, driving the bidding to astronomical heights before it was finally sold.","That alone showed just how incredibly precious and rare Grade Four treasures truly were.","Even among professional Foodsmiths, only established Grandmasters could occasionally produce Grade Three meals after many failed attempts.","As for Grade Four...","There were only three Grandmaster Foodsmiths registered in the entire city, and none of them could guarantee a successful Grade Four creation.","Yet Dexter, utilizing his system-granted Great Grandmaster skills, had just successfully created one inside his modest kitchen on a simple stove.","Suddenly—","’Rumble!’","The clear morning sky outside the kitchen window began to darken rapidly.","Heavy, dark clouds gathered directly above their small bungalow, swirling in a tight circle. Faint flashes of silver lightning crackled within the dark depths of the clouds.","Dexter’s eyes widened as he looked out the window.","\"A mini heavenly tribulation?\" he muttered.","The creation of the Grade Four meal had actually attracted the passive attention of the natural laws of heaven.","Fortunately, because the meal’s energy was stable and condensed, the dark clouds only gathered briefly. After a few tense seconds, seeing that the energy was not escaping, they slowly dispersed, allowing the morning sunlight to break through once more.","The meal was not quite powerful enough to fully trigger a destructive heavenly lightning strike.","But Dexter knew very well that if this meal had reached Grade Five, a real tribulation lightning strike would have definitely descended upon their roof.","Fortunately, even if it had, he was not overly worried. The Type-5 House Protection Talisman hidden beneath the living room rug was more than strong enough to easily withstand a Grade Four or Five atmospheric disturbance.","After calming his racing heart, Dexter finally turned off the golden flames.","The legendary meal was complete.","A screen appeared in his mind, displaying the details of his creation:","•••","’[Celestial Origin Star Rice]’","’Grade:’ 4","’Creator:’ Rank 3 Great Grandmaster Foodsmith","’Appearance:’","The individual rice grains shine like tiny, polished diamonds beneath a smooth, golden sauce made from the Origin Sun Fruit. Thin, delicate threads of crimson Millennium Ginseng weave throughout the dish, while silver petals from the Void Spirit Lotus float elegantly above the surface. Tiny, sparkling specks of starlight drift upward from the meal like fireflies, and the rich aroma alone causes the nearby spiritual energy in the air to gather toward the plates.","’Effects:’","Unlike ordinary, violent Arcane meals that release their heavy medicinal effects immediately and strain the body, this dish is designed to release its power subtly and gently. It will not overwhelm the user’s damaged meridians, but its healing and strengthening effects will continue to increase drastically over time.","---","’[First Heavenly Resonance]’","’Effects:’","’ +300% cultivation speed","’ +250% mana absorption speed","’ +200% stamina recovery","’ +200% mana regeneration","’ +150% physical recovery speed","’ +100% increase in blood essence production","’ Removes 90% of accumulated bodily impurities","---","’[Second Heavenly Resonance]’","’Activation Time: 2 Hours After Consumption’","The true physical power of the meal awakens deep within the body. The Heavenly Marrow Cleansing Capsule and Millennium Blood Ginseng combine to forcefully elevate the consumer’s physical frame to an entirely new level of strength.","’Effects:’","’ +120% increase in physique","’ +100% increase in bone density","’ +100% increase in muscle strength","’ +80% increase in movement speed","’ +200% increase in vitality","’ Lifespan increased by 10%","’ Heals 95% of hidden physical injuries and internal damage","’ Removes all residual pill toxins and old cultivation impurities from the meridians.","---","’[Third Heavenly Resonance]’","’Activation Time: 3 Hours After Consumption’","The Origin Sun Fruit and Star Essence Serum fully merge within the dantian. The consumer’s body temporarily becomes a miniature sun of pure spiritual energy.","’Effects:’","’ +300% maximum mana capacity","’ +250% mana absorption speed","’ +250% mana recovery speed","’ +150% spell and technique power","’ +100% mana control precision","’ ’Note: Fire and Light affinity cultivators receive an additional +100% bonus to all mana-related effects.’","---","’[Fourth Heavenly Resonance]’","’Activation Time: 4 Hours After Consumption’","The Void Mana Lotus blooms within the deep recesses of the soul, providing profound mental clarity.","’Effects:’","’ +200% mental power","’ +150% soul defense","’ +120% comprehension speed","’ +100% resistance against mental illusions","’ +100% resistance against soul-based attacks","’ +80% increase in learning speed","’ Mental clarity improved by 300%","’ ’Many consumers enter a state of spontaneous enlightenment during this stage.’","---","The intoxicating, rich aroma of the food instantly filled the entire bungalow, drifting through the hallways and under the doors.","Before Dexter could even begin to dish the glowing rice out into bowls—","He suddenly felt a strong, intense gaze staring at his back.","Turning around slowly, he froze.","Lyra was already standing silently at the entrance of the kitchen.","A tiny, comical trail of drool hung from the corner of her lips. Her eyes, hidden behind her AI glasses, were locked onto the steaming pot with absolute, unwavering focus.","No. More accurately—","She was staring at the food as though she wanted to run forward and devour the entire metal pot in a single bite.","Dexter could not help but laugh softly at her expression.","\"Good morning, Lyra,\" he said gently.","Lyra did not react to his greeting nor did she move a muscle. She simply stood there, staring at the food with a burning desire that she made no effort to hide.","Dexter smiled, shook his head, and immediately began preparing their breakfast.","Knowing her truly terrifying appetite, he intentionally used an enormous, deep porcelain bowl for Lyra, filling it to the very brim with the glowing, star-flecked rice.","The moment he carried the heavy bowl to the dining table and placed it down—","’Whoosh!’","Lyra practically teleported across the room.","She sat down instantly, grabbed her spoon with a tight grip, and began eating.","The very first spoonful of the Celestial Origin Star Rice entered her mouth.","She froze.","Her entire body became completely still."]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54 | Open Your Mouth And Say ‘Ah’","paragraphs":["Her eyes widened behind her glasses. It was a look of pure, unadulterated shock.","She looked up at Dexter in complete disbelief.","Then, she looked back down at the food in her bowl.","Then, she looked back at Dexter again, her mouth slightly open.","She clearly wanted to ask him how a human being could possibly create something that tasted this incredible.","Unfortunately for her, she could not speak, and her vocal cords remained destroyed. Nor did she have the patience or the time right now to pull out her phone and type a message.","So, she simply abandoned all questions and continued eating.","A second spoon went in.","Then a third spoon.","Then a fourth spoon.","As she ate, a powerful, warm current of energy began to flow smoothly through her throat and down into her stomach. From there, it radiated outward like a gentle wave, reaching into every single corner of her body.","Her damaged, scarred meridians which had been cold and painful for years began to tremble slightly.","A feeling of intense warmth, comfort, and a pleasant tingling sensation spread rapidly throughout her limbs.","The tiny, jagged cracks within her mana pathways actually began to repair themselves, the energy of the rice acting like a warm, soothing salve that sealed the old wounds.","Lyra’s eyes widened even further at the sensation.","Without a single second of hesitation, she began eating even faster, her spoon practically becoming a blur as she scooped the glowing rice into her mouth.","At that moment, Dexter had already walked down the hallway to fetch the other two girls.","He gently pushed Mira’s wheelchair out of her room, guiding her toward the dining table, before walking back to help Selene to her seat.","Just as he was about to let go of Selene’s arm after guiding her safely onto her chair—","A small, cold hand suddenly reached out and grabbed his wrist.","Dexter froze in place.","Selene was holding his hand tightly.","Not only that, she was squeezing his wrist gently, her fingers wrapping completely around it.","A shocked, confused expression appeared on Dexter’s face.","Usually, due to her extreme sensitivity to temperature and her painful condition, Selene never allowed anyone to touch her if she could avoid it. Even he was rarely allowed to touch her, unless there was absolutely no one else available to help her move around the house.","He had always respected her boundaries, only guiding her occasionally when necessary.","But now...","She was the one who had actively reached out and grabbed him.","He waited for a moment, then carefully tried to remove his hand so he could sit down.","However, the moment he gently pulled back—","She tightened her grip, catching his hand again and refusing to let go.","Dexter blinked in surprise. His confusion only grew as he looked at her calm face.","\"Selene...?\" he asked softly.","She remained completely silent for a few seconds, her head tilted slightly downward, before she spoke in a soft, quiet whisper.","\"...Warm.\"","Dexter blinked again.","\"Warm?\"","She nodded her head slightly, her silver hair shifting over her shoulders.","\"You’re very warm... and comfortable today.\"","His eyes widened in sudden realization.","Then, he immediately thought about his newly evolved Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline.","Selene’s body, due to her mysterious, chronic illness, constantly emitted a freezing, painful energy that made her feel cold to the bone.","Perhaps... the natural, warm energy constantly radiating from his evolved fire bloodline was acting as a natural counter, soothing her condition and making her feel comfortable for the first time.","It was the only logical explanation he could think of.","Eventually, after a long moment, Selene slowly loosened her grip, letting his hand go.","Dexter gently guided her hand toward the handle of her spoon.","Although she was completely blind, once her fingers touched the edge of the wooden table and the spoon, she was highly independent and could feed herself without any issues.","He then sat down on the chair beside Mira.","At that exact moment—","Selene took her very first bite of the glowing rice.","She froze instantly.","Her blind, pale eyes widened slightly.","The incredible, rich flavor of the Origin Sun Fruit and the Diamond Rice exploded inside her mouth, a perfect balance of sweetness and warmth.","A deep, soothing warmth spread rapidly through her physical body. The cold, frozen meridians inside her chest began to thaw, the old, damaged pathways healing slowly under the gentle influence of the Millennium Blood Ginseng.","Without saying a single word, she immediately took another spoonful.","Then another.","Then another.","Dexter smiled warmly as he watched her. The healing effects of the Grade Four meal seemed to be even better and more immediate than he had originally expected.","Meanwhile, Mira was sitting in her wheelchair, her brows furrowed in a deep frown.","She looked at Lyra, who was practically inhaling her food.","Then, she looked at Selene, who was eating with an unusual, quiet intensity.","Both girls were behaving as though they had completely lost their minds.","\"Why are you two behaving like uncultured monkeys?\" Mira asked sharply.","Neither of them replied to her. They did not even look up as they ignored her. They simply continued eating their food.","Dexter almost burst into loud laughter at the scene.","\"Uncultured monkeys? Where did you even learn such an insult, Mira?\" he asked, amused.","Mira turned her head and glared at him immediately.","\"You should have seen me in my prime,\" she said proudly, raising her chin. \"My vocabulary was far more refined than yours.\"","Dexter chuckled softly.","\"I’m sure your insults in your prime could make grown men sit down and cry.\"","Mira snorted softly, turning her head away.","Then, she looked down at the steaming bowl of rice sitting in front of her. She looked at it suspiciously, her eyes narrowing at the glowing silver petals and the starlight drifting from the plate.","Dexter scooped up a small spoonful of the warm rice.","\"Open up. Say Ah.\"","Mira’s face flushed slightly, and she glared at him with intense annoyance.","She absolutely hated it when he treated her like a helpless child. Especially when he used that patronizing tone and said, \"Ah.\""]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55 | Strange Behaviors","paragraphs":["\"Open up. Say Ah.\"","Mira’s face flushed slightly, and she glared at him with intense annoyance.","She absolutely hated it when he treated her like a helpless child. Especially when he used that patronizing tone and said, \"Ah.\"","She was about to open her mouth to deliver a sharp, angry retort, but then, the incredible, sweet aroma of the rice entered her nose.","Her eyes widened and her anger vanished in an instant, replaced by a sudden, intense hunger.","She looked at the spoonful of food, then she looked at Dexter’s calm face.","Then, she looked back at the food.","\"Where did you actually get the ingredients for this?\" she demanded, trying to remain suspicious.","Dexter rolled his eyes playfully.","\"Must you question every single thing I do? Just eat, Mira. I promise you I didn’t poison the food.\"","Mira wanted to ask another question, to demand to know how he could afford such luxury.","Unfortunately... the smell was simply too tempting to resist.","Without even realizing what she was doing, she slowly, reluctantly opened her small mouth.","Dexter gently guided the spoon inside.","The very next second, Mira’s pupils constricted.","The flavor was completely indescribable. It did not feel like she was eating a simple bowl of rice at all.","It felt as though she was eating soft, warm, heavenly clouds that melted instantly on her tongue.","The rich, sweet flavors of the fruit and the savory, earthy tones of the ginseng blended together perfectly. A deep, comfortable warmth spread rapidly through her entire body.","Her damaged meridians, which had felt like dry, cracked twigs for years, trembled.","Then... they began to heal.","Her eyes slowly closed on their own. A soft, blissful, and completely relaxed expression appeared on her face, replacing her usual defensive frown.","A few seconds later—","She opened her eyes, and then, without realizing it, she opened her mouth again.","This time, she did it entirely on her own.","She looked at the spoon in Dexter’s hand expectantly, her eyes wide.","Dexter nearly laughed out loud.","At this moment, she looked incredibly cute. She looked like an obedient, hungry puppy waiting patiently for her master to feed her.","Of course, he wisely kept that specific thought entirely to himself. If he said it out loud, she would definitely become angry and refuse to eat another bite.","So, he simply continued to feed her.","One spoon after another.","Three spoons.","Four spoons.","Five spoons.","By the time Dexter finally managed to pick up his own spoon to eat a single bite of his own portion—","Lyra had already completely emptied her enormous bowl.","She sat quietly, holding her empty wooden spoon, looking at him with an intense, expectant, and slightly pleading gaze.","Dexter looked at her empty bowl, then at his own plate, and shook his head helplessly.","\"That’s all for today, Lyra,\" Dexter said, his voice soft as he looked at her empty bowl. \"This meal is highly complex. The ingredients are extremely rare and difficult to balance, so it isn’t something I can prepare in large quantities or multiple times a day. If you are still feeling hungry, I cooked a fresh pot of ordinary rice on the side.\"","Lyra’s shoulders slumped slightly as she pouted sadly. The sheer disappointment on her face was so vivid that Dexter felt a brief pang of guilt. But a moment later, she seemed to realize how much she had already eaten. She looked down at her hands, then pressed both palms against her flat stomach.","A quiet, satisfied expression returned to her face. She closed her eyes for a moment, letting her head lean back.","\"Burp.\"","A small belch escaped her lips.","The entire dining room went completely silent. The quiet hum of the refrigerator seemed to grow louder in the sudden stillness.","Dexter blinked.","Mira, who had been about to swallow another spoonful of rice, stopped mid-movement, her eyes wide with surprise.","Even Selene, who usually remained completely detached from her surroundings, paused her spoon halfway to her mouth, her head tilting slightly toward Lyra.","A second later, Dexter could not hold it in any longer. He burst into an amused laughter.","\"Hahaha.\"","Lyra’s face turned bright red. The blush started at the base of her neck and rushed upward, coloring her cheeks and the tips of her ears a deep crimson.","She quickly pulled her hands away from her stomach, picked up her empty bowl, and stood up so fast her chair screeched against the floor. Keeping her head bowed and her eyes fixed firmly on the ground, she hurried toward the sink, placing the bowl down with a loud clatter before retreating down the hallway toward the bedrooms.","\"Well,\" Mira remarked, her voice dry as she watched Lyra disappear around the corner. \"It seems someone has completely forgotten her manners. Her family tutors would have had a stroke if they witnessed that.\"","\"She enjoyed the food. As a cook, there is no greater compliment than seeing someone finish their plate and feel satisfied.\"","\"Hmph,\" Mira muttered, though the small, content smile on her own face contradicted her sharp words. She took another bite of her rice, closed her eyes, and chewed quietly.","Meanwhile, Selene was still only halfway through her meal. Normally, Selene ate very, very little food. She was always the very first person to quietly say she was full.","Most days, ten small spoonfuls were more than enough to make her stop eating entirely.","But today... she showed absolutely no signs of stopping. One warm spoonful after another disappeared quickly into her mouth.","Even Mira, who normally stopped eating out of pride after a few bites, had eaten absolutely everything on her plate. Everything. There were only two or three single grains of rice left sticking stubbornly to the edge of the bowl.","Before she asked to be pushed off, she had immediately hestured with her chin at those grains. \"There are still three left.\"","Dexter had stared at her for a moment before bursting into laughter. \"You’re actually counting individual grains of rice now?\"","Mira had glared at him fiercely. \"Food is food. Don’t waste it.\"","Chuckling, Dexter had scraped the remaining grains into the spoon and fed them to her. Only then did she look completely satisfied. For a brief, funny moment, Dexter even felt that she wanted to pick up the bowl and lick it clean.","Then he suddenly remembered—Lyra had actually done exactly that.","Dexter almost laughed again remembering it.","Back at the table, Selene finally let out a small, quiet hum of deep satisfaction as she finished her bowl.","Her blind, white eyes remained closed as she sat quietly, deeply enjoying the lingering warmth spreading through her cold body.","The strong medicinal energy from the Heavenly Treasures flowed rapidly through her damaged meridians, nourishing and repairing them little by little.","Since Mira was already gone, Dexter stood up and began clearing the table. Selene didn’t move. She remained sitting exactly where she was at the dining table.","Even after Dexter began noisily washing the dirty dishes in the sink. Even after he thoroughly cleaned the kitchen counters. She simply sat there in perfect silence, Cultivating.","Dexter glanced over his shoulder at her strangely. Lately, she had been acting even stranger than usual.","Then again... all three girls occasionally behaved in ways that could only be described as highly unusual due to their trauma.","Sometimes, Lyra would stand completely still by the living room window for an entire hour without moving a muscle. Sometimes, Mira would sit in her chair and stare silently at the blank television screen despite not even watching a show.","As for Selene... he had once walked into the backyard and found her standing still, facing a brick wall, her empty eyes staring forward silently for almost twenty minutes.","So compared to that... remaining seated quietly at the dining table wasn’t particularly strange. Dexter simply shrugged his shoulders and continued scrubbing the pots.","Suddenly—"]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56 | 9th Heavenly Flames","paragraphs":["Suddenly—","’BOOM!’","A violent surge of mana erupted from the far end of the hallway, specifically from the bedroom.","The air in the corridor rippled visibly, carrying a warm, dry draft that rustled the small calendar hanging on the kitchen wall.","Before Dexter could even turn his head—","’BOOM!’","Another distinct explosion of energy rattled the living room windows. The faint layer of dust on the ceiling fan drifted down as a cool, dense wave of shadow-like energy swept across the floor, making the shadows under the furniture lengthen and twist for a brief second.","And then, right in front of him—","’BOOM!’","The air directly around the dining table trembled.","Dexter slowly turned his gaze toward Selene.","A pale, beautiful blue light was radiating from beneath her skin. The wood of the dining table beneath her fingers began to frost over, thin patterns of white ice spreading out like delicate spiderwebs from her hands.","All three of them had broken through.","The Superhuman Realm. First Stage.","Dexter stood there in the middle of the kitchen, a clean dish towel in his hand, completely stunned.","When he had consumed his own portion of the Grade Four meal, the effect wasn’t as immediate and even now he still hadn’t felt it.","But for the girls, whose cultivation bases had been severely damaged and suppressed, the concentrated, gentle energy of the ’Celestial Origin Star Rice’ had acted like a spark in a dry forest.","It had cleared the blockages in their primary pathways, repaired the initial structural damage, and allowed them to easily step over the massive barrier dividing the Awakened Realm from the Superhuman Realm.","[Ding!]","The clear, ringing sound echoed in his mind, followed by a detailed display of text.","[You invested: Grade 4 Celestial Origin Star Rice into your wives.]","[Investment Multiplier Triggered: 100x!]","[Calculating rewards...]","[Ding! Congratulations, Host. You have obtained the following rewards:]","[1. Professional Rank Promotion: Great Grandmaster Foodsmith (Early Stage) ➔ Great Grandmaster Foodsmith (Middle Stage)]","[2. Special Physical Constitution: Heavenly Gastronomy Body]","[3. Elemental Evolution: Alchemist Flame ➔ 9th Heavenly Flame: Emperor Void Flame]","[4. Raw Materials: 1,000kg of Premium Diamond Rice]","[5. Rare Liquids: 100kg of Cosmic Star Origin Nectar]","[6. Premium Alcohol: 100kg of Burning Sun Lava Wine]","[7. Talent Evolution: Mana Affinity (SS-Rank) ➔ Mana Affinity (SSS-Rank)]","...","Dexter immediately focused his mind.","He wanted to check their current conditions.","Three names and status panels materialized in his field of vision. He focused on Selene first.","[Name: Selene Frostborn]","[Age: 20]","[Relationship: Wife]","[Affection: 41%]","[Talent: Eternal Winter Frost (S-Rank)]","[Cultivation Status]","- Previous Realm: Ultra Realm (Peak)","- Current Realm: Superhuman Realm (First Stage)","- Current Mana Level: 12% (Sealed / Restricted by physical condition)","- Activated Star Nodes: 4 / 12","[Body Condition]","- Meridian Damage: 77% (Improved: 12% healed and actively stabilizing)","- Vision: Complete Blindness (Optic nerves damaged)","- Chronic Illness: Severe elemental imbalance. Infected by an unknown object Sit constantly generates high-density cold energy that her damaged meridians cannot safely export. This results in regular, painful frost seizures and gradual internal freezing.","[Mental State]","- Quietly relieved","- Highly focused","- Comfortable (soothed by the warmth radiating from the Host)","- Slightly Aroused","[Warning: Danger Level: High]","The built-up frost energy inside her lower meridians has reached a critical density. The temporary suppressant serums are no longer capable of neutralizing the cold source. If this imbalance is not resolved, her body will slowly begin to crystallize from the inside out, starting with her extremities and eventually leading to complete physical stasis and death.","[Estimated Time Before Next Major Crisis: 14 Days]","[Possible Solutions]","1. Locate and refine a Grade 7 Heavenly Treasure: [Ice Warm Cocoon]. This rare artifact can absorb and balance the extreme frost constitution, permanently stabilizing her meridians.","2. Acquire and integrate a high-grade Heavenly Flame: [Abyssal Demon Heart Flame]. This legendary flame, born in the deepest trenches of the Demon Abyss, possesses the unique thermal properties required to melt her internal ice without harming her physical organs.","’’’","Dexter’s chest tightened as he read the detailed warnings. His heart felt heavy.","A Grade 7 Heavenly Treasure?","Grade 1 and 2 items were common, sold if you used your hero license to purchase it in various high end shops.","Grade 3 items were considered luxury goods, reserved for wealthy families and mid-level guild leaders.","Grade 4 items, like the meal he had just cooked, were rare enough to cause a massive sensation in the entire city and even auctions.","Grade 7 was a mythical tier and it had never even been heard of in the city.","As for the ’Abyssal Demon Heart Flame’...","He had no idea either but he could stretch the internet on how to get it.","The task ahead of him was incredibly difficult. It felt like trying to climb a mountain made of smooth glass.","But as he looked at Selene’s calm, pale face—her blind eyes closed as she sat quietly at the table, enjoying the simple warmth of the kitchen, Dexter’s determination hardened. He would not let her freeze. He would find a way, step by step, using the system’s investments to bridge the gap.","He shifted his gaze to the second panel.","[Name: Lyra ]","[Age: 18]","[Relationship: Wife]","[Affection: 42%]","[Talent: Shadow Manipulation (A-Rank)]","[Cultivation Status]","- Previous Realm: Ultra Realm (5th)","- Current Realm: Superhuman Realm (First Stage)","- Current Mana Level: 9% (Sealed)","- Activated Star Nodes: 2 / 12","[Body Condition]","- Meridian Damage: 62% (Improved: 12% healed and stabilizing)","- Hearing: Completely destroyed eardrums","- Speech: Destroyed vocal cords","[Mental State]","- Deeply satisfied (feeling physically full for the first time in days)","- Shaken by the rapid breakthrough","- Highly protective of her immediate surroundings","- Faintly embarrassed about her table manners","[Warning: Shadow Corruption Level: 5%]","Because she has spent years in dark, damp environments without proper medical care or cultivation guidance, her rare Shadow Manipulation talent has begun to turn inward.","The dark mana has started to corrupt her physical cells.","If this corruption level reaches 100%, her physical body will collapse and transform into a permanent, open portal to the Shadow Realm.","This will allow high-level shadow entities to pour directly into the physical world, resulting in her immediate death.","[Recent Changes]","- The Grade 4 Celestial Origin Star Rice has successfully reduced her shadow corruption level by 3% (down from 8%).","- Consistent consumption of highly pure, light-aligned or neutral spiritual food can continue to suppress and eventually cleanse the corruption entirely."]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57 | S-so Warm!","paragraphs":["Dexter let out a quiet breath of relief.","Although the shadow corruption warning was terrifying, the solution was much more manageable than Selene’s crisis. It simply required him to keep doing what he was already doing: cooking highly refined, pure arcane food for her every single day.","With his new ’Great Grandmaster (Middle Stage)’ cooking skills and the 1,000 kilograms of premium ’Diamond Rice’ he had just received as a reward, he could easily keep her corruption level under tight control while slowly working to eliminate it completely.","He turned his focus to the final panel.","[Name: Mira Vane]","[Age: 21]","[Relationship: Wife]","[Affection: 39%]","[Talent: Spectral Arm (Amber Flames, D-Rank / Spectral Arms D, Rank)]","[Cultivation Status]","- Previous Realm: Ultra Realm (Peak)","- Current Realm: Superhuman Realm (First Stage)","- Current Mana Level: 15% (Sealed)","- Activated Star Nodes: 5 [500% mana]","[Body Condition]","- Meridian Damage: 80% (Improved: 15% healed and stabilizing)","- Physical State: Full paralysis, severe nerve damage and spinal trauma.","[Mental State]","- Deeply frustrated by her physical limitations","- Highly competitive","- Suspicious of outsiders","- Faintly pleased by the warm feeling in her spine (the nerve damage is beginning to show early signs of minor recovery)","’’’","Dexter closed the status screens and rubbed the bridge of his nose.","All three of them were carrying incredibly heavy, painful burdens. It was a miracle they had managed to survive this long.","He looked at the clock hanging on the kitchen wall. It was already past eight in the morning.","\"Dexter,\" Mira’s voice was unusually soft.","Whjch meant she needed him to do something embarrassing to her.","Dexter shook off his serious thoughts and smile. \"I’m coming, Mira. Give me a second.\"","He walked into the living room. Mira was sitting in her wheelchair, glaring at the blank plastic frame of the television set.","Even though her entire body was paralyzed, her posture was still remarkably straight, a habit drilled into her from her days as a wealthy, proud young lady.","\"You know,\" Dexter said as he walked over and unlocked the wheels of her chair, \"you should learn how to say please wine of these days.\"","\"If pleas truly works, wouldn’t this world be a better place?\" She sneered in response.","\"Hm... you are right but you’re also wrong.\" Dexter replied easily.","He pushed her wheelchair toward the bathroom at the end of the hallway.","The daily routine of helping Mira wash up was always a slow, careful process. Because of her pride, she hated every single second of her dependency. She would glare at him through the mirror, her eyes sharp and dark, as he carefully held her up to the sink, wetted a soft towel, and gently wiped her face.","\"Your hands are too warm today,\" she muttered, her eyes narrowing as he wiped her forehead. \"It feels like you’ve been standing too close to a furnace.\"","\"It’s just my circulation,\" Dexter lied smoothly, carefully adjusting the warmth of his ’Emperor Void Flame’ so it would not accidentally scorch her skin. \"A good night’s sleep does wonders for your health.\"","\"Hmph. Lies,\" she whispered, but she did not pull away.","Next came the most difficult part of the morning: brushing her teeth.","For some reason, this specific task always seemed to offend her pride the most.","Dexter prepared her pink toothbrush with a small dab of mint toothpaste. He held it up in front of her.","\"Alright, Mira. Say Ah.\"","Mira’s jaw tightened, and she glared at him with intense, silent fury through the bathroom mirror. Her pale cheeks flushed a faint, embarrassed pink.","\"I am twenty-one years old, Dexter,\" she hissed, her voice low. \"I am not a toddler. Stop saying ’Ah’ to me.\"","\"And I am your husband, which means I have to make sure you don’t get cavities,\" Dexter replied, his voice completely calm and even. \"Now, open up.\"","Mira glared at him for another ten seconds, trying to see if he would back down. But Dexter simply stood there, holding the toothbrush with a patient, steady hand. He had learned early on that the only way to handle Mira’s sharp tongue was to remain completely unaffected by it.","Eventually, seeing that her death glare had no effect, she let out a sharp, annoyed huff and reluctantly opened her mouth.","’\"Ah.\"’","Dexter smiled victoriously and began to brush her teeth with gently. He was incredibly careful not to hurt her sensitive gums, moving the brush in slow, steady circles.","If looks could kill, Dexter would have been turned into ash a hundred times over by now. But he simply kept brushing, ignoring the intense, fiery gaze she directed at him through the glass.","Once she was clean, rinsed, and dry, Dexter carefully lifted her in his arms to transfer her back to the wheelchair.","Despite her paralysis, she felt remarkably light. He made sure her feet were positioned comfortably on the footrests before pushing her back into the living room, setting her wheelchair near her favorite spot by the window where the morning sun was starting to stream in.","He then walked back to the dining room. Selene was sitting perfectly still, her hands resting flat on the cold wooden table, her head tilted toward the kitchen sink.","\"I will help you wash your hands, Selene,\" Dexter said softly as he walked over.","She did not move, but her head turned slightly toward the sound of his voice. \"No.\"","\"I know,\" Dexter said, his voice gentle. \"But the floor is a bit wet near the sink, and I don’t want you to slip.\"","Selene remained silent for a moment. Then, she slowly stood up, using the edge of the table to balance herself.","Dexter did not try to hold her arm. Instead, he simply walked half a step ahead of her, letting the warm, comfortable air of his evolved bloodline guide her like a silent heat beacon.","She didn’t do as he expected but grabbed his arm instead and then squeezed it against her chest and unconsciously muttered.","\"S-so warm!\"","Dexter was stunned by the sudden half hug. She was practically hogging his arm fiercely.","Her teo beautiful breasts pressed tightly against his arm and he felt the softness of them like heavenly cloud right bound against his flesh.","His face flushed red as blood rushed to his brain and lower body.","He quickly cleared his throat and guided her till she reached the sink, Dexter turned on the tap, adjusting the water until it was lukewarm, and placed a clean bar of soap in her palm.","\"You can let go now, you’re already before the sink.\"","Deeply reluctantly she eventually released his arm from her embrace and she washed her hand.","While she washed her hands, Dexter managed to calm his boiling blood and then leaned against the counter and looked at her.","\"Do you think we should hire a professional nanny or a medical caretaker to help around the house?\" he asked with the most casual tone he could offer. \"With the money I received from the association, we can easily afford to hire someone reliable from the hero association. It would make things much easier for you girls when I am out running errands or visiting the dungeons.\""]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58 | Meeting Rachael Again","paragraphs":["\"No.\"","The sharp response came from the living room.","Mira did not even hesitate. She turned her head toward the kitchen, her eyes narrowing. \"I don’t want some stranger in our house, touching my wheelchair, looking at my legs, and whispering about our families behind our backs. We are not charity cases for the public to gawk at.\"","Selene, who was carefully rinsing the soap from her fingers, also shook her head and spoke with a quiet voice. \"Same.\"","Dexter chuckled softly, shaking his head. He knew their pride was still a tad sensitive. They had gone from being highly respected young ladies of prominent families to being hunted, crippled outcasts living in a cheap bungalow.","The last thing they wanted was some stranger witnessing their daily struggles and looking down on them with pity.","\"Alright, alright,\" Dexter said, raising his hands in a placating gesture. \"No caretakers. It was just a thought. We will keep things exactly as they are.\"","Besides, with the ’Type-5 House Protection Talisman’ fully active and his own strength rising, he felt much more comfortable leaving them alone now. The bungalow was practically a fortress.","Just as Dexter was about to reach for the kitchen towel to dry Selene’s hands—","’Knock. Knock. Knock.’","A series of sharp knocks echoed from the heavy wooden front door.","Instantly, Dexter’s body went on high alert.","His ears twitched as his ’Enhanced Hearing’ talent activated. Through his mental connection with the ’Type-5 House Protection Talisman’, he felt a sudden, distinct ripple in the invisible dome surrounding the property.","Someone had entered the front yard. They had walked straight up the cracked concrete path and were now standing on the porch.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed, a cold, dangerous light flashing through his pupils. His mind immediately went to Kreg and then the assassins on the bridge.","His face turned cold as killing intent radiated off him like a beast.","With heavy footsteps, he walked toward the front door.","He looked through the small, dusty peephole.","The tension in his shoulders vanished instantly, replaced by pure awkwardness.","Standing on the front porch, dressed in a sleek, tight-fitting white suit that accentuated her stunning curves, was Rachel.","Her long, dark red hair was tied back in a neat ponytail, and she was holding a leather folder against her chest. She looked perfectly professional, yet highly fashionable.","Dexter let out a slow, quiet sigh, let go of the kitchen knife, and unlocked the deadbolt.","He opened the door.","\"Rachel?\" he blinked, sounding genuinely surprised. \"What are you doing here so early?\"","The beautiful woman smiled brightly, her green eyes sparkling with warmth as she looked at him.","\"Good morning, Dexter,\" she said, her voice carrying a cheerful, melodic tone.","Before he could even take a step back or say another word, she stepped forward into the doorway, wrapped her arms around his neck, and gave him a warm, enthusiastic hug.","Dexter’s entire body went completely stiff.","He stood there like a stone statue, his hands hovering awkwardly in the air, not knowing where to put them.","He could smell her perfume, a subtle, expensive scent of fresh lilies and mint, and feel the soft, warm curve of her body pressed against his chest.","A second later, Rachel stepped back with a playful, teasing smile, her eyes scanning his face.","Meanwhile, somewhere directly behind him—","The temperature in the living room dropped by at least two degrees in a fraction of a second.","Dexter did not need to turn around to know that three pairs of cold eyes were currently drilling holes into his back. He pretended not to notice, keeping his focus firmly on the woman in front of him.","Rachel looked past him, her eyes wandering into the living room. \"Aren’t you going to invite me inside, Dexter? It’s a bit chilly out here on the porch.\"","Dexter wanted to face palm. ’ Are you trying to get yourself killed?’","He cleared his throat awkwardly, stepping aside to make room. \"Right. Of course. Please, come in.\"","Rachel entered the bungalow, her high heels clicking sharply against the wooden floorboards.","She looked around the small, modest room with genuine curiosity.","She did not show any signs of disgust or pity at the simple, cheap furniture or the worn-out rugs. Instead, she nodded with quiet appreciation.","\"It’s a nice place, Dexter. Simple, cozy, and very clean. You’ve taken good care of it.\"","\"It’s enough for us,\" Dexter shrugged, closing the heavy wooden door behind her and locking it. He looked toward her. \"Would you like something to drink? I have some tea, juice, or water.\"","Rachel turned to him, her smile widening. \"Tea would be wonderful, thank you.\"","Dexter blinked. Usually, when visitors came to a modest home, they would politely refuse to avoid causing trouble for the host. He had only asked out of basic politeness, expecting her to decline so they could get straight to business.","But Rachel seemed completely at ease, as if she was visiting an old friend rather than a client.","\"Alright,\" Dexter nodded. \"Give me a couple of minutes.\"","He walked back into the kitchen, leaving Rachel standing in the center of the living room.","Left alone, Rachel’s gaze wandered around the space once more before finally landing on the sofa, and then on the wheelchair.","Mira was sitting perfectly still, her hands resting on her lap. She slowly turned her head toward Rachel.","Their eyes met.","Rachel smiled politely, giving a small, professional nod. \"Hello there.\"","Mira did not smile. She did not nod. She simply stared at Rachel with an expressionless, cold, and incredibly heavy gaze that seemed to freeze the very air between them.","The temperature in the corner of the room rose by another degree, a faint trace of flame seem to lit up in Mira’s eyes.","A second later, Mira slowly turned her head away, ignoring Rachel completely as if she was nothing more than a piece of cheap, uninteresting furniture.","Rachel coughed awkwardly, her smile faltering for a brief moment. She had met many powerful, arrogant heroes in her line of work, but the sheer, fiery pride radiating from this paralyzed girl was genuinely intimidating."]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59 | Pure Jealousy","paragraphs":["Fortunately, Dexter returned at that moment, carrying a simple ceramic cup filled with hot, steaming tea.","The tea leaves he had used were from the system’s rewards, highly refined spiritual tea leaves that carried a faint, natural sweet aroma. The steam rising from the cup carried a quiet, soothing energy that immediately filled the room.","Rachel took the cup, her fingers brushing against his hand for a brief intentional second. She took a slow, delicate sip.","Her green eyes widened in instant surprise.","\"This is... incredible,\" she murmured, looking down at the pale amber liquid. \"The mana density in these leaves is remarkably high. Even the specialized tea served at the high-level guild meetings cannot compare to this. What kind of tea is this, Dexter?\"","Dexter rubbed the back of his neck, offering a helpless, casual shrug. \"I honestly don’t know. I bought a small bag of it randomly from an old merchant in the lower market a while ago. He said it was just a local wild blend.\"","Rachel looked highly unconvinced, her eyes narrowing slightly as she studied his face. She knew very well that such highly refined, pure spiritual tea could not possibly be bought randomly in a cheap lower market. But seeing that he had no intention of sharing his source, she chose not to push the matter.","She took another sip, then carefully placed the cup down on the small wooden side table.","\"I’ve been expecting you at the Hero Association branch for a while now, you know,\" she said, her tone shifting to a gentle, playful scolding. \"You kept me waiting for hours, Dexter. I had to push back several important meetings because I thought you would show up.\"","Dexter offered an apologetic, awkward smile. \"Sorry about that, Rachel. We had some things to sort out here around the house first. I was actually planning to head over there today.\"","Rachel’s green eyes brightened instantly. \"Perfect! I have my car parked outside. We can complete the paperwork here, and then we can drive over to the Association together. It will save you a lot of time, and I can guide you through the registration process personally.\"","At that exact moment—","\"Hmph.\"","A loud, cold, and highly irritated snort echoed from the wheelchair by the window.","Dexter turned his head. Mira was glaring at him, her dark eyes flashing with a dangerous, sharp light.","He blinked, feeling a sudden cold sweat forming on his back. He walked to her and in front of her as he asked. \"Do you need something, Mira?\"","Mira glanced at him indifferently, her voice extremely cold.","\"You men really aren’t satisfied with what you have, are you? Flirt.\"","\"What—\" Dexter shook his head rapidly.","But Mira let out cold snort as she closed her eyes.","Dexter opened his mouth and closed it. Trying to explain. But he knew it would come out wrong so he calmed down and replied.","\"Rachel is here for official business,\" he said slowly, keeping his voice calm and steady.","The small living room became incredibly, suffocatingly quiet.","Dexter stood there, feeling like a criminal standing before a highly unsympathetic judge. He rubbed his forehead, trying to find his words.","\"And for the record, I have not flirted with anyone.\"","He paused, looking at Mira’s smooth hair and milky neck, and then at Selene, who was sitting silently at the dining table.","\"I haven’t even flirted with the three of you yet,\" he added with a whisper only she could hear.","\"So why on earth would I suddenly start flirting with someone else?\"","Mira opened her eyes and glanced at him for a brief, fleeting second, her sharp expression faltered.","A beautiful, deep redness climbed up her neck and quickly spread toward her cheeks, coloring her pale skin.","\"Hmph. Glib tongue,\" she muttered, turning her head even further away so he could not see her face.","Dexter let out a quiet sigh of relief, then went back to Rachel, offering an apologetic smile. \"I’m really sorry about that. She’s been through a lot of stress lately, and their nerves are a bit frayed.\"","Rachel, however, looked thoroughly entertained. She was leaning back against the sofa, her chin resting on her hand, a wide, amused smile on her face.","\"I can see that, Dexter,\" she laughed softly. \"You certainly have a very lively household.\"","Dexter coughed awkwardly, desperately trying to steer the conversation back to a safe, professional topic. \"So... what exactly did you need to clarify regarding the bridge incident?\"","Rachel quickly opened her leather folder, pulling out several official documents covered in neat, typed text.","She began to ask him basic, standard questions about the assassination attempt.","She asked if any suspicious individuals had been seen loitering around the neighborhood since then. She inquired if he had thought of any specific enemies—either from his past or from his family’s connections—who would want him dead.","Dexter shook his head firmly. \"I don’t have any personal enemies, Rachel. Our families cut ties with us. We aren’t a threat to anyone anymore. We are just trying to live a quiet life here. So honestly... I have no idea why anyone would target us.\"","Rachel nodded thoughtfully, her pen scratching against the paper as she took notes. Once she finished, she closed the folder with a sharp snap and slid it back into her bag.","She stood up from the sofa, smoothing her white suit jacket. She walked toward Dexter, stopping just a foot away from him.","Her green eyes locked onto his, a sudden, soft light appearing within them.","\"You know, Dexter,\" she whispered, her voice low and intimate. \"I really enjoyed the time we spent together at the hotel bar. It was... refreshing.\"","Dexter’s heart skipped a beat, and he immediately coughed, his survival instincts screaming at him.","Unfortunately—","Mira heard every single word.","’Crack.’","The small ceramic teacup sitting on the side table beside her wheelchair suddenly shattered into several pieces, the hot water spilling across the wood.","A heavy, suffocating silence filled the room."]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60 | Selene And Mira","paragraphs":["\"So honestly... I have no idea why anyone would target us.\"","Rachel nodded thoughtfully, her pen scratching against the paper as she took notes. Once she finished, she closed the folder with a sharp snap and slid it back into her bag.","She stood up from the sofa, smoothing her white suit jacket. She walked toward Dexter, stopping just a foot away from him.","Her green eyes locked onto his, a sudden, soft light appearing within them.","\"You know, Dexter,\" she whispered, her voice low and intimate. \"I really enjoyed the time we spent together at the hotel bar. It was... refreshing.\"","Dexter’s heart skipped a beat, and he immediately coughed, his survival instincts screaming at him.","Unfortunately—","Mira heard every single word.","’Crack.’","The small ceramic teacup sitting on the side table beside her wheelchair suddenly shattered into several pieces, the hot water spilling across the wood.","A heavy, suffocating silence filled the room.","Dexter slowly, reluctantly turned his head.","Mira was smiling.","It was a small, polite, and extremely sweet smile.","But her eyes were completely dark, devoid of any warmth. For some reason, that sweet smile felt ten times more terrifying than when she was openly glaring at him.","Rachel, completely oblivious to the sheer elemental danger surrounding her, or perhaps simply choosing to ignore it continued to look at Dexter with a playful smile.","\"And that goodbye kiss wasn’t bad either,\" she added, her voice carrying a light, teasing tone.","Dexter almost stopped breathing. He felt as if his soul was about to leave his body.","Across the room—","The temperature suddenly plummeted.","At the dining table, a thick layer of blue frost quietly spread across the wooden surface, freezing the spilled water in an instant. At the same time, an oppressive, suffocating heat began to radiate from Mira’s direction, the air around her wheelchair distorting slightly like a desert highway in mid-July.","One extreme cold.","One extreme heat.","The two powerful, clashing elemental pressures collided directly in the middle of the small living room, making the light bulb hanging from the ceiling flicker weakly.","Rachel raised a dark eyebrow, her green eyes scanning the room with quiet interest.","Only then did Dexter realize something. Rachel was strong. Very strong.","At the very least, she was a high-tier hero in the Superhuman Realm. Possibly even at its peak, or perhaps even higher. Her body remained completely relaxed and unaffected by the intense, conflicting elemental pressures radiating from the two girls.","Rachel smiled, stepping back toward the front door. \"So, Dexter. Shall we go to the Hero Association branch together? My car is ready.\"","Dexter shook his head so quickly and violently that his hair almost became a blur.","\"No!\" he squeaked, his voice slightly higher than usual.","Rachel blinked, surprised by his rapid refusal. \"No?\"","\"I... I suddenly remembered I have something extremely important to do first,\" Dexter lied, his heart pounding against his ribs. \"I need to clean up the kitchen, organize some things, and prepare some medicine. I will head over to the Association on my own in an hour or two. I promise.\"","Rachel narrowed her green eyes suspiciously, her gaze moving from Dexter’s sweating forehead, to Mira’s smiling face, and finally to Selene’s frozen table.","A look of deep, amused understanding appeared in her eyes. She let out a soft, beautiful laugh that sounded like silver bells.","\"Alright, Dexter,\" she said, her voice dripping with amusement. \"I won’t force you. I wouldn’t want to cause any more... domestic disturbances.\"","She stepped forward, as though intending to wrap her arms around his neck for another warm goodbye hug.","Dexter’s survival instincts flared. He immediately, rapidly extended his right hand straight in front of him, keeping a firm, solid distance between them.","Rachel stopped. She stared at his extended hand for a moment, then burst into a loud, delighted laugh.","\"You are cruel, Dexter,\" she teased, but she still reached out and shook his hand, her grip surprisingly firm. \"I’ll see you at the Association branch later. Don’t keep me waiting too long.\"","She turned around, unlocked the door, and stepped out onto the porch.","Once the heavy wooden door finally closed behind her and the lock clicked back into place—","Dexter released a long, deep breath, his shoulders slumping as if he had just survived a life-or-death battle against an S-Class monster. He wiped the cold sweat from his forehead with the back of his sleeve.","\"Phew...\"","He turned around to head back to the kitchen.","\"Fuck!\"","He nearly jumped out of his skin.","Selene was standing directly behind him.","She had moved from the dining table so quietly and silently that even his ’Enhanced Hearing’ had not registered her approach over the sound of his own racing heart.","She stood there, motionless, her long silver hair covering half of her pale face. Her blank, white eyes stared directly at him.","For a moment, in the dim light of the hallway, she genuinely looked like a vengeful, silent ghost from an old horror movie.","Dexter’s heart hammered against his chest. \"Selene! You... you scared me.\"","Selene tilted her head slightly, her expression calm but incredibly serious.","\"Who was she, Dexter?\"","Dexter forced a dry, awkward smile, his hands raised. \"She is Rachel. She is the official representative assigned to our case by the Hunter Association. She came here to complete the paperwork regarding the bridge incident and the assassins.\"","Selene tilted her head to the other side, her white hair shifting. \"What is your relationship with her?\"","Dexter blinked. \"Relationship? We don’t have one. I literally just met her a couple of days ago during the investigation.\"","Selene remained completely silent for several seconds, her face close to his. Dexter could feel the cool, refreshing air radiating from her skin.","Then—","\"Oh.\"","Another long, heavy pause.","\"So you kiss people you don’t have relationships with?\"","Dexter’s eyes widened, and he immediately panicked, his hands waving rapidly.","\"It wasn’t like that! It wasn’t a real kiss! She was drunk and she kissed me. I-I actually pulled back immediately! If that helps...\""]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61 Gifts & Forgiveness","paragraphs":["Selene’s lips curved into a small, delicate smile.","For some reason, that beautiful, gentle smile sent a cold shiver straight down Dexter’s spine. It felt incredibly dangerous.","\"You haven’t kissed your wives,\" she said, her voice quiet and even. \"But you kiss strangers.\"","Step.","She moved half a step closer to him.","Dexter instinctively stepped backward, his heel hitting the wooden baseboard of the front door.","Step.","She moved closer again, her pale, cool hand reaching out to touch the wooden door frame beside his shoulder, pinning him in place.","For the first time since he had met her, Dexter realized that Selene was genuinely, incredibly scary when she wanted to be.","He let out an awkward, nervous laugh. \"I... I didn’t think you girls would appreciate me kissing you. Given our situation, and how much you value your personal space...\"","Selene tilted her head slightly, her blank eyes fixed on his face.","\"But kissing beautiful, wealthy strangers is acceptable?\"","Dexter shook his head violently. \"No! Absolutely not! It’s not like that at all. She... she didn’t know I was married at first. She thought I was single, so she acted a bit forward.\"","He coughed rapidly, trying to find a way out of the conversation.","\"But now that she knows I have three lovely, beautiful, and incredibly cute wives living here with me, she definitely won’t do anything like that ever again. I will make sure of it.\"","Selene remained silent, her pale face just inches from his. She seemed to be listening to his heartbeat, verifying if he was telling the truth.","Eventually, she slowly nodded her head. \"I see.\"","Dexter secretly let out a massive sigh of relief, his muscles relaxing slightly.","Then, Selene asked another quiet question.","\"If she is no longer interested...\"","\"Why did she stay to have tea?\"","Dexter immediately replied. \"Because it was polite! And... and she’s our main contact at the Association. We need to maintain a good, professional relationship with her so we can get our licenses and resources without any administrative delays.\"","Selene slowly nodded again. Then, without another word, she turned around and carefully guided her way back toward the dining table, sitting down in her chair once more as if nothing had happened.","Dexter released a long, shaky breath, leaning against the front door.","Thankfully... that crisis was finally over.","Or so he thought.","He had barely taken five steps down the hallway when he froze in his tracks.","Lyra was standing silently at the entrance of the corridor.","Her dark AI glasses were active, the tiny red lights on the frame blinking slowly.","Even though her eyes were hidden behind the dark lenses, Dexter could feel her gaze. She was staring directly at his face, judging him.","Dexter swallowed hard. Had she heard everything from her room?","He had no idea. But as he walked past her toward the kitchen, he could still feel her eyes tracking his every movement like a silent, judging shadow.","Meanwhile, the temperature in the living room remained incredibly high. Mira’s fire talent was clearly still active, the hot air radiating from her direction practically screaming: ’Danger. Do not enter.’","Dexter wisely decided to avoid the living room entirely.","He quietly retreated to his own small bedroom.","The moment the door closed and the lock clicked, he sank onto his bed and wiped the thick sweat from his forehead.","\"Phew...\"","\"Those girls are absolutely terrifying.\"","He lay back against his flat pillow, staring at the ceiling.","\"Not one.\"","\"Not two.\"","\"Three of them. Three terrifying, powerful women living under my roof.\"","He suddenly paused. A strange, unexpected thought appeared in his mind.","Were they...","Jealous?","Dexter immediately shook his head, dismissing the ridiculous idea.","Impossible. That couldn’t be it.","They had only been living together for a short time, and their relationship had been primarily focused on survival and recovery. There was no way they had developed those kinds of feelings for him so quickly.","After thinking about it for a few minutes, he arrived at what his practical, logical mind considered the correct, obvious answer.","\"They’re just protecting their property,\" he muttered to himself, nodding with confidence.","\"It’s like how kids get angry when someone tries to touch their favorite toys. They don’t want some outsider from the inner districts interfering with their household.\"","Completely unaware of how hilariously wrong his conclusion was, Dexter nodded to himself, feeling highly satisfied with his logical deduction.","A few minutes later, after ensuring the temperature in the living room had returned to normal, he walked back out.","Mira was still sitting in her wheelchair near the window, her arms unmoving on her laps as she stared at the television screen. Her expression remained cold and stubborn.","Without saying a word, Dexter walked over. He reached into his pocket and pulled out a beautiful, delicate necklace.","It was the ’Type-5 Protective Amulet Necklace’ he had received from his system rewards.","The necklace was stunning. It was made of a rare, silver-colored metal that looked like liquid starlight, with a small, deep blue gemstone hanging in the center.","He leaned down and gently placed it around Mira’s neck, fastening the small clasp.","Mira froze. She looked down at the beautiful gem resting against her collarbone, her eyes widening.","Then, she immediately turned her head and glared at him. \"Do you think giving me expensive gifts will make me forgive you for flirting with that woman?\"","Dexter shrugged, offering a small, playful smile. \"Will it work?\"","Mira lowered her eyes back to the gemstone. It was incredibly beautiful.","Far more refined and high-grade than any jewelry her family had owned during their prime. She could feel a gentle, warm energy flowing from the metal, soothing her tense nerves and making her feel remarkably safe.","For several long seconds, she simply stared at it.","Then—","\"Hmph.\"","She turned her head away.","But she did not ask him to remove it.","Dexter smiled. That was already an answer.","Unfortunately—","Lyra had witnessed the entire scene from the hallway."]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62 | Trouble, Heading To The Hero Association","paragraphs":["Unfortunately—","Lyra had witnessed the entire scene from the hallway.","She stood there, staring at the beautiful blue gemstone resting on Mira’s neck. Then, she stared at Dexter’s empty hands.","Then, she turned around and walked back to her room without making a single sound.","Dexter immediately felt a massive headache coming.","Giving a highly valuable, beautiful gift to one girl while leaving the other two completely empty-handed was a massive, amateur mistake in household management.","He made a mental note in his head. ’ Buy two more matching necklaces as soon as possible. Otherwise, my life in this house will become unlivable.’","After settling the immediate matter, Dexter wrapped his blade in clothing and place it behind him.","After making necessary preparations, he looked toward the girls and spoke.","\"I’m heading out to the Hero Association branch now,\" he said, his tone turning serious.","\"I will be officially obtaining my Hero License today.\"","The girls remained silent.","Then, Mira suddenly spoke, her voice quiet but carrying a rare trace of worry.","\"I don’t understand why you are so determined to walk down this path, Dexter.\"","Dexter paused, looking at her.","Mira’s eyes remained fixed on the television screen.","\"We ended up like this because of dungeons. And yet, you are still running toward them with open arms.\"","She paused.","\"I don’t approve of it. But you are a man. So I know you will do whatever you want anyway, regardless of what we say.\"","Dexter let out a soft laugh, his eyes warm as he looked at her.","\"Your reverse psychology won’t work on me, Mira. Just like it didn’t work the first time we met.\"","Mira snorted.","Dexter’s expression softened, his voice turning incredibly serious and gentle.","\"I’ll be careful, Mira. I promise you.\"","\"And don’t worry.\" He grinned, his white teeth showing. \"Your husband is incredibly tough. I’m not that easy to kill.\"","Mira opened her mouth to retort, but then stopped herself.","She recalled the dead assassins on the bridge. They had been experienced, professional killers, yet Dexter had managed to defeat them completely on his own. He was no longer the weak, unawakened youth she had first met.","Eventually, she simply turned her head away. \"Hmph.\"","Dexter smiled. He waved toward the girls. \"I’m leaving now. Take care of yourselves.\"","He walked to the front door, opened it, and stepped onto the porch.","Two seconds later—","He pushed the door open again, sticking his head back inside.","\"And remember, do not open the door for anyone while I am gone. No matter who they claim to be.\"","The response came instantly, loud and highly irritated.","\"You are not our father!\" Mira growled.","Dexter chuckled, closed the heavy door, and locked it from the outside.","As he walked down the cracked concrete steps, the cool morning air brushed against his face, clearing his mind.","He was finally ready. Today, he would officially enter the world of Heroes.","’’’","As Dexter walked down the quiet, sunlit street, his mind was busy calculating his next moves.","The immediate neighborhood was peaceful, a stark contrast to the chaotic, battle-torn streets during the dungeon outbreak.","He noticed a sleek black car parked near the curb about fifty meters down the road. It was a high-end BMW, its polished metal chassis reflecting the bright morning sun. It looked completely out of place in this run-down neighborhood, where most residents drove old, dented trucks or relied on the squeaky public transit buses.","Dexter walked past it, his eyes lingering on the luxury vehicle for a brief second before continuing forward.","A few steps later, he stopped in front of a familiar house.","Tessa’s house.","The heavy iron gate was closed tightly, and a small brass padlock hung from the latch. The windows were shut, and the heavy fabric curtains were drawn closed, keeping the interior dark and silent.","Seeing her house reminded him of her.","as he looked at her property more closely, his sharp senses registered something unusual.","Her house had survived the outbreak completely unscathed. In fact, out of the dozens of homes on this long, dusty street, only five had remained entirely untouched by the rampaging monsters.","Tessa’s house had been one.","It was a highly unusual statistical anomaly.","Monsters during an outbreak were driven by a chaotic, violent urge to destroy everything in their path. They did not usually bypass specific, wooden houses unless there was a powerful deterrent or a reason to avoid them.","Dexter shook his head, pushing the suspicious thoughts away.","He turned and continued walking toward the main road where he could catch a bus to the Hunter Association branch.","Just then—","The smooth, quiet hum of a high-end engine echoed from behind him.","He stopped and turned around.","The sleek black BMW he had passed earlier was slowly, smoothly rolling forward, pulling up right beside him on the dusty roadside.","The tinted glass window slid down silently and Rachel’s beautiful, smiling face appeared from the air-conditioned interior of the car. Her red hair shifted over her shoulder as she leaned toward the passenger side window.","\"Hey there, Dexter!\" she waved enthusiastically, her green eyes bright. \"Get in! I told you I’d be waiting for you.\"","Dexter blinked in surprise, looking at the luxury car and then back down the road toward his bungalow.","\"You were actually waiting for me?\" he asked, a bit dumbfounded.","\"Of course I was,\" Rachel nodded proudly, her lips curving into a playful pout. \"I’m your assigned representative, remember? It’s my job to ensure you reach the Association safely and complete your registration without any issues. Besides, it’s much faster than waiting for the old public bus.\"","Dexter instinctively turned his head, glancing back toward the far end of the street where his small bungalow stood.","The heavy front door remained closed, and there was no sign of his wives at the windows. He let out a silent, massive sigh of relief.","If Mira or Selene were to look out the window right now and see him getting into a luxury car with the very same woman who had just hugged him on their porch, he would probably return tonight to find the house frozen solid or burned to the ground.","He looked back at Rachel, scratching his cheek awkwardly.","Why was this wealthy, high-status woman showing so much personal interest in him?","If they had known each other for years, he would have assumed she had some hidden, calculated motive—perhaps she wanted to use his strength for her own guild, or she wanted to access some non-existent family fortune.","But they had literally just met a couple of days ago. During their brief conversation at the hotel bar, they had simply gotten along well. But that was just a casual chat.","Yet, here she was, waiting for him in her private car, offering him a ride, and teasing him like an old friend.","Dexter could not understand it. Perhaps rich women were simply more forward and direct or perhaps she simply enjoyed the thrill of a challenge.","Rachel pouted from inside the car, her fingers tapping against the leather-wrapped steering wheel.","\"Come on, Dexter,\" she coaxed, her voice soft. \"I’m not going to kidnap you or bite you. It’s just a simple, comfortable ride to the branch office. Please?\"","Dexter looked at her beautiful, pleading green eyes, and then at the clean, luxurious leather seats of the passenger side.","Seeing a stunning woman making puppy eyes at him while offering a free ride in a luxury car was surprisingly difficult to refuse.","Eventually, he let out a defeated sigh and smiled. \"Fine. But just a ride, okay?\"","Rachel’s face lit up with a brilliant, beautiful smile. \"Deal! Get in.\"","Dexter opened the heavy passenger door and stepped inside.","The interior of the BMW was absolutely incredible. It felt like stepping into an entirely different world, far away from the dusty, run-down streets of the outer district. The leather seats were incredibly soft, conforming perfectly to his back, and the air conditioning was cool and carried a faint, refreshing scent of pine.","\"Seatbelt, Dexter,\" Rachel reminded him gently, her eyes lingering on his shoulder as she shifted the car into drive.","\"Right,\" Dexter said, pulling the strap down and clicking it into place.","With a smooth, almost silent purr, the black BMW pulled away from the curb, heading down the dusty street toward the main highway that led straight to the central districts of the city.","Meanwhile—","Behind the closed, blinds of the bungalow’s living room window, three pairs of eyes silently, watched the black car disappear around the far corner of the road.","One pair of dark eyes was cold and narrowed in a deep, burning glare.","One pair of pale, blank eyes was motionless, listening to the fading hum of the high-end engine.","And one pair of eyes, hidden behind active AI glasses, was completely expressionless, recording the entire scene.","The atmosphere inside the small living room suddenly became very, very quiet."]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63 | Crippled Fetish","paragraphs":["Rachel turned the wheel, and the car smoothly exited the street before accelerating onto the larger road beyond.","Inside the vehicle, silence filled the air.","Not the comfortable kind of silence that exists between old friends who have run out of things to say and don’t mind. This was the awkward kind. The kind where both people are acutely aware of the quiet and are thinking about it but neither wants to be the first to acknowledge it.","Dexter sat quietly in the passenger seat while Rachel focused on driving. Every now and then, she stole glances in his direction, a small smile lingering on her lips. Not a polite smile. Something more personal. More intimate. Like she was remembering something pleasant and wanted to share it but was waiting for the right moment.","Dexter shook his head slightly at the awkward atmosphere.","He could feel her gaze landing on him every few seconds. Warm. Persistent. Unapologetic. It was the kind of attention that would have made his heart race a month ago. Back when he was nobody. Back when any beautiful woman showing interest in him would have felt like winning a lottery.","But things were different now.","Not because he didn’t find Rachel attractive. He did. Anyone with eyes would. She had the kind of beauty that turned heads on busy streets. The kind that made people forget what they were doing mid-sentence.","But his life had become complicated in ways that left no room for additional entanglements. Three wives. Three broken women depending on him. Three people who needed his attention far more than a beautiful woman in a BMW.","After several moments, Rachel finally spoke.","\"Should I turn on the radio?\"","Dexter quickly nodded.","\"Yeah.\"","Anything was better than sitting in silence.","Rachel reached over and switched it on.","Unfortunately, fate seemed determined to make things worse.","The first song that played was about romantic tension and unresolved feelings between two people. The lyrics spoke of longing glances and unspoken desires and the space between two people in a car that felt smaller with every passing minute.","Rachel raised an eyebrow.","Dexter stared straight ahead. His jaw tightened slightly. Of all the songs. Of all the stations. Of all the moments.","Then the lyrics became even worse.","The song shifted from romantic tension to blatant sexual tension. The singer’s voice dropped lower. The tempo slowed. Words about heat and skin and temptation filled the car like smoke.","Rachel let out an amused chuckle.","Dexter blinked before immediately turning his head toward the window as if the passing buildings outside had suddenly become fascinating. A mailbox. A fire hydrant. A traffic light. Absolutely riveting. The most interesting traffic light he had ever seen in his entire life.","Rachel struggled to hold back her laughter.","\"Should I change it?\"","Dexter merely shrugged. Casual. Indifferent. As though he hadn’t just been staring at a fire hydrant for eleven seconds straight.","Rachel switched stations.","The next song was somehow even more unfortunate.","This one was about unrequited love. A woman singing about a man who didn’t know she existed. About watching him from afar. About wishing he would turn around and see her standing right there.","Dexter almost facepalmed.","Was the universe actively trying to make this car ride as awkward as possible? Had he offended some cosmic DJ in a previous life? Was there a deity somewhere laughing at him right now?","Rachel finally burst into laughter. Not polite laughter. Full, genuine, shoulder-shaking laughter that made her grip the steering wheel tighter. The kind of laugh that crinkles the eyes and shows teeth and makes the person hearing it want to laugh too even when nothing is funny.","A moment later, Dexter joined in.","He couldn’t help it. The situation was so absurd that fighting it would have been pointless. Here he was. A man with three wives at home who were probably still furious about the morning’s events. Sitting in a luxury car. Listening to love songs. Next to a woman who had kissed him and showed no signs of regretting it.","The tension in the car eased considerably.","Still chuckling, Rachel switched stations again.","Thankfully, the third song was normal.","No love songs.","No confessions.","No hidden meanings.","Just rap music.","Aggressive, loud, completely inappropriate rap music about money and power and surviving the streets. It was so far removed from romance that it practically existed in a different dimension.","Rachel left it there.","For the first time since entering the car, the two began talking naturally.","\"So, Dexter,\" Rachel began, keeping her eyes on the road, \"I didn’t know much about your situation with your three wives before. But after I found out, I looked it up online.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow.","\"And?\"","Rachel glanced at him.","\"There was... a lot.\"","\"What did you read?\"","Rachel looked genuinely surprised.","\"Wait, are you telling me you’ve never searched your own name online?\"","Dexter shook his head.","\"No.\"","\"You really don’t care what people say about you?\"","\"I don’t.\"","He leaned back in his seat. The leather was warm against his back. Comfortable in a way that reminded him how far he still was from providing this kind of comfort for his family.","\"People are going to think whatever they want. Their opinions don’t change my life.\"","He paused.","\"Opinions don’t feed my family. Don’t heal their wounds. Don’t keep them safe at night.\"","Rachel stared at him for a moment before smiling.","\"See? That’s one of the reasons I’m attracted to you.\"","Dexter’s eyes widened slightly.","How could she say something like that so casually? Like telling someone you were attracted to them was the same as commenting on the weather. Oh, nice day today. By the way, I find you attractive. Pass the salt.","Perhaps it was because he already had three wives and women always likes things they can’t get their hands on.","Whatever the reason, he chose not to respond.","Rachel continued anyway.","\"Some people online said you were sold off to the three families.\"","Dexter remained silent and his expression didn’t change. He wasn’t hurt because he had heard worse.","\"Others said you begged your father to arrange the marriage because you desperately wanted three wives.\"","She laughed softly.","\"One post claimed you’re secretly a sadist.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow.","Rachel continued counting on her fingers.","\"And then there were the people claiming that disabled women were your dark fetish.\"","Dexter was stunned. \"People have fetishes about crippled people?\""]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64 | Hero Association","paragraphs":["Rachael shrugged. \"Yeah. There are lots of weird people in this world.\"","Rachel glanced at him.","\"So which one is true?\"","Dexter shrugged indifferently.","\"They might all be right.\"","Rachel blinked.","Dexter simply looked out of the window.","The truth was that there was nothing he wanted to explain.","He had married them.","That was all.","The details of his relationship with his wives were personal, and Rachel was still someone he had only recently met. Trust was built over time. Through actions. Through consistency. Not through confessions shared during a car ride with a woman he barely knew.","He had no intention of discussing it further.","Rachel seemed to understand immediately.","She nodded and quietly dropped the subject.","The car continued through the city streets.","Outside the window, the world unfolded before them.","Massive holographic billboards towered above the roads, displaying advertisements for everything from mana-enhancing supplements to the newest combat gear. One billboard showed a hero in gleaming armor slashing through a monster while text flashed: \"STORMBREAKER BLADES. WHEN YOUR LIFE DEPENDS ON YOUR WEAPON.\"","Electronic flyers drifted through the air, projected by nearby advertisement drones. They displayed discount codes for potion shops and recruitment notices for guilds looking to fill their rosters.","The streets were lively and peaceful.","Children laughed as they ran through nearby parks, chasing each other around fountains that shot streams of mana-infused water into the air. The water changed colors as it fell. Blue. Green. Purple. The children screamed with delight every time the colors shifted.","Parents watched from benches nearby. Some talked on phones. Others read. A few dozed in the morning sunlight with their faces tilted toward the sky.","Large signs pointed toward emergency shelters and evacuation centers built to protect civilians during monster outbreaks. The signs were everywhere. Constant reminders that the peace these people enjoyed existed on a knife’s edge. One breach. One outbreak. One dungeon that spiraled out of control. And this peaceful street would become a battlefield.","In the distance stood enormous Guild Headquarters buildings, their banners fluttering proudly above their entrances. Each guild had its own colors. Its own emblem. Its own identity. They competed for members, resources, and territory like medieval houses vying for power.","Numerous academies could be seen throughout the city, each training the next generation of hunters, warriors, and awakened individuals. Young students in matching uniforms walked along tree-lined paths toward campus entrances. Some carried practice weapons. Others carried stacks of books. A few carried both.","Unlike in the old world, people openly carried weapons on the streets.","Swords rested at people’s waists.","Spears were strapped to backs.","Firearms designed for monster hunting were visible everywhere.","A businessman in a suit walked past carrying a briefcase in one hand and a mana pistol at his hip. A mother pushed a stroller with one hand while a short sword hung from a sheath on her opposite hip. An elderly man sat on a park bench feeding pigeons with a staff leaning against the bench beside him.","No one found it unusual.","Above them, patrol drones flew through the sky, silently monitoring the city below. Their red sensors swept across streets and buildings in systematic patterns. Always watching. Always ready.","Maglev trains powered by mana technology raced across elevated rails overhead. They moved so fast they were barely visible. Silver streaks cutting through the morning sky. Inside them, hundreds of commuters traveled to work, school, and daily obligations while the city hummed with activity below.","The city was alive.","Modern technology and supernatural power existed side by side, woven together into the fabric of everyday life. Magic and machinery. Tradition and innovation. The ancient and the futuristic. All coexisting. All necessary. All part of what kept humanity alive in a world that wanted them dead.","Dexter watched the passing scenery through the window in silence.","For all its chaos and dangers, the world was strangely beautiful.","The journey toward the Hero Association took nearly thirty minutes.","As the city buildings gradually thinned out, Dexter finally saw it in the distance.","His eyes widened.","The Hero Association headquarters wasn’t a building.","It was a fortress.","A massive concrete and alloy structure stretched across several city blocks on the outskirts of Stargate City. It dominated the landscape. Everything else around it looked small. Insignificant. Like the entire city had been built in the shadow of this single structure.","Tall defensive walls surrounded the compound.","Watchtowers stood at every corner.","Anti-air turrets and mana cannons were mounted along the walls, their dark metallic surfaces gleaming beneath the sunlight. Each one was positioned with mathematical precision. No blind spots. No weaknesses. No way in that wasn’t watched and guarded and ready to fire.","From above, the entire facility looked like a mixture of a military fortress, research laboratory, academy campus, and training ground all merged into one gigantic complex. It was as though someone had taken every aspect of the hero world and compressed it into a single location.","Massive banners bearing the Hero Association emblem fluttered in the wind. The emblem was a shield crossed by a sword and a mana circle. Simple. Powerful. Meaningful. Protection. Strength. And the supernatural force that made both possible.","Countless heroes moved in and out of the compound.","Some wore combat armor that covered their bodies from neck to toe. Scratches and dents in the metal told stories of battles fought and survived.","Some wore long coats that billowed behind them as they walked. The kind of dramatic clothing that seemed impractical but somehow looked perfectly natural on someone who could punch through a wall.","Others carried weapons larger than ordinary people could even lift. A woman walked past carrying a hammer the size of a small car over one shoulder. She didn’t seem bothered by the weight. She was eating an apple with her free hand.","Swords, spears, mana rifles and even cannons.","Even beast companions could occasionally be seen following some heroes. A man walked past with a lion the size of a massive horse walking silently beside him. Its fur shimmered with a faint golden glow. Its eyes scanned the crowd with intelligence.","The atmosphere was busy but disciplined.","Professional and incredibly dangerous.","Dexter stared through the window.","\"So this is the Hero Association...\"","Rachel smiled proudly.","\"Impressive, isn’t it?\""]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65 | Ultra Rank","paragraphs":["Dexter nodded honestly.","This place alone was enough to make anyone understand why the Hero Association was considered one of humanity’s greatest powers.","Standing here, watching heroes walk past like ordinary commuters going to work, it was easy to forget that each one of them could probably level a city block if they wanted to.","Near the entrance stood an enormous holographic display.","It displayed rankings, achievements, dungeon statistics, and city-wide alerts. Numbers scrolled constantly. Dungeon clear rates. Monster activity reports. Hero deployment statuses. The information was endless and updated in real time.","One section caught Dexter’s attention immediately.","═══════════════════","Hero Classification System","F-Rank Heroes. Entry-Level Heroes who have successfully cleared at least one dungeon.","E-Rank Heroes. Competent Heroes who have cleared at least three dungeons.","D-Rank Heroes. Experienced Heroes who have cleared at least five dungeons.","C-Rank Heroes. Professional Heroes who have cleared ten or more dungeons, including C-Rank Dungeons.","B-Rank Heroes. Elite Heroes who have cleared twenty or more dungeons, including B-Rank Dungeons.","A-Rank Heroes. Master-Class Heroes capable of clearing S-Rank Dungeons.","S-Rank Heroes. Legendary Heroes capable of changing the fate of entire cities.","════════════════════","Dexter read through the classifications carefully. Each rank represented a different level of power, experience, and responsibility.","The gap between F-Rank and S-Rank was so vast that an F-Rank hero might as well be an ant standing before a dragon.","Yet every hero started somewhere.","Even the legends were once beginners who entered their first dungeon with trembling hands and racing hearts.","As Rachel approached the entrance gate, she produced an identification card.","Several guards immediately saluted.","Dexter, however, wasn’t looking at the card.","He was staring at the guards.","Every single one of them radiated immense pressure.","Superhuman Realm.","Peak Superhuman Realm.","Every single guard.","Dexter couldn’t hide his shock.","Peak Superhumans were supposed to be powerful experts.","The kind of people that ordinary heroes spoke about with respect and caution.","Yet here they were.","Working security.","Standing at gates and checking IDs. Waving cars through. Like bouncers at a nightclub. Except these bouncers could probably flatten the nightclub if they sneezed too hard.","Rachel noticed his expression and laughed softly.","\"Superhuman Heroes aren’t nearly as rare as ordinary people think.\"","She pointed toward one of the guards.","\"Besides, working for the Hero Association pays incredibly well. About 500k annually. \"","\"Many heroes prefer stable income over risking their lives in dungeons every week.\"","Dexter was stunned. That’s almost a billion in one year!","She shrugged.","\"If I didn’t already enjoy field work, I probably would’ve become a guard too.\"","Dexter was genuinely surprised.","Being a guard actually paid that much?","Maybe becoming security wasn’t such a bad career choice after all. Standing at the gate all day, doing nothing but scanning the IDs and getting paid handsomely without dungeon hunting.","It sounded almost peaceful.","Rachel drove toward the parking area and parked the car.","Both of them stepped out.","The inside of the compound was even larger","There were separate buildings everywhere.","The Dungeon Registration Hall. A wide building with a constant flow of heroes entering and exiting.","Some looked excited. Others looked exhausted. A few looked like they had seen things they wished they could forget.","The Hero Licensing Center. A more formal structure with official banners and a line of nervous newcomers waiting outside.","The Medical Wing.","The Hero Hospital. Larger than the Medical Wing. Several heroes on stretchers were being wheeled inside by medical staff while concerned teammates followed behind.","The Research Division. A futuristic building covered in sensors and antennas. Drones flew in and out of open windows carrying samples and equipment.","The Beast Material Exchange Department. Heroes walked out carrying bags of materials. Monster parts. Herbs. Crystals. All harvested from dungeons and brought here for evaluation and sale.","The Auction Hall. An elegant building with marble pillars. Through the open doors, Dexter could hear an auctioneer’s voice calling out prices.","The Training Complex. The largest building visible. Multiple combat arenas were visible through transparent reinforced glass walls. Inside, heroes sparred while instructors observed from elevated platforms.","The Combat Arena. A circular colosseum-like structure that roared with the sound of explosions and cheering crowds.","The Hero Academy Liaison Office. A smaller building with young students in uniforms entering and exiting.","There was even a private shopping district exclusively for registered heroes.","Heroes could buy weapons, armor, artifacts, potions, and dungeon supplies there at discounted prices.","Mana-powered trains connected different sections of the compound together.","Small platforms dotted the pathways where heroes waited for the next train.","The entire place felt like a miniature city.","A city built by heroes and for heroes.","Rachel smiled as she watched his expression.","\"Not what you expected?\"","Dexter shook his head honestly.","\"Not even close.\"","He had expected an office building.","Instead, he found an entire civilization built around heroes. A self-sustaining ecosystem where every need was catered to.","Rachel laughed.","\"Welcome to the center of Stargate City’s power.\"","She led him toward the main entrance.","Heroes constantly passed by them.","Some were chatting casually about recent dungeon runs. Comparing kills and sharing strategies.","Some looked exhausted. Others looked injured. One hero walked past with half his face covered in fresh bandages.","Several carried freshly harvested monster materials.","Dexter even spotted someone carrying the severed claw of a monster larger than a truck.","Suddenly.","His steps suddenly slowed and his pupils constricted as a powerful aura swept past him.","He instinctively turned his head.","An Ultra Rank Hero.","The pressure radiating from the man was unlike anything Dexter had ever felt before.","The man walked through the crowd and people parted around him without being asked. Without even thinking about it. Like water flowing around a stone in a river.","It felt as though a mountain had walked past him.","Before he could fully process it, another figure emerged from the building.","This time, the entire entrance hall fell silent.","People moved aside instinctively for this woman without hesitation.","Dexter looked up.","A woman stepped out of the building.","Long silver hair flowed behind her like a river of moonlight.","She wore a black combat coat with silver trim. The coat was fitted perfectly to her body."]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66 | Meeting With Teammates","paragraphs":["On her chest was an S-rank badge.","A genuine S-Rank Hero.","Following his gaze, Rachel chuckled.","\"That’s Aurora.\"","\"She became an S-Rank Hero just last month after successfully clearing her first S-Rank Dungeon.\"","Dexter stared.","Aurora walked calmly through the courtyard as though she didn’t notice the countless eyes watching her.","\"Her talent is Sky Manipulation,\" Rachel continued.","\"A ridiculously rare ability that lets her control almost anything connected to the sky.\"","Dexter’s eyes widened.","\"That’s absurd.\"","Rachel nodded.","\"It is.\"","\"Wind. Weather. Lightning. Even the air itself bends to her will.\"","\"Some people believe she’ll become one of humanity’s strongest heroes someday.\"","As Aurora disappeared into the distance, paparazzi gathered at the front gate. They didn’t dare enter the Hero Association grounds. That would have been like walking into a lion’s den with a camera and a death wish. But they hovered at the boundary, lenses extended, trying to get better photos of her as she walked away.","Dexter slowly looked back toward the towering Hero Association building.","For the first time since arriving in this world.","He truly felt it.","The world was bigger than he had imagined, much bigger.","The heroes he had fought, assassins he had killed. All of it felt significant in the context of his small life. But standing here, surrounded by people who could probably destroy city blocks without breaking a sweat, he understood how small his world had been.","And somehow.","For the first time.","That thought excited him.","Not because he wanted to compete. But because there was so much room to grow. So much strength to gain so much investment to be made.","\"Alright,\" Rachel said as she led Dexter deeper into the Hero Association headquarters.","Finally, they arrived at a towering silver building.","Large words were engraved above the entrance.","HERO LICENSING CENTER","\"This is where your journey officially begins,\" Rachel said.","The hall inside was enormous.","Far larger than Dexter had expected.","Hundreds of people moved through the building.","Some were newly awakened heroes that couldn’t contain their excitement.","Others were veterans renewing licenses or submitting reports.","Several queues stretched across the hall.","Rachel pointed toward one of them.","\"You’ll need to register first.\"","Dexter looked toward the line.","Around fifteen people were already waiting.","Rachel lowered her voice slightly.","\"The licensing examination itself isn’t complicated.\"","She crossed her arms.","\"Usually it’s a controlled dungeon environment.\"","\"You’ll be observed while fighting monsters alongside several other candidates.\"","\"They’ll evaluate your combat ability, teamwork, decision making, adaptability, and overall potential.\"","Dexter listened carefully.","Rachel continued.","\"Clearing the first wave automatically grants an F-Rank Hero License.\"","\"If you perform better than expected and clear additional waves, your evaluation score increases.\"","\"The Association keeps records of promising newcomers.\"","\"Those with high scores are given priority for dungeon requests, emergency missions, and sponsored expeditions.\"","Dexter nodded.","That sounded reasonable.","However, Rachel suddenly smiled mischievously.","\"Although...\"","\"Don’t try too hard.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow.","Rachel shrugged.","\"The more talented you appear, the more attention you’ll attract.\"","\"The Hero Association values talent.\"","\"But dangerous missions tend to find talented people first.\"","\"If an unusually dangerous F-Rank Dungeon appears. The outstanding rookies are usually among the first names considered.\"","Dexter understood immediately.","Outstanding talent brought opportunities.","But opportunities often came with risks. Sometimes fatal ones.","\"I’ll keep that in mind,\" he replied.","Rachel smiled.","\"Good.\"","Then she leaned slightly closer.","\"Try not to die, alright?\"","Dexter laughed.","\"I’ll do my best.\"","She smiled flirtatiously before turning around and leaving.","\"Good luck, Dexter.\"","He watched her disappear into the crowd, then he joined the queue.","Fifteen people stood ahead of him.","He took ticket number sixteen and waited patiently.","Twenty minutes later, his number was finally called.","The receptionist was a beautiful young woman with glasses and a completely expressionless face.","She barely looked up from her computer.","\"Purpose of visit.\"","\"Hero License Registration.\"","She typed something. Her fingers moved with mechanical speed across the keyboard.","\"Current cultivation level.\"","\"First Rank Superhuman.\"","\"Talent rank?\"","\"E-Rank.\"","For the first time, her fingers stopped moving.","She looked up as her expression shifted slightly.","Superhuman Realm wasn’t particularly impressive inside the Hero Association.","There were thousands of Superhumans within Stargate City alone.","But an E-Rank talent holder reaching the Superhuman Realm at such a young age.","That was different.","It usually meant one of two things.","Exceptional background.","Or exceptional luck.","The receptionist studied him for a moment before returning to her work.","\"Identification card.\"","Dexter handed over his ID.","She scanned it, entered several details into the system, then returned it.","\"For F-Rank Hero Licensing, candidates must clear at least one monster wave inside a controlled dungeon environment.\"","She handed him a temporary identification card.","\"This is your temporary candidate license.\"","She pointed toward a hallway.","\"Proceed to Building Twenty-One.\"","\"Next.\"","Dexter accepted the card and headed toward the designated building.","The door to Building 21 slid open with a soft hiss.","Dexter stepped inside and immediately noticed that he wasn’t the first to arrive.","Four people were already seated in the briefing room.","The first was a tall and handsome young man with sharp features and a confident expression.","He sat lazily with one leg crossed over the other, his posture radiating arrogance and superiority. Everything about him screamed money and privilege. From his tailored clothes to his perfectly styled hair to the expensive-looking sword resting against his chair.","The second was a massive young man built like a tank. His muscles strained against his shirt, and his thick arms looked as if they could crush stone with ease. He sat still with his arms folded across his chest and an enormous shield rested against the wall beside him.","The third was an athletic young woman with shoulder-length black hair and two daggers hanging from her waist.","She looked energetic and approachable, with sharp eyes.","The fourth was a quiet girl sitting in the corner of the room.","A longsword rested against the chair beside her.","The moment Dexter entered, all four pairs of eyes turned toward him.","Or more specifically.","Toward the temporary identification card hanging on his chest.","The large letter printed on it was impossible to miss.","F-Rank Talent Holder."]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67 | Preparations!","paragraphs":["The tall young man frowned immediately.","\"What the hell? Why did they assign an F-rank to our group?\"","He stood up slightly from his chair and stared at Dexter as though looking at a stray animal that had wandered into the wrong room.","\"Seriously? Out of everyone they could have picked, they sent us an F-rank?\"","His expression twisted with annoyance.","\"Great. Looks like we’ll have to babysit dead weight.\"","Before Dexter could respond, the young woman with the daggers suddenly stood up.","\"Ignore him.\"","She walked over with a smile and extended her hand.","\"Hi. My name is Fiona Chen.\"","Dexter shook her hand politely.","She pointed toward the tall young man.","\"That grumpy idiot over there is Marcus Webb.\"","Marcus snorted. \"I’m sitting right here.\"","Fiona ignored him completely and pointed toward the muscular giant.","\"The mountain of muscles is Gregor Halt.\"","Gregor opened one eye, glanced at Dexter for a second, then nodded before closing it again.","Finally, Fiona pointed toward the quiet girl in the corner.","\"And the silent one over there is Lena Park.\"","Lena glanced at Dexter briefly before returning her attention to the floor.","Fiona shrugged helplessly.","\"She’s not very talkative.\"","Dexter nodded.","\"Nice to meet all of you. I’m Dexter Ashford. \"","The moment he said his full name, however, the room became noticeably quieter.","Marcus narrowed his eyes.","\"...Ashford?\"","His expression slowly changed.","Then he smirked.","\"Oh.\"","Realization flashed across his face.","\"So you’re that Ashford.\"","\"The bastard son of the Ashford family.\"","Marcus laughed heartily.","\"I didn’t expect to meet a celebrity here.\"","Dexter remained silent. His expression didn’t change one bit.","Marcus leaned back in his chair.","\"I also heard you recently married three beautiful women.\"","His grin widened.","\"The three crippled daughters from three famous families, right?\"","His eyes carried obvious mockery.","\"So.\"","\"How do they taste?\"","The room instantly fell silent.","\"I’m sure you’ve been enjoying yourself the past two weeks. \"","Marcus laughed.","\"After all, they’re crippled, they can’t exactly run away from you.\"","Fiona’s expression darkened instantly.","\"Marcus!\"","She slammed her hand onto the table.","\"What the hell is wrong with you?\"","Marcus merely shrugged.","\"What? I’m just asking questions.\"","\"Sit the hell down and shut up.\"","For the first time, genuine anger appeared on Fiona’s face.","Marcus stared at her for a few seconds before sneering.","He looked back at Dexter.","\"Just make sure you don’t slow us down in there.\"","\"If you get yourself killed, don’t expect me to save you.\"","With that, he sat back down.","Fiona turned toward Dexter apologetically.","\"Sorry about that.\"","Dexter shook his head.","\"You don’t have to apologize.\"","\"It isn’t your fault.\"","He calmly walked over to an empty chair and sat down.","Marcus’ words didn’t bother him.","Compared to everything he had experienced over the last few weeks, it was nothing.","He had been looked down on his entire life. One more person looking down on him was just another drop in an ocean.","Fiona sighed in relief before glaring at Marcus one final time and returning to her seat.","The room gradually fell silent once more.","All five candidates waited quietly for the arrival of the proctor.","Five minutes later, the door opened.","A middle-aged man wearing an expensive suit entered the room. His hair was graying at the temples and hw stood with straight posture.","His eyes were sharp despite his age as he smiled at the group.","\"Welcome, candidates.\"","His smile widened.","\"Or should I say.\"","\"Welcome, future heroes.\"","Several of them straightened their backs immediately. Because they were a reminder of why everyone was here. To become heroes. To protect people.","The man activated a holographic display.","A map appeared in the air.","\"Your examination will take place inside a controlled dungeon environment.\"","\"The monsters are real.\"","\"The danger is real.\"","\"Only the environment itself is controlled.\"","The room grew quiet.","\"The dungeon currently contains monsters ranging from One Star to Six Star.\"","He glanced at the candidates.","\"Our strongest participant today is a Third Rank Superhuman.\"","He turned to look at Marcus.","\"Therefore, the Association has limited the highest threat level accordingly.\"","The candidates visibly relaxed.","The instructor continued.","\"There will be three monster waves.\"","\"Clear Wave One and you earn your F-Rank Hero License.\"","\"Clear Wave Two and your rookie ranking score increases significantly.\"","\"Clear Wave Three and your name enters the Association’s Novice Leaderboard.\"","Several candidates became excited immediately. The Novice Leaderboard was where every rookie dreamed of appearing. It was the first step toward recognition. Toward sponsorships. Toward the kind of career that turned names into legends.","The instructor nodded.","\"High rankings bring benefits.\"","\"Higher mission priority.\"","\"Higher dungeon invitations.\"","\"Emergency response opportunities.\"","\"Sponsorship offers.\"","\"Resources.\"","\"Training recommendations.\"","Then his expression became serious.","\"The Association tracks every participant individually.\"","\"The more monsters you kill, the higher your score.\"","\"Cooperation is encouraged but not required.\"","\"If a candidate suffers fatal injuries, emergency extraction protocols will activate immediately.\"","\"Death inside the testing dungeon is extremely unlikely.\"","He paused.","\"However.\"","\"Injury is very real.\"","\"Broken bones are common.\"","\"Severe injuries are not uncommon.\"","The room became silent once more.","The instructor smiled.","\"If you’re afraid, now is the time to leave.\"","Nobody moved.","\"Excellent.\"","The instructor turned toward the exit.","\"Follow me.\"","As the group stood and followed him toward the dungeon entrance, Dexter listened with only half his attention.","The other half of his attention was busy calculating.","Because among everyone present.","He could already roughly estimate their strength.","Marcus was Tier 3 Superhuman. But his arrogance would make him predictable.","Gregor was Tier 2.","Fiona was Tier 1.","Lena was also Tier 1 and for himself, his actual cultivation was Tier 3 Superhuman but because of his bloodline, he could actually control the energy wave his body releases, making himself a walking Tier 1 Superhuman.","But his real combat strength far exceeded that.","Following the instructor, the group headed deeper into the Hero Association headquarters.","They eventually arrived at a large elevator located at the end of a heavily guarded corridor.","The instructor stepped inside first and the six candidates followed behind him."]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68 | Mana Hurricane!","paragraphs":["The apartment felt strangely peaceful after Dexter left.","Silence settled over the house.","The apartment had been completely restored by the Hero Association. Every cracked wall had been repaired and repainted and even the shattered window had been replaced with new glass so clear it seemed invisible and every damaged piece of furniture had been restored or replaced with identical items.","If someone had never seen the destruction caused by the monster attack, they would never believe anything had happened here.","Even the kitchen looked brand new. The countertops gleamed. The stove sparkled.","The refrigerator hummed quietly in the corner.","The lingering aroma of breakfast still floated through the apartment. Diamond Rice had a unique scent that lingered for hours. It was subtle and pleasant, like the memory of a beautiful dream.","Lyra sat on the couch, hugging a pillow as she lazily rubbed her full stomach. Her feet were tucked beneath her. Her smart glasses reflected the light on the ceiling and beside her rested several empty bowls stacked carelessly on the table. A pile that would have embarrassed any ordinary person.","She had folded and eventually eaten the ordinary rice Dexter had prepared","The food had been delicious.","No...","It had been unbelievable.","She had never tasted anything like it. Every grain of rice had seemed alive on her tongue. Every bite had been like swallowing pure energy. The warmth had spread from her stomach to her fingertips to the roots of her hair.","She wasn’t even cultivating but the Grand Cosmos Scripture was automatically circulating, draining in mana from the void by itself after her absorption speed increased so massively. Her muscles felt loose and relaxed and her mind felt sharp and clear.","She couldn’t understand how Dexter’s cooking kept improving every single day. It wasn’t a gradual improvement either.","Meanwhile...","Selene quietly returned to her room.","She closed the door behind her with a soft click and sat cross-legged on the bed with her back straight and her palms resting on her knees. She closed her eyes and breathed in slowly.","She breathed out slowly.","Golden streams of mana drifted through the room like invisible currents. With the permanent increase of absorption speed, mana flowed like a flood into her, through her pores.","They flowed through the air in spirals before being drawn toward the dormant Star Node within her body.","Unlike ordinary cultivation techniques that relied on shattered meridians...","The Grand Cosmos Scripture ignored them entirely.","Every strand of mana bypassed the broken pathways inside her body and flowed directly toward the sleeping Star Node. It was like water finding a new route around a collapsed dam. The mana didn’t force its way through. It simply went around.","It was nothing short of miraculous.","There was no burning sensation nor was there any sharp stabs in her chest or feeling of her meridians tearing apart under pressure.","Just mana flowing into her ceaslessly.","A faint smile unknowingly appeared on Selene’s lips. It was small and barely visible. But it was real.","She treasured this feeling. She held onto it like a precious gem found in the dark and this was all due to Dexter. Her life changed when she met him and he hadn’t stopped surprising them yet.","Outside the room...","Mira rested quietly on her wheelchair near the living room window. The morning sunlight streamed through the glass and warmed her face. Her eyes remained closed as she also cutivated.","Streams of energy flowed through her like a dam released. Even the window shook with pressure as mana surged directly towards her.","If it wasn’t for the barrier, the neighbors with sharp mana affinity would be stunned to see as mana roared and surrounded the entire house like a barrier surging around as though a mana vaccum was in side the room.","They called this phenomenon Mana Hurricane. It was rumored that only when someone with SSS rank mana affinity was cultivating or when a Transcendent level Hero was cultivating did this phenomenon happen. And right now, it was happening in Dexter’s house.","Simultaneously, orange glowing spectral arms floated behind her.","Although she had awakened them yesterday, controlling them still felt awkward. It was like trying to write with her feet, it was clumsy.","She needed practice.Lots of practice but Still...","Compared to lying helplessly in bed, unable to move, unable to reach for a cup of water, unable to scratch her own nose...","This tiny improvement was enough to give her hope.","Hope that perhaps... One day...","She would stand again.","Hours quietly passed.","The apartment remained silent except for the faint sounds of breathing as the three girls immersed themselves in cultivation. The clock on the wall ticked steadily. Sunlight crept across the floor in slow steps, just like a thief.","It was nearly noon when Selene finally opened her eyes.","\"...Water...\"","Her throat felt slightly dry. Cultivating for extended periods always left her dehydrated.","Without disturbing the others, she slowly stood up from the bed. She pushed herself upright with both hands and waited a moment for her balance to stabilize.","Although blind, she had memorized every corner of the apartment within two days after moving in. She had walked the space countless times since then, mapping it in her mind.","She quietly made her way toward the kitchen. Her bare feet touched the floor softly, making almost no sound.","Her fingers lightly brushed against the wall as she walked. The texture of the wallpaper guided her forward. Smooth. Cool. Familiar.","Ten more steps...","Five...","Three...","She reached the kitchen.","Using memory alone, she stretched her hand toward the cabinet where the drinking glasses were stored. Her fingers found the edge of the counter. She traced along it until she reached the correct spot, her hand moving with the confidence of someone who had done this exact motion hundreds of times.","At that exact moment, a sharp sound echoed overhead.","CRACK!","The wall-mounted cabinet suddenly tilted forward without warning. One of the screws holding it in place had apparently loosened during the previous repairs. The repair team had replaced the cabinet but hadn’t checked the mounting brackets thoroughly.","The entire wooden cabinet detached from the wall. It swung downward heavily.","Straight toward Selene’s head."]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69 | I can See You","paragraphs":["The entire wooden cabinet detached from the wall as it swung downward heavily.","Straight toward Selene’s head.","Everything happened in less than a second.","Lyra had been watching Selene curiously ever since she came out from the room. So when the cabinet started to shake. She saw it and also watched saw as the cabinet fell with Selene standing directly beneath it.","Her mouth opened to scream out with warning, but no sound came out.","Mira’s eyes instantly snapped open. Superhuman Heroes hearing range was about a 100 meter radius so she heard as the cabinet started to fall.","She turned around only to watch the cabinet fall directly on Selene.","\"Selene!\"","Neither Mira nor Lyra could react in time.","The cabinet was already falling. Gravity pulled it down with relentless force. Glasses and cups spilled from inside, shattering against the counter below.","Yet...","At that very instant —","Something shocking happened.","\"Crack!\"","Something snapped inside of her, like a dam breaking inside her soul.","\"BOOM!\"","An invisible pulse exploded outward from her body, expanding in every direction like a shockwave made of pure energy. It passed through walls, furniture, and air without disturbing any of it physically.","But to Selene...","The world suddenly changed.","Ripples spread through the air like circles across a still lake. Each ripple carried information. Each wave painted a picture.","Every vibration...","Every heartbeat...","Every movement...","Everything around her became astonishingly clear and she suddenly realized with astonish shock that... she could see.","She couldn’t see with her eyes, but With sound instead.","The pulse she had released bounced off every surface and returned to her. The returning waves carried shapes, distances, and textures. Her brain processed them instantly, constructing a three-dimensional image of her surroundings.","She could feel the cabinet falling above her, she could tell its weight, its speed and even Its trajectory.","Her hand shot upward instinctively.","\"Bam!\"","The heavy cabinet landed firmly in her palmx stopping it from falling on her, barely an inch above her head.","The impact sent a jolt through her arm. The wood was heavy. The edges dug into her skin. But she easily held it with her strength.","Silence filled the entire apartment.","Broken glass lay scattered across the counter and floor. A coffee mug rolled in a slow circle, its handle snapped off.","Lyra froze in place. One foot was mid-step about to activate her movement technique. Her hand was still reaching toward the kitchen.","Mira’s pupils contracted to pinpoints. Her Spectral Arms had already formed halfway when this shocking thing happened.","Even Selene herself stood motionless. Her breath came in short gasps. Her arm trembled under the weight of the cabinet.","Slowly...","Very slowly...","She lowered the cabinet onto the floor. It landed with a heavy thud as the glasses inside clinked against each other.","Her breathing became uneven. Her chest rose and fell rapidly. Sweat beaded on her forehead.","\"What...\"","She whispered as her voice trembled in shock.","\"I...\"","She slowly turned her head.","Although her empty eyes remained unfocused...","She could perceive the outlines of the kitchen. Shapes appeared before her like shadows painted on black canvas.","She couldn’t see colors but she could see clearly in black and white. And the shapes were extremely clear but the details not soo much.","The kitchen counter stretched before her like a long flat shadow.","The refrigerator hummed to her right, its outline clearer than everything else because of the constant vibration of its motor.","The dining table stood in the center of the room, four chairs tucked around it.","Everything appeared like pale silhouettes floating inside an endless black world. Like watching ghosts move through dark water.","She lifted a trembling hand toward her own face.","\"...I...\"","Tears suddenly welled inside her eyes before spilling over.","\"I...\"","\"I can...\"","Her voice cracked as though she still couldn’t believe it.","\"I can really see...\"","The words barely escaped Selene’s lips before tears spilled down her cheeks. They ran in silent streams, dripping from her jaw onto the floor.","Her entire body trembled from overwhelming emotion that had been locked inside her for years.","For years, she had lived in endless darkness without shapes colors or form, missing countless sunrise and moonlight. Nor even able to see shadows or light of any kind.","Nothing but an eternal black world. A void that swallowed everything. She had forgotten what her own hands looked like. She had forgotten what the sky looked like. She had forgotten what faces looked like.","Yet now...","Although the world before her was slightly blurry and colorless...","Although it was made of vibrations rather than light...","It was still a world and a world she could perceive, a world that existed beyond the darkness.","She slowly lifted both hands, staring at them with disbelief. Rather than seeing flesh and skin, she perceived two hazy silhouettes outlined by countless vibrating waves. She could see her fingers. She could see them move when she wiggled them.","Everything around her was the same.","The walls...","The table...","The chairs...","Even the air itself seemed alive with rippling vibrations. Every surface reflected her pulse back to her, creating a constantly updating image of her surroundings.","It was unlike normal vision.","It was something completely different.","Something that transcended sight itself and she felt that she could see farther and more detailed than true sight even though it isn’t as detailed as real eyes.","She couldn’t see the moles or pores or her finger nails or details like that, but it was still amazing.","\"...I can really see...\"","Her knees nearly gave out beneath her. She grabbed the edge of the counter to steady herself.","\"Selene!\"","\"Are you alright?\"","Selene turned toward the familiar voice and saw Mira in the wheelchair, her neck turned as she faced her and looked at her worriedly.","For the first time...","She wasn’t merely listening to the voice, she could actually distinguish Mira’s figure.","A blurry silhouette sitting in a wheelchair. She could see the wheels. She could see Mira’s arms. She could see her hair falling over her shoulders.","Selene gasped in disbelief and excitement. She slowly walked towards Mira and stopped before her. Bending down slightly,","\"I...\"","\"I can see you...\"","Mira froze."]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70 | Selene’s Second Awakening","paragraphs":["\"What?\"","\"I can see you...\"","Selene repeated, her voice shaking as she spoke.","\"It isn’t clear...\"","\"I can’t see colors...\"","\"Everything is black and white. But... I can see...\"","She didn’t try to wipe the tears in her face. She didn’t even notice she was crying at this point.","Her hands reached forward, and they accurately touched Mira’s shoulders.","She knelt beside the wheelchair and she gently cupped Mira’s face with trembling hands.","Her fingertips slowly traced Mira’s cheeks. The curve of her jaw. The bridge of her nose. The softness of her skin.","As she touched each feature, the blurry outline in her strange vision became clearer. The combination of touch and vibration created a more detailed image than either sense alone.","\"You’ve gotten much thinner. Since the accident.\"","She smiled through her tears. The smile was raw and completely unguarded. It was the most honest expression Selene had worn in years.","\"You’re beautiful regardless.\"","Mira remained speechless. Her mouth opened slightly but no words came out. Her eyes glistened. She blinked rapidly, as though trying to hold back her own tears","She had never seen Selene cry this much before. Not even after the accident.","But today...","She cried like a little girl.","Lyra quietly walked to them, watching silently. Her smart glasses translated what was been said rapidly to texts for her.","Her lips pressed together tightly as she was stunned when she read what was been said.","Selene sensed another familiar presence. The new sight was fully 360, unlike normal sight, so she could see behind her as Lyra approached.","She turned toward Lyra.","Although the outline was slightly blurrier than Mira’s, she could still make out the young woman’s figure. Her slender frame, her glasses, and the way she tilted her head when observing something.","She reached out.","Selene gently held Lyra’s cheeks. Her trembling fingers carefully explored every contour of her face.","A smile slowly appeared on Selene’s face.","\"You look so much different now.\"","Lyra’s eyes became moist. She blinked several times. A single tear escaped and rolled down her cheek, touching Selene’s fingertip.","She couldn’t hear Selene’s voice. She hadn’t heard a single word spoken in the kitchen.","But even without the glasses, she could understand from her lips.","She nodded gently.","Selene chuckled softly.","\"As time went on, my senses lost their perspective, and my memories weren’t what they once were. Everyone’s faces gradually got lost, and I thought I would never see your faces again.\"","She looked at the two girls with a grin. \"Now I can see your faces.\"","The two girls faintly smiled at her.","Several minutes passed before Mira finally broke the silence. She cleared her throat softly.","\"...Tell me, what exactly happened?\"","Selene took a deep breath as she thought back to it with furrowed brows.","\"I have no idea either. The cabinet was falling, I heard your voice and thought there was an assassin, and then...\"","\"The entire world suddenly opened.\"","She closed her eyes.","The strange perception didn’t vanish instantly.","\"It doesn’t work with my eyes,\" she murmured as she covered her ears.","Suddenly, the strange perception diminished but didn’t disappear.","\"When I close them, it reduces...\"","She closed her ears again. Then opened them. Closed. Opened.","Each time, the vibration-sight appeared and disappeared.","\"It feels...\"","She searched for the right words. Her brow furrowed in concentration.","\"...like I’m hearing vibrations.\"","\"I don’t see light.\"","\"I don’t see colors.\"","\"I only see movement.\"","\"The stronger the vibration...\"","\"The clearer it becomes.\"","She pointed toward the refrigerator. \"That’s the clearest thing in the room. Because it’s always humming.\"","Then she pointed toward Lyra. \"You’re the blurriest. Because you barely move. I think it’s due to your shadow talent.\"","Mira’s expression gradually became serious. Her mind was already working. Her eyes widened as a thought struck her.","\"A talent...\"","Selene blinked in confusion; so did Lyra, as they looked at her curiously.","\"A talent?\"","Mira nodded slowly as she remembered what happened to her.","\"I think you’ve awakened a second talent.\"","The room instantly fell silent.","Second awakening.","Those two words carried enormous weight.","Throughout the entire city...","Double Awakeners were almost nonexistent. The probability was so astronomically low that most people considered it a myth. A fairy tale told to young awakeners to give them false hope.","The chance of awakening a second talent was less than one in a hundred thousand.","Many people with low talent spent their entire lives hoping for such a miracle. They risked their lives in dungeons searching for items that might trigger a second awakening.","Most died without ever experiencing it.","Yet...","Selene had just awakened one. Sitting in a kitchen and catching a falling cabinet.","Mira stared thoughtfully at her. Her eyes narrowed slightly.","\"If I’m right...\"","\"It should be an A-Rank sensory talent.\"","\"A talent that allows you to perceive the world through vibrations.\"","Selene slowly nodded.","\"It does feel like that...\"","\"I don’t use my eyes...\"","\"I use...\"","She hesitated. The sensation was still so new. So foreign.","\"...everything around me.\"","Lyra suddenly began typing rapidly on her phone. Her thumbs flew across the screen.","A second later, the AI speaker spoke in its mechanical voice.","\"Like a bat?\"","Selene blinked.","Her eyes slowly widened.","\"...Yes.\"","\"Exactly like a bat.\"","\"I send something out...\"","\"And it comes back.\"","\"That’s how I can see.\"","Mira tilted her head, and she thought of a talent that fits the description.","\"...Echolocation.\"","\"The talent is called Echolocation.\"","\"It’s a rare sensory talent. \"","The three girls exchanged stunned looks as the information settled on them.","Suddenly, Mira closed her eyes and then two orange spectral arms emerged from behind her. Even Selene could see those arms as they floated in the air.","The two girls were shocked.","\"W-what is that?\"","Mira inhaled and replied. \"I also awakened a second talent yesterday. I call it mana arms.\"","Lyra and Selene were really surprised. \"You awakened yesterday, and now Selene awakens today. Which means I might awaken a second talent tomorrow.\""]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71 | Lyra’s Awakening I","paragraphs":["Mira frowned as she slowly exhaled.","\"Something is not right.\"","Selene looked toward her, the blurry outline of Mira’s face turning in her direction.","\"What do you mean?\"","Mira frowned. The lines on her forehead deepened.","\"A second awakening is not something that simply happens. It has an extremely low probability. In the entire city, there has not been a confirmed Double Awakener in years. Maybe decades. And now you suddenly awaken one too?\"","She shook her head slowly.","\"It does not make sense.\"","Selene lowered her head. She stared at her own hands. The blurry silhouettes of her fingers wiggled back at her, still strange and wonderful even as doubt crept into her mind.","\"I do not know,\" she admitted quietly.","\"I awakened mine and thought I was lucky. But now you awakened one too. That changes everything.\"","Lyra quickly typed on her phone.","The AI voice echoed through the room.","\"Could it be that strange accident that did this to us?\"","Selene was the first to shake her head slowly.","\"I do not think it was the accident. There were many injured people along with us during the expedition. If the accident caused this, others should have awakened too. We would have heard about it from our families.\"","Mira agreed.","\"Exactly. So it was not the accident. The accident just caused this. It did not give us anything new.\"","Lyra typed another question.","\"Then what do we all have in common?\"","\"The food?\" Selene suggested. Her voice was hopeful but uncertain.","Mira immediately shook her head.","\"I awakened mine before we ate the meal. It can’t be the tea\"","\"The cultivation technique?\" Selene asked again. It was the only thing that made sense.","Mira frowned deeper, the crease between her eyebrows becoming more pronounced.","\"I have never heard of a cultivation technique granting talents. No matter how powerful. The Grand Cosmos Scripture is incredible, but it is still just a cultivation method. It helps you gather and circulate mana. It does not create talents. Talents come from the soul, not from mana.\"","Again, silence.","The three girls sat quietly in the room, thinking.","Then, almost simultaneously, the same name surfaced in all three of their minds.","\"Dexter,\" Mira whispered.","Selene’s pupils contracted behind her white eyes.","Lyra slowly looked toward Dexter’s empty room. His door was open and she could see half way into his room.","Everything had started after meeting him.","The miraculous tea, the astonishing meals, and the impossible cultivation technique that appeared out of nowhere.","And now two second awakenings. Both happening within days of each other. Both happening to people living under the same roof as Dexter.","None of it made sense unless you connect Dexter to it.","Selene slowly muttered, \"It cannot be him. No one can grant talents.\"","Her voice was uncertain, and she wanted to believe it was impossible. But the evidence was piling up, and each new piece fit the pattern too perfectly to ignore.","Mira nodded.","\"I know. It should not be possible. Talents are innate.\"","She paused, her gaze drifting around the apartment.","\"But the only common factor between us is Dexter.\"","Lyra’s fingers slowly hovered above her phone. She wanted to type something but could not find the right words.","Instead of typing, she closed her eyes.","A thought surfaced inside her mind.","What if I awakened too?","The thought took hold, and it refused to let go no matter how much she tried to push it away.","She slowly sat cross-legged on the couch, and both Mira and Selene looked at her curiously.","\"What are you doing?\" Mira asked.","Lyra opened one eye before typing.","The AI speaker responded.","\"If both of you awakened, maybe I have one too.\"","Mira blinked, caught off guard by the statement.","\"That is,\" she started, then stopped to think. Her frown deepened as she considered the possibility. Then slowly, reluctantly, she nodded.","\"It is not impossible. If there really is a common trigger, and all three of us were exposed to the same things, then perhaps you should try sensing your body.\"","Selene smiled encouragingly. Through her vibration sight, she could see Lyra sitting on the couch. The blurry outline of her folded legs. The way her hands rested on her knees, palms up in a meditation posture.","\"Close your eyes. Do not think about anything else. Just feel.\"","Lyra nodded.","She slowly closed her eyes.","The apartment fell completely silent. Even the refrigerator seemed to quiet its humming, though that was probably just her imagination.","She regulated her breathing.","She focused on her body.","Something that would indicate a hidden talent waiting to be discovered.","Minutes passed, but nothing happened.","She searched every corner of her body with her mind, looking for anything different, anything new, but there was nothing—just the darkness of the endless void and the three blazing star modes.","Apart from that’s sh has nothing.","After nearly ten minutes, she slowly opened her eyes and shook her head.","Nothing.","Mira smiled gently.","\"Do not force it. Maybe it just needs more time. Or maybe it will come when you least expect it. That is how these things usually work.\"","Lyra sighed quietly in disappointment.","She had honestly been hoping for a miracle after seeing Mira’s Spectral Arms and Selene’s Echolocation, but it didn’t happen.","Still, seeing Selene smile for the first time in years, seeing Mira regain a little independence with her new arms, she was genuinely happy for them. That happiness outweighed her own disappointment.","Even if she remained the same, she could still see what they were saying with the AI glasses. It was nice.","Lyra let out another quiet sigh and slowly stood up to go to the room.","Just as she was about to leave the kitchen, she heard a voice speaking.","\"Don’t try to give up. Just try again.\"","Lyra frowned and looked towards Mira. She clearly didn’t see her mouth move, so how did she speak? Not to mention. She heard her eardrum had been thoroughly destroyed, so how could she hear anything?","’It must have been the wind.’"]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72 | Lyra’s Awakening II","paragraphs":["Seeing Lyra gaze at her like that, Mira raised an eyebrow.","\"What happened?\"","Lyra blinked in confusion. She quickly typed on her phone.","\"Did you say something just now?\"","The AI glasses read the words aloud in their flat, emotionless tone.","Mira looked puzzled. Her brow furrowed.","\"No. I only spoke a minute ago. I have not spoken since then.\"","Selene nodded in agreement.","\"I did not hear her say anything either.\"","Lyra froze.","A strange feeling crept into her chest. It was Like standing at the edge of a cliff in the dark, knowing something was there but not being able to see it.","Then the voice came again.","\"So sad. She’s truly desperate to awaken a second talent to help her hear sounds again.\"","Lyra’s breathing hitched, and her heart skipped a beat.","This time the voice sounded clearer, and she saw Mira didn’t open her mouth, but she clearly heard her voice.","And it was coming from inside her head.","She looked deeply at Mira again. Her eyes were wide. Searching.","\"You really did not say anything and are not tricking me?\"","Mira slowly shook her head. Her expression was serious now, concern replacing her earlier confusion.","\"No. I have been quiet this whole time.\"","Selene’s expression gradually turned serious as well. Through her vibrating sight, she could see Lyra’s heartbeat increasing. The vibrations coming from her body were accelerating, her chest pulsing faster than before.","\"Lyra, a-re you actually hearing voices?\"","Lyra swallowed. Her throat felt tight and dry.","She slowly typed.","\"It sounds like Mira’s voice.\"","Mira frowned.","\"But I never said it, and you also can’t hear anything.\"","The AI glasses translated the words, and the apartment became eerily quiet.","A chill ran down all three of their spines simultaneously.","Lyra slowly sat back down on the couch in dejection. Maybe she really was wishing she had a second talent and was hallucinating Mira’s voice.","’Try again.’","The voice sounded out, and this time it was Selena’s voice.","Lyra didn’t bother checking if it was hallucinations but closed her eyes and tried again.","This time she really calmed herself down and listened.","Nothing happened as expected.","But after 7 minutes, a strange frequency seemed to spread through the room. It radiated outward from her mind like a pulse, similar to Selene’s echolocation but different.","It was faint at first. Almost impossible to notice. Like hearing a whisper from across a vast field, carried on wind that kept shifting direction.","Yet the more she focused, the louder it became.","Then a gentle voice echoed inside her mind.","’Come on. One more try. You can do it.’","Lyra’s eyes snapped open.","She looked directly at Selene. Her expression changed, and her lips parted slightly.","Selene blinked.","\"What?\"","Lyra immediately began typing furiously. Her thumbs hammered the screen, making mistakes in her haste.","The AI speaker read her words correctly without including the mistakes.","\"You keep encouraging me.\"","Selene stared at her.","\"I did not. I swear on my life, I did not say anything.\"","Lyra’s fingers paused above the screen.","First it was Mira, and now it was Selene.","If it was not them, then whose voice was she hearing?","Suddenly her body trembled violently.","A sharp pulse exploded inside her mind. It was like a door being kicked open. A wall collapsing. A dam breaking after years of holding back pressure.","\"BOOM!\"","The world around her suddenly became noisy.","Countless voices flooded into her consciousness all at once.","Fragments of thoughts from everywhere.","The neighbor on the left thinking about what to make for lunch, the words drifting through her mind like smoke.","A child on the street below wondering if it would rain, a dog somewhere nearby feeling hungry but loved playing toss and chase.","Random emotions washed over her in waves. Confusion. Hunger. Sleepiness. Boredom. Excitement. Loneliness. They came from every direction, overlapping and mixing until she could not tell where one ended and another began.","Everything rushed into her mind at once—a tidal wave of unfiltered consciousness from every living thing within range.","\"Mmm.\"","She made a sound of discomfort. She couldn’t feel pain due to Dexter taking her pain away, but she still felt the discomfort.","Lyra instinctively covered her head with both hands. Her fingers pressed against her temples hard enough to hurt. Her face turned pale, and her body curled inward, making herself as small as possible.","Mira immediately wheeled herself forward. Her Spectral Arms reached out, the crimson limbs extending toward Lyra.","\"Lyra! What is wrong?\"","Selene hurried over as well. She could see Lyra’s body shaking and the rapid pulsing of her heart even from across the room.","Lyra squeezed her eyes shut. The voices became even louder and more insistent.","Dozens of minds pressing against hers simultaneously, all of them unaware that she could hear them.","Then one voice suddenly became clear. Crystal clear. It cut through the noise like a blade through static.","’What’s wrong with her?’","’Is this a backlash?’","Lyra’s body froze.","That voice.","It belonged to Mira.","She recognized the tone. She had heard it 2 years ago, during the expenditure.","Slowly, Lyra opened her eyes.","She looked at Mira without blinking.","Mira frowned.","\"What?\"","Lyra typed with trembling fingers.","The AI speaker spoke.","\"You were thinking about me.\"","Mira blinked.","\"Of course I was. You just collapsed. I am worried about you.\"","\"No.\" Lyra shook her head firmly, her expression intense.","She typed again.","\"I think I heard your thoughts.\"","\"Eh?\"","The room fell completely silent.","Selene stared at her in disbelief. Her mouth hung open slightly.","Mira’s pupils contracted.","\"What?\"","Lyra took a deep breath.","She closed her eyes again.","The strange frequency returned. This time she controlled it and focused it solely on the person sitting directly in front of her, blocking out everything else.","Immediately a stream of thoughts entered her mind.","’Did she really awaken too?’","Lyra opened her eyes again in shock then she unconsciously spoke to them.","’Mira, you just said this in your mind. ’Did she really awaken too? It will be best if all three of us awakened with no one left behind.’’","Mira’s face changed slightly.","\"I, I never said those aloud. But I was thinking of them. Which means you’ve also awakened and you can read minds.\"","She stopped as her eyes widened when she realized Lyra didn’t actually use the AI glasses to speak, she spoke directly into her mind.","Selene was stunned as she also heard Lyra’s voice.","Their eyes widened as they both stared at Lyra as though she had grown two heads.","Lyra only realized after they told her.","’You can hear us and speak now? Your second talent is truly amazing.’","’Since it’s not just reading minds but speaking directly into them, it’s called Telepathy Talent.’","Mira nodded her head with a small smile","Lyra stared blankly at them. She had actually awakened too, and for the first time in two years, she could hear people’s voices and also express herself."]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73 | First Dungeon","paragraphs":["Following the instructor, the group walked deeper into the Hero Association headquarters.","They finally reached a large elevator at the end of a heavily guarded corridor.","Two massive guards stood on either side.The instructor nodded at them and pressed a button on the wall, and the elevator doors slid open.","The instructor stepped inside first. The six candidates followed behind him.","As soon as everyone entered, the instructor pressed a button. -15.","’-15?’","Dexter raised his eyes in surprise.","Only now did he truly notice the enormous list of floors beside the elevator panel.","There were thirty floors above ground, but beneath them, another thirty floors went deep into the earth, from 0 to -30.","It felt like the Hero Association was not just a building but was was practically an underground city. Thirty floors of secrets buried beneath the soil, Dexter couldn’t help but image what was hidden down there.","The elevator doors closed with a soft thud, and immediately the platform began descending.","-3.","-10.","-15.","The whole elevator stayed silent during the fall, nobody speaking.","Perhaps it was because six strangers were trapped together inside a small metallic box. Perhaps it was the knowledge of what waited below. Perhaps it was the simple fact that the earth was pressing in around them and the only direction was down.","Dexter could even hear the breathing of everyone around him.","Behind him, the tall young man crossed his arms impatiently while tapping his fingers against his arm.","The dagger woman leaned lazily against the wall. While the muscular giant remained expressionless.","The quiet girl in the corner lowered her head and said nothing","Meanwhile, Dexter’s thoughts had already drifted elsewhere. Specifically How exactly was he going to find two necklaces similar to the one he had given Mira?","Giving one wife a gift without giving the other two the same gift.","That was simply asking for trouble.","He had already seen the look in Lyra’s eyes when she noticed the necklace on Mira and knew and didn’t know what to think of it. He could only purchase two more similar necklaces for them.","And Selene.","She probably hadn’t noticed the necklace yet. But when she did...","He shook his head and chuckled silently. He had become one of those people scared of their wives. And not only did he have just one. He has three of them.","Forty-five seconds later.","\"Ding.\"","The elevator stopped and the doors slid open.","The six of them stepped outside. Instantly, Dexter’s eyes narrowed slightly as he saw two people staring outside the elevator.","They were guards and their energy wave was extraordinary. They were both","Superhuman Realm heroes!","Dexter couldn’t help wondering exactly how many Superhuman experts existed inside Stargate City.","Because ever since arriving at the Hero Association, they seemed to be everywhere. Guards, receptionists, instructors and even the Maintenance workers.","The instructor stepped forward and showed his identification.","The two guards nodded immediately.","One of them pressed his hand against a scanner. A blue light swept across his palm, reading mana signatures and comparing them against stored data.","The other pressed a massive red button mounted beside the wall.","Rumble.","A gigantic metallic gate, nearly three meters tall, slowly split apart from the middle. The thick steel doors ground open with a heavy mechanical groan.","Behind the gate was a portal floated in midair, a glowing violet portal swirling like a whirlpool made of light.","Dexter’s eyes widened, for this was his first time seeing one. And he was not the only one stunned.","The lady with the dagger stared with sharp interest, her lips parting slightly, her natural curiosity pushing aside her attempt to look professional. The muscular man raised his eyebrows a tiny bit, even the quiet girl could not hide her curiosity,","Only the tall young man and the instructor appeared unaffected.","Clearly, they had seen portals before.","The portal resembled a gigantic glowing amoeba suspended in space, its surface constantly rippling like water touched by a gentle breeze.","Colors shifted endlessly within it: purple, blue, black, silver, all swirling and blending. It looked as though an entire universe had been compressed into a single doorway, stars and darkness and light dancing together in an endless, silent song.","Beautiful and terrifying, the sight was strangely mesmerizing and very hypnotic.","It made Dexter want to reach out and touch it to feel what the portal felt like against his fingertips.","The instructor suddenly spoke \"This is a modified F-Rank Dungeon. We have changed parts of it for this licensing examination to match your strength.\" He turned toward the group. \"You will enter as a team. You may cooperate if you wish, or you may act independently. That decision is yours alone.\"","The instructor reached into a metal case and removed several black wristbands. One by one, he handed them out. The moment Dexter put his on, the band automatically adjusted itself around his wrist. A soft beep confirmed activation, and a tiny light on its surface blinked green once before going dark.","\"This is your emergency extraction device. If you wish to leave the dungeon, press the button on the side, and you will immediately be pulled out.\" His expression became serious, his eyes hard. \"However, if you voluntarily withdraw from today’s examination, you will need to wait three months before applying for another Hero License examination.\"","The candidates’ expressions shifted slightly. Three months was a long time.","The instructor nodded. \"Do not throw away your life for pride, but do not surrender too easily either.\" He stepped aside. \"Good luck. Now enter the dungeon.\"","The candidates looked at one another, nobody moving right away.","Everyone seemed to be waiting for someone else to take the first step.","Just as Dexter was considering entering, Marcus suddenly snorted.","\"Cowards.\"","A confident smirk appeared on his face and without hesitation, he stepped forward.","The moment his body touched the portal, he suddenly disappeared like he had never been there at all.","Fiona clicked her tongue.","\"Show off.\"","She stepped forward next, her figure melting into the violet light.","The muscular giant entered third, walking forward with heavy steps and vanishing without a sound.","The quiet girl followed shortly after, her small form swallowed by the portal.","Only Dexter remained.","He stared at the swirling portal for a few seconds. This was his first dungeon and also his first step into the world of heroes.","Taking a deep breath, Dexter stepped forward. The moment his body touched the violet light, his vision exploded into countless colors, and the world around him disappeared completely."]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74 | Fight! First Wave","paragraphs":["The moment the five candidates stepped through the portal, the world around them changed.","The sensation was indescribable.","Dexter felt as though his body had been torn apart into countless tiny fragments before being stitched back together again.","It wasn’t painful like Dexter had thought, but it was deeply unsettling. For a brief moment, it felt as though something foreign was probing his body, his mind, and even his soul.","Then as the feeling appeared, it vanished.","Just like that.","His feet touched solid ground.","\"Blurgh!\"","Before Dexter could properly regain his balance, his stomach twisted violently. He turned aside and vomited onto the grass. Some of the legendary food he had eaten, wasted just like that. Luckily there essence had been absorbed.","Not far away, the quiet swordswoman, Lena Park, was experiencing exactly the same thing.","Dexter wiped his mouth with the back of his hand. His face slightly flushed and his stomach was still churning but it was bearable.","Lena looked even worse. Her face was completely white. She gripped her sword with one hand while holding her stomach with the other. Her lips were pressed tightly together as though she was fighting a second wave.","Marcus burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! Seriously? You two are vomiting from portal sickness?\"","He shook his head with obvious contempt.","\"Pathetic.\"","Fiona rolled her eyes.","\"Not everyone has the opportunity to enter a dungeon early like us, Marcus. Im pretty sure yours was words than this.\"","Gregor merely grunted and said nothing.","Dexter wiped his mouth and took a deep breath.","So this was dungeon transfer sickness.","He had read countless things about heroes and monsters, but somehow nobody had mentioned portal sickness.","’ Maybe it’s a running joke between heroes.’","He raised his head and finally looked around.","The dungeon had fully materialized around them.","The air was thick with so much mana it was denser, heavier, and strangely alive. Like breathing in air that had weight.","Each breath filled his lungs with energy that was more potent than anything back in earth.","The five of them stood in the center of a large clearing about 300 meters in radius.","But that clearing was surrounded by towering trees. Thetrees themselves had dense fog covering the forest in every direction.","Tall grass reached all the way to their waists, swaying gently beneath an invisible wind.","Above them hung a single silver moon.","Its pale light illuminated the clearing while leaving the surrounding forest hidden beneath darkness and mist.","Everyone’s expression became solemn.","Marcus immediately stepped forward.","\"I’ll take point.\"","His voice carried unquestionable confidence.","\"Gregor, take the rear.\"","\"Fiona, left flank.\"","\"Lena, right flank.\"","Marcus finally turned toward Dexter, his eyes landing on the F-Rank symbol displayed on Dexter’s temporary badge.","Open contempt flashed across his face. \"And you.\" He smirked.","\"Stay in the center.\"","His tone became colder.","\"And try not to get in our way.\"","The others moved into formation almost immediately. Fiona looked as if she wanted to say something, her mouth opening, then closing.","She glanced at Dexter with an apologetic expression before moving to her position.","Lena frowned slightly, not agreeing with Marcus’s attitude, but she was too quiet to object.","Neither of them spoke up.","Dexter simply stood in the center of the formation.","He was not surprised.","Marcus was a Tier 3 Superhuman, Gregor was Tier 2, Fiona and Lena were Tier One.","Meanwhile, his displayed rank was merely F-Rank.","From Marcus’s perspective, placing the weakest member in the safest position was the logical choice, actually good leadership: protect the weakest link, maximize the team’s effectiveness, play to everyone’s strengths.","’ Fine by me.’","The less attention he drew, the better.","The dungeon wasted no time. A long howl suddenly echoed through the fog-covered forest.","\"Awooooo!\"","A second howl answered it. \"Awooooo!\"","Then a third. The sounds surrounded them from every direction, not from one point but from everywhere.","The pack was already circling, already hunting, already deciding who would be the first to fall.","Everyone immediately tensed up as rustling sounds came from the tall grass.","Then.","Figures burst from the fog, they were Grey Wolves and 12 of them.","Each stood nearly as tall as a horse and possessed glowing yellow eyes filled with hunger and pure rage.","Their brown fur blended almost perfectly with the darkness. If not for their glowing eyes, they might have been invisible.","[Monster Classification: Mutated Class (1 - 12), Fiend Class (1 - 12), Transcendent Class (1-12), Abomination Class (1 to 4 stars), Calamity Class (1 to 4 stars) and Ender Class (1 to 4 stars) ]","[Hero Classification: Awakened Hero also called Meta Heroes (1 to 12), Super Hero (1 to 12), Ultra Hero (1 to 12), Transcendent (Initial, Mid, Advance, Peak), Supreme (Initial, Mid, Advance, Peak), and Legend.]","Marcus narrowed his eyes. \"Fiend Class, Level 1 Grey Wolves.\"","\"Graaah!\"","The creatures spread out, slowly circling the group as they growled, revealing fangs as spit drooled down their faces.","The wolves continued circling them, strangely waiting and watching.","Suddenly, a louder and sharper howl echoed from deeper within the forest.","\"AWOOOOO!\"","\"Awoo!\" \"Awoo!\" \"Awoo!\"","Instantly, the entire pack attacked, the wolves exploding forward from all directions.","Marcus face hardened as he roared.","\"Kill them!\"","The first wolf bristled towards him and Marcus smirked as he clenched his hand.","Immediately, his talent erupted and blue flames exploded in his fist as he struck first at the first Wolf.","\"BOOM!\"","His fist smashed directly into the skull of the leading wolf, the creature’s head exploding instantly as its body crashed lifelessly into the grass.","Without pausing, Marcus drew his sword, silver flash arced through the air.","\"Slash!\"","Another wolf collapsed. \"Slash!\" Then another.","At the same time, Fiona moved like flowing water. Her twin daggers danced through the battlefield.","One wolf lunged toward her throat.","Clang!","She redirected its claws with one dagger while the second blade sliced cleanly across its neck.","Blood sprayed into the air.","Before the body even hit the ground, she had already spun toward another target.","Slash!","A second wolf fell. In the blink of an eye, four out of twelve grey wolves were dead."]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75 | Second Wave","paragraphs":["Gregor was even more brutal.","One wolf jumped toward him. Instead of dodging, he caught the beast by the throat with one massive hand.","\"Rawoooo!\"","The wolf struggled violently. Its claws raked against his arm causing blood to appeared but Gregor did not flinch.","Instead, he locked the beast neck into a vice grip and slowlydrove his sword through the creature’s neck.","\"Crunch.\"","The wolf whimpered in pain and its body shook violently before itwent limp.","Thw next second, his dropped the dead beast, twisted his waist as he slammed into another wolf’s skull with force.","\"Squelch!\"","The skull cracked as the beast died instantly.","Lena was the least experienced fighter among them.","The first wolf nearly caught her off guard. She blocked awkwardly, the impact almost knocking her off balance.","Fear flashed in her eyes. But she gritted her teeth and stubbornly glared at the wolf.","Suddenly, she flashed forward and her sword flashed with speed.","The blade sliced across the wolf’s neck before it could realize what was happening, letting blood pour out as the creature stumbled several steps before collapsing.","Meanwhile, more wolves continued rushing towards them.","Marcus, Fiona and Gregor killed them with speed.","Lena slowly found her rhythm and she was able to kill another beast.","Five minutes later, silence returned to the clearing and 12 wolf corpses littered the grass.","Not a single monster remained alive. Blood soaked the ground and the metallic scent hung heavy in the air.","Dexter stood exactly where Marcus had ordered him to stay. He had not even drawn his sword and the wolves had never reached him.","Every monster that came close had been intercepted and killed by the others before he even had the opportunity to move.","\"AWOOO!\"","The alpha grey wolf was enraged as it charged at them. It’s claws immediately struck out with force.","Gregor’s eyes hardened and he immediately stepped forward with his sheld as he roared","\"Parry!\"","\"Ding!\"","The beast paused for a second, Fiona used the opportunity to charge at it and slashed at its ankles causing it too stumble.","Marcus grin widened and he leapt five meters upwards and descended like a meteor.","\"Slash!\"","The head of the beast was immediately severed into two.","Marcus looked around at the battlefield, breathing hard, and grinned proudly.","\"Too easy.\"","He wiped blood from his sword.","\"The first wave is complete.\"","He rolled his shoulders confidently. \"F-Rank licenses secured already.\"","Fiona wiped blood from one of her daggers before sliding it back into its sheath. \"Looks like the first wave really was just a formality.\"","She glanced toward the dark forest surrounding them. \"The second wave should be much stronger.\"","Gregor silently picked up his shield and tightened the strap around his forearm. Lena carefully cleaned the blood from her sword with a piece of cloth. Her hands trembled slightly from leftover adrenaline.","The first wave had barely lasted five minutes. 13 wolves. 13 corpses. Not a single injury among them.","Marcus glanced back at Dexter and smirked. \"Congratulations, F-Rank. You officially contributed absolutely nothing and still earned your Hero License.\"","Fiona frowned. \"Marcus.\"","He shrugged. \"What? The wolves didn’t even get close to him. He spent the entire fight standing there looking pretty.\"","He paused before adding with a grin, \"Actually, scratch that. Standing there looking ugly.\"","Fiona rolled her eyes. Marcus ignored her. \"The least you can do is harvest the Nexus Cores. Otherwise you’ll be completely useless in here.\"","Dexter looked at the corpses around him and smiled inwardly.","Perfect .","That gave him the perfect excuse. He crouched beside the first corpse and placed his hand against it and curated the Extraction System.","[Extraction Successful.]","+3 Strength","+5 Agility","+2 Mana","+1 Physique","Dexter’s eyes widened slightly with excitement. He quickly moved to the second corpse, then the third, then fourth, fifth. One after another.","[Extraction Successful.]","+2 Strength","+4 Agility","+1 Mana","[Extraction Successful.]","+4 Strength","+3 Physique","+2 Mana","The notifications continued appearing inside his mind. By the time he reached the final wolf, a warm, tingling current surged through his entire body.","His muscles became denser. His bones felt heavier, sturdier. His mana circulation smoothed our and his body had become noticeably stronger.","According to the system, he was still a Tier 3 Superhuman.","However, his physical attributes had risen tremendously. If his previous strength represented an average Tier 3 Superhuman, then his current physical power was already approaching Tier 6 to 7.","Dexter suppressed the excitement in his eyes. This was the main reason why he wanted to enter the dungeon. Because if the extraction system.","The value of dungeons to him was simply absurd.","In his hand rested twelve glowing Nexus Cores.","Looking at the perfectly nearly aplit head of the wolves without bashing the skull in, Marcus sneered. \"Looks like you’ve found your calling. You’d make a pretty decent porter.\"","He crossed his arms. \"Honestly, your next dungeon run should probably be as support staff.\" He laughed. \"Carrying luggage suits you perfectly.\"","\"Marcus!\"","Fiona glared at him and the turned to Dexter. \"Don’t take it personally. He’s always a jerk.\"","Dexter merely smiled. \"I wasn’t planning on taking it personally.\"","Marcus snorted.","\"Ding!\"","They watch suddenly rang out as an holographic screen appeared above each device.","[Wave One Cleared.]","[Preparing Wave Two.]","[Preparation Time Remaining: 60 Seconds.]","Instantly, the atmosphere changed and the casual confidence disappeared from everyone’s expressions.","Gregor frowned deeply. \"The mana density increased.\"","Dexter had already noticed.","In fact, he had been the first to notice with his SS-Rank Mana Affinity, which allowed him to sense changes in mana far earlier than ordinary heroes.","The mana floating through the forest was becoming increasingly violent. Even the fog itself began twisting into slow swirls.","Then, a growl echoed through the darkness.","\"Grrrrrr.\"","Another followed.","\"Grrrrrr.\"","Suddenly, pairs of glowing eyes appeared throughout the forest.","Ten pairs, twenty pairs, thirty pairs and the darkness itself seemed alive.","Lena tightened her grip on her sword. \"There are more than before.\"","Fiona’s expression darkened. \"A lot more.\" Marcus slowly nodded. \"Formation.\"","Immediately, everyone moved.","Marcus took the front. Gregor guarded the rear. Fiona moved to the left flank. Lena took the right.","As for Dexter, he remained in the center.","Marcus glanced back toward him and smirked. \"Same as before. Stay in the middle and don’t become a burden.\" Dexter did not reply. He had no interest in arguing."]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76 | Joining The Battle","paragraphs":["The countdown on their wristbands ticked downward.","3.","2.","1.","0.","\"BOOM!\"","Immediately, the forest exploded into motion as tall grasses bent violently as monsters burst from every direction, the fog rippling as dark shadows raced through it.","This time, they were not ordinary wolves.","These monsters were nearly twice the size of the previous wave, their fur darker, their bodies leaner and more muscular.","Crimson eyes glowed beneath the moonlight while strange markings covered their bodies like natural tattoos, their claws long enough to rival daggers.","Even Fiona’s expression changed.","\"Direwolves.\" Marcus licked his lips as he spoke.","\"Level two this time.\"","There were not merely two or three of them, they were about fifteen.","Then suddenly, another figure stepped out from the forest, and everyone froze.","Unlike the others, this beast stood nearly three meters long, its fur darker than the night itself and seeming to shimmer beneath the moonlight.","Ther was a scar in across its left eyes, while its remaining eye radiating cold intelligence, and the pressure it emitted was on an entirely different level. Gregor’s expression darkened.","\"Alpha Direwolf.\" Marcus cursed immediately. \"Damn it.\"","The Alpha slowly raised its head toward the moon.","\"ROOOOOAR!!\"","The entire forest trembled.","The fifteen Direwolves moved simultaneously, like soldiers responding to their king’s command, and they charged.","Marcus struck first.","\"BOOM!\"","His gauntleted fist collided with the claws of the nearest wolf, a shockwave erupting outward as the beast was blasted backward through the grass.","Before it even landed, another wolf lunged toward his throat.","Marcus grinned, his sword flashing. \"Slash!\"","Blood sprayed into the air as the wolf’s head separated from its body.","\"Ocean Flame Erupt!\"","\"Whoosh!\"","Blue flames ignited across his blade, as he activated hus Ocean Flame Talent.","The flames wrapped around his sword and intensified its cutting power tremendously.","Another Direwof leapt at him as it struck its cake at Marcus head.","\"Whoosh!\"","Marcus slashed backwards at the claw and the Ocean flames burned through the claw as the sword easily sliced through the wolf’s body, letting blood spray in the air as it fell tk the ground.","At this moment, Marcus had become even powerful with such a talent.","Fiona pupils dilated as she also didn’t hesitate and activated her talent.","\"Time Dilation!\"","\"Whoosh!\"","Everything around her slowed down in her eyes as she processed information at astonishing speed and her body also responded at that same speed.","The wolves becoming sluggish and predictable. Her daggers transformed into silver streaks dancing across the battlefield. As she cut through them rapidly.","Blood erupted everywhere. Fiona moved like flowing water through the battlefield, elegant, precise, and lethal.","Gregor was an entirely different monster. The massive young man roared as muscles bulged beneath his armor, his talent activating.","\"Super Strength.\"","His already terrifying strength increased by over fifty percent.","A charging Direwolf met his shield head-on.","\"BOOM!!\" The impact shattered the beast’s ribs instantly, and before it could recover, his sword pierced through its neck.","Another wolf lunged toward him, and Gregor simply swatted it away with his shield, causing the wolf to fly several meters before crashing lifelessly into a boulder with a sickening thud.","Lena struggled the most. Her movements lacked experience, and one Direwolf nearly tore open her shoulder. She barely managed to roll away as claws tore through the ground where she had stood moments earlier.","But despite her inexperience, her fundamentals were excellent. She recovered instantly, her sword piercing into the side of the beast’s neck.","\"Shink!\"","Blood splattered across the grass, and the wolf collapsed.","Meanwhile, Dexter remained standing at the center of the battlefield, watching.","Marcus possessed overwhelming offensive power, Gregor possessed monstrous physical strength, Fiona was incredibly fast and deadly, and Lena lacked experience but had remarkable foundations.","For an ordinary F-Rank team, they were exceptional.","Then, his expression changed. His Danger Sense exploded, every instinct in his body screaming a warning.","Without hesitation, Dexter stepped backward.","\"WHOOSH!\"","A massive shadow tore through the air where he had been standing a fraction of a second earlier.","\"BOOM!!\"","The ground exploded, dirt and shattered stone flying everywhere.","Every face in the clearing shifted instantly.","Standing within the crater was another wolf.","No, calling it a wolf felt wrong.","This creature stood nearly three meters tall at the shoulder, jet-black fur covering its body, its claws shining silver beneath the moonlight.","Golden eyes stared coldly at the battlefield, and the pressure pouring from its body alone made Lena’s face turn pale.","Marcus’s confident expression disappeared instantly. \"A Level three Fiend monster.\"","Silence filled the clearing. The wolf slowly rose to its feet, ignoring Marcus, Fiona, Gregor, and Lena.","Its golden eyes locked directly onto Dexter.","The monster’s lips slowly curled upward, revealing rows of razor-sharp teeth.","\"Grrrrrr.\"","A low rumble escaped its throat. For some reason, out of everyone present, it had chosen him. Dexter’s eyes narrowed. \"Interesting.\"","The Third-Star Dire Wolf lowered its body, muscles tightening beneath its dark fur.","Then it vanished.","\"BOOM!\"","The ground exploded beneath its feet as the beast transformed into a black blur racing toward Dexter at terrifying speed.","Itwas far faster than any of the previous wolves.","Fiona’s expression changed. \"Watch out!\" But","Dexter had already moved. His hand reached over his shoulder and drew the weapon wrapped in cloth, a beautiful black sword appearing in his hand.","\"CLANG!\"","Sparks erupted as the Dire Wolf’s claw smashed against Dexter’s blade, creating a shockwave that swept through the clearing and bent the surrounding grass flat against the ground.","Everyone froze in shock. Marcus’s eyes widened, Fiona stopped moving, Gregor stared in disbelief, and even Lena looked shocked.","Dexter had blocked the attack effortlessly, not even taking a single step backward, only the earth beneath his feet shattering under the impact.","They quickly continued their battle but were keeping an eye on Dexter.","The Dire Wolf flipped in mid air and landed several meters away then slowly began circling him.","Its instincts were knew there was something not right about Dexter.","Dexter glanced down at his sword before looking back at the beast, a smile slowly spreading across his face. \"So you’re stronger than the others.\"","His eyes drifted toward the Alpha Wolf standing silently atop the distant boulder. \"If this thing is this strong, then how strong is the Alpha?\""]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77 | Alpha Wolf!","paragraphs":["Around them, the battle continued. One wolf fell, then another.","Their talents allowed them to hold the line, but the battle was becoming a slow grind. Blood. Sweat. Heavy breathing. The kind of fighting that wore you down inch by inch.","Meanwhile, Dexter’s attention remained fixed entirely on the Third-Star beast before him.","The wolf moved first. Its body blurred. A black afterimage remained where it had been standing.","\"Skill: Phantom Moonstep.\"","A movement skill possessed by elite Dire Wolves. By flooding their limbs with mana, they momentarily merge with their own shadow, allowing them to move with explosive bursts of speed that create afterimages and distort an opponent’s perception.","To weaker opponents, it appears as if the wolf has teleported.","The Dire Wolf reappeared behind Dexter. Its jaws opened wide as it lunged toward his neck.","\"CLANG!\"","Dexter casually swung his blade backwards and intercepted the bite.","The beast twisted in midair, performing an impossible flip before landing lightly on the ground several meters away.","Before it could move again, Dexter vanished.","The wolf’s instincts screamed. It barely turned its head before Dexter appeared beside it.","His blade shot toward its throat.","The wolf immediately activated Phantom Moonstep once more. Its body dissolved into a blur and reappeared behind Dexter. Its claws flashed toward the back of his head.","\"Swish!\"","But instead of flesh, it actually hit nothing. The wolf’s eyes widened as it realized it was an afterimage and Dexter had disappeared.","The beast looked around but couldn’t find Dexter.","It’s eyes widened in panic but suddenly it felt a heat sensation above.","Three meters above it, Dexter seem to hovered in mid air with his sword raised, he activated his bloodline talent.","\"Flame Slash.\"","The black blade erupted with crimson fire as Dexter slashed downwards.","A two-meter crescent of blazing energy descended toward the wolf with overwhelming speed.","\"Rooooar!\"","The Dire Wolf roared and swung its claws toward the attack.","The flames sliced through its claws as though they were paper, then continued onward.","\"SHING!\"","The beast split cleanly into two halves. Its body crashed heavily onto the ground.","\"THUD.\"","Silence fell across the battlefield. Marcus stared. Fiona blinked. Gregor’s mouth slowly opened. Lena simply looked at Dexter as though seeing him for the first time.","The Tier 3 Dire Wolf had died in less than a minute.","Killed by the supposed F-Rank burden.","Meanwhile the others were still struggling against the remaining beasts.","The battle resumed and the beast fell one after the other until only the Alpha remained. The massive beast stood silently atop the boulder overlooking the battlefield.","Its crimson eyes watched them with intelligence that no ordinary monster should possess.","Even as its entire pack died around it, it never moved and It simply watched.","Then slowly, the Alpha raised its head toward the moon.","\"ROOOOOOAR!!\"","The entire forest trembled and the fog rolled violently. The mana in the air suddenly became heavier.","Everyone felt it as the pressure increased.","Their eyes narrowed on the alpha.","\"Everyone, be vigilant.\" Marcus suddenly spoke as he locked his gaze in the alpha. Bht he didn’t say anything to Dexter this time.","\"Whoosh!\"","The Alpha suddenly vanished.. It was as though a drawing wiped clean from a canvas.","Marcus’s face changed instantly. \"Where did it go?!\"","Gregor reacted first as he activated his skill.","\"Guardian’s Will!\"","He slammed his shield into the ground. Golden light erupted outward, forming a protective barrier around the group.","Less than a quarter of a second later, a massive shadow appeared before them and a gigantic claw descended beside Marcus.","\"BOOOOOOM!!\"","The impact shook the entire clearing. The barrier trembled violently as cracks spread across its surface.","\"CRACK!\"","The shield shattered.","But those precious fractions of a second had been enough.","Everyone immediately flew off with speed.","Marcus leapt backward.","Fiona disappeared in a silver blur. Lena rolled to safety. Gregor threw himself aside. Dust exploded into the air.","The Alpha stood where the barrier had once been. Moonlight reflected off its dark fur. Its body was nearly four meters long.","Silver claws extended from its paws. Its single remaining eye glowed with fierce intelligence.","The scar crossing the other eye somehow made it look even more terrifying. The pressure pouring from it dwarfed every monster they had faced so far.","Marcus swallowed.","\"It’s actually a level 5 beast.\"","Fiona’s face paled. \"That’s impossible. Shouldn’t it be level 3?\"","Gregor tightened his grip on his shield. Lena unconsciously stepped backward.","The Alpha slowly looked across the battlefield, Then its gaze settled on Dexter.","The beast’s lips curled upward into what almost looked like a smile.","Dexter narrowed his eyes. The Alpha had chosen its prey. And strangely enough, Dexter felt the exact same way.","The Alpha Dire Wolf slowly lowered its body. Its single golden eye remained fixed on Dexter. Marcus tightened his grip on his sword.","\"Everyone spread out! Don’t let it trap us together!\"","The Alpha’s muscles suddenly tensed. Then, it disappeared.","\"Left!\"","Dexter shouted.","The Alpha appeared beside Fiona,","Fiona activated time dilation as she immediately reacted with break neck speed.","\"BOOM!\"","its massive claws crashed heavily into the ground where she had been standing only a moment earlier.","The impact sent dirt and grass flying in every direction. Fiona’s face paled. \"That speed is ridiculous!\"","Marcus immediately charged forward. Blue flames erupted around his sword. \"Blue Flame Slash!\"","His blade cut toward the Alpha’s neck. The beast twisted unnaturally in midair and vanished once more.","Phantom Moonstep.","Marcus’s attack sliced through empty air.","\"Behind you.\"","Dexter’s voice came out again and the Alpha reappeared behind him. Its claws descended.","\"CLANG!\"","Marcus barely turn his body and managed to block.","Even then, he was sent skidding backwards through the grass. His arms trembled violently. \"What kind of monster strength is this?\"","The Alpha did not stop. It lunged toward Lena next.","Lena’s eyes widened. She raised her sword but she was too slow.","\"BOOM!\"","Gregor slammed his shield into the Alpha’s side.","The massive wolf was knocked several meters away.","Gregor planted himself in front of Lena. \"I’ve got you.\"","The Alpha slowly stood. Its gaze swept over the battlefield.","Then it raised its head.","\"ROOOOOOOAR!\"","A wave of mana exploded outward. Everyone felt their bodies become heavier. Their movements slowed slightly. Even breathing felt more difficult. The alpha had activated its crowd control skill.","\"Lunar Predator Aura,\""]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78 | Sabotage!","paragraphs":["The Alpha moved again. This time the target was Gregor. Its body blurred as its claw struck downward. Gregor gritted his teeth and resied his shield.","\"BOOM!\"","The impact drove him to one knee. Cracks spread across the surface of his shield. A second strike followed immediately.","\"CRACK!\"","The shield shattered and Gregor’s expression changed.","The Alpha opened its jaws to chomp on his head when, silver flashed.","Fiona appeared beside the beast as she activated her Dilation. Everything around her slowed as her daggers struck the Alpha’s shoulder three times in rapid succession.","\"Clang. Clang. Clang.\"","Her face changed as she realized her dagger only death superficial wounds on its boys.","\"Rooar!\"","The Alpha swung its tail and Fiona was sent flying backwards. She rolled across the ground before stopping herself.","\"It has defensive enhancement too?!\" Marcus clenched his teeth. \"This thing is ridiculous.\"","The Alpha ignored everyone. Its gaze returned to Dexter. Dexter sighed. \"I was hoping to stay low profile.\"","The Alpha disappeared. Danger Sense exploded inside Dexter’s mind.","Without hesitation, he moved.","\"BOOM!\"","A claw struck where he had been standing. The earth collapsed inward.","The Alpha appeared beside him. Its claws flashed mutiple times.","Dexter raised his sword.","\"CLANG! CLANG! CLANG!\"","Shockwaves rippled through the clearing as the others stared with stunned expression.","Marcus could hardly believe his eyes. The Alpha was actually being pushed back. The supposedly useless F-Rank was matching the boss monster head-on.","The Alpha suddenly leapt backwards. Its fur suddenly began glowing crimson.","The mana in the surroundings rushed toward it.","Gregor’s face darkened. \"It’s powering up!\"","The beast raised its head toward the moon.","\"ROOOOOOOOOAR!\"","Crimson energy erupted around its body. Its muscles expanded. Its claws grew longer and it eye became blood red. Blood Moon Frenzy. Marcus cursed. \"It can still get stronger?!\"","The Alpha vanished.","This time even Dexter almost lost sight of it. Almost.","The wolf appeared above him. Its claws descended like falling blades. Dexter raised his sword.","\"BOOM!\"","The ground beneath him exploded. Cracks spread across the clearing. For the first time, Dexter took a step backwards. The Alpha landed gracefully. Its lips curled upward. It was enjoying this.","Dexter smiled. \"So you wanted a real fight.\"","His grip tightened around his sword. Flames slowly began spreading along the black blade.","The surrounding temperature started rising. Marcus stared. \"Fire attribute?\" Fiona frowned. \"No. That’s not ordinary fire.\"","The Alpha sensed danger. Its instincts howled.","As it hesitated. For the first time since the battle started, the predator felt fear.","Dexter lowered his stance. The mana around him gathered toward him as Crimson flames condensed on his blade.","The Alpha lunged forward, activating Phantom Moonstep in the blink of an eye.","Three afterimages suddenly appeared around it as Flfour wolves charged simultaneously at Dexter.","Dexter smirked as he casually slashed out horizontally casually.","\"Crimson Flame Arc.\"","The flames expanded into a massive crimson crescent over ten meters wide.","\"FWOOOSH!\"","The afterimages were slashed into two and they vanished instantly. The real Alpha tried to dodge it it was too late.","The attack crossed the clearing entering deep into the forest and severing mutiole trees behind before it dissipated and turned into more mana.","Suddenly silence followed. The Alpha landed several meters away took two steps forward and then stopped.","A thin line appeared across its chest. The line expanded and with two separated thuds, the beats at body collapsed to the ground.","\"THUD.\"","The dungeon immediately became silent. For several seconds nobody spoke.","Marcus stared blankly, basically everyone had the same expression in their faces. The one they had looked down on was actually the one who killed the Tier 4 beast?","Finally Marcus was able to open his mouth and he spoke. \"You’re no F-Rank. You been deceiving all of us, hiding your true strength.\"","Dexter glances indifferently at Marcus who immediately choked up.","He ignored him and simply went to the corpse of the Alpha Dire Wolf then used extraction on the beast.","[Phantom Moon Step (Rare Grade Skill) Extracted]","[+10 Agility]","Suddenly, the silence was broken by a mechanical voice.","[Wave Two Cleared.]","[Wave Three Beginning In 20 Seconds.]","Everyone froze. Marcus frowned. \"Another wave so soon.\"","Fiona frowned as well.","Gregor’s expression darkened. \"And if the second wave already had a Tier-4 Alpha.\"","Nobody finished the sentence. Because they all knew the answer. If the second wave had a Tier-4 alpha then the third wave would be much much more terrifying.","Marcus immediately raised his wrist. \"We leave.\"","He looked at everyone and they all nodded their heads. Nobody objected. The objective had already been completed.","They had earned their licenses.","There was absolutely no reason to continue. \"Alright. Then let’s all press the extraction button and leave.\"","Marcus pressed the extraction button. Nothing happened. He frowned and pressed again. Still nothing.","Fiona tried hers however, it was also nothing.","Gregor’s expression slowly changed as he clicked his own and it failed. Lena pressed hers repeatedly. Still nothing.","Dexter looked down at his wrist and pressed his own. Silence.","Marcus slowly lowered his arm. \"That’s not funny.\"","Fiona’s face turned pale. \"Is this supposed to happen?\"","Gregor looked around the clearing. \"Not all five at once.\"","Silence. An ugly answer slowly formed in their minds. Sabotage.","Someone had trapped them inside. Lena spoke for the first time in several minutes.","\"We’re trapped.\" Nobody corrected her. Because she was right.","A deep rumble echoed throughout the forest.","The ground shook and the fog surrounding the clearing suddenly thickened.","The moon overhead slowly shifted color as the white became crimson.","Then came the footsteps.","\"Boom. Boom. Boom.\"","The trees at the edge of the forest trembled.","[Wave Three Initiating.]","The mechanical voice vanished. The world became quiet. Then, the forest exploded.","\"CRASH!!\"","Trees snapped apart and a gigantic creature burst into the clearing.","It was four meters tall and its body was covered in dark armored scales.","Its claws alone were larger than swords and its crimson eyes scanned the battlefield.","Marcus’s face changed. \"Tier 4 Armored Bear.\"","Before anyone could react, another Armored bear emerged, then another, then another until they were 30 Armored Bear surrounding the clearing.","\"30 freaking Armoured Bear? How are we supposed to survive?\"","Everyone’s face paled."]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79 | Get Them Out!","paragraphs":["The observation room sat twelve floors above the dungeon floor, enclosed behind reinforced walls and lined with state of the art monitoring equipment.","Ten meter wide rows of screens displayed feeds from various examinations ongoing in different dungeons.","Rachel sat near the back, her eyes fixed on a particular screen. She had bribed her way into this room specifically for this.","Her friend, a frazzled blonde girl with a security clearance smuggled her in for a favour.","She wanted to watch Dexter battle. That was all. She simply wanted to see that man fight with her own eyes.","On the screen, the first wave of beasts poured into the clearing.","Dexter stood among his team, but he didn’t attack and the team seem to be protecting him instead.","Rachel tilted her head, watching and pondering why he was at the middle and the it seemed like the team was protecting him instead.","The other participants engaged the creatures, but Dexter simply observed.","\"I have no idea why you came here to watch that weakling. You can teased the favour for something else.\" Her friend whispered to her.","\"Just keep on watching.\"","She knew better than to think he was helpless from the beginning she knew there was singing different about him.","The first wave ended and the beasts were easily dealt with by the others.","Rachel smiled as the second wave came.","They were the Dire wolves this time, circling the participants with coordinated precision.","It was then she saw Dexter finally move killing both the beta Dire Wolf and the Alpha Dire wolf easily!","Rachel leaned forward in her seat, her grin spreading wide across her face.","\"I knew it! I knew he was stronger than he let on.\"","The blonde girl beside her shot a sharp look and pressed a finger to her lips. \"Shh. Keep your voice down. If teh boss knows I snuck you in here, we are done for.\"","Rachel covered her mouth with one hand and nodded, but the smile did not leave her face.","At the front of the room, the Head Supervisor stood with his arms folded, his gaze locked on the screens.","He was a broad man with a square jaw and a strict behavior.","Around him, several other invigilators monitored their assigned stations, though more than a few of them kept glancing at the same screen Rachel was watching.","They recognized the Ashford bastard and in just a few minutes, there was a quiet wager circulating through the room.","People had placed bets on which wave Dexter’s group would fail. First wave, second wave, third wave, or fourth. A few optimists had even bet on seventh wave.","When Dexter and the others decided to exit the dungeon, the workers who had bet on the first two waves collected their earnings with satisfaction. One man near the left terminal actually chuckled as he pocketed his winnings.","Suddenly. They saw from the feed that the extraction device wasn’t working","The mood immediately shifted.","An invigilator near the center console frowned and tapped his earpiece. \"Extraction watch is not responding.\"","A murmur rippled through the room. The Head Supervisor turned sharply. \"What do you mean, not responding?\"","\"The extraction watches on the participants, sir. They are not activating.\"","The Supervisor frowned. \"Then activate a remote extraction.\"","The worker immediately got to work but a red alert filled his screen.","\"Sir! The system is not acknowledging the command.\"","The man who had just collected his winnings slowly closed his hand around the money in his pocket. His smile disappeared.","The Supervisor stepped forward, his face hardening as he growled at the workers. \"Fix it. Immediately.\"","Immediately, tens of workers fired at their keyboards.","Three different operators began running diagnostics simultaneously, their faces illuminated by the pale blue glow of their screens.","The room had somehow gone quiet. The only sounds were the tapping of keys.","Thirty seconds passed. Then one of the operators raised his hand without looking away from his monitor. \"Sir, it has been sabotaged internally. This is not a system error. The extraction protocol has been deliberately tampered with from inside the watch units themselves.\"","The silence that followed was intense.","Rachel’s smile vanished. She turned to her friend. \"What the fuck does that mean?\"","\"Calm down,\" the blonde girl said, though her own fingers had already started moving across her keyboard. \"Let me work.\"","Before anyone could process the implications of the first alert, a second one fired. A sharp, shrill tone cut through the room, and every screen flashed red with a cascading warning message.","[Dungeon 1435: WAVE 3 TRIAL UPGRADED TO WAVE 5 TRIAL.","Every operator in the room went still. The Head Supervisor’s face drained of color. If they could barely handle wave 3 just what would happen in wave 7?","\"Sir,\" another operator said, his voice tight, \"the watch protection bubble has also been destroyed. The participants have no defensive barrier active.\"","The Head Supervisor’s face finally paled.","\"Bang!\"","\"Fix it immediately. We cannot allow this to continue. The others, fine, but if an Ashford dies in this facility, there will be consequences that none of us can survive. Do you understand me? Even the director will not be able to protect us from what the Ashford family would do. Fix this now.\"","He straightened up and pointed toward the elevator. \"Open the gate manually. Send a team down to extract them physically.\"","Three guards and two technicians immediately moved for the elevator.","Rachel was on her feet before she fully realized she was moving, and she slipped into the elevator just before the doors closed. Nobody stopped her as no one was paying attention to her.","They descended fifteen floors and came down.","At the far end was the heavy arc door, the entrance to the dungeon zone. The lead guard placed his palm on the access panel.","Nothing happened. He tried again. The panel flickered but the door remained sealed.","\"Override it,\" one of the technicians said.","The guard entered a manual code. The panel flashed red. He tried a second code. Red again. He tried a third.","Still nothing.","\"Back to the observation room,\" the lead guard said through gritted teeth. \"Now.\"","When they returned and delivered the news, the Head Supervisor looked as though he might strangle someone.","\"Do you understand what happens if Dexter Ashford dies in there?\" he growled with gritted teeth.","\"The others are expendable. He is not. Find a way to override the system and get a team inside that dungeon. I do not care what you have to do. Hack it, break it, tear it apart if you must. Get them the fuck out.\""]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80 | Leaving The Dungeon","paragraphs":["Every operator in the room attacked their keyboards like warriors battling in ancient times.","Minutes crawled past like hours as they tried to figure out a solution.","Rachel stood near the back, her hands clenched at her sides, her face flushed red.","She could not hear what the operators were saying anymore as she focused on Dexter who wasthe screen. There were about 30 Armored Bears that had rushed towards them!","Still, Dexter hadn’t move at this point but his teammates were getting injured.","\"BEEP! BEEP! BEEP!\"","The screen displaying Dexter’s dungeon suddenly went black!","The Head Supervisor face turned extremely dark and he slammed both hands onto the nearest desk.","\"What is happening? Is there someone in this building actively sabotaging us? Find them. Find whoever is doing this. We need a scapegoat if this goes wrong. If an Ashford dies here, someone will answer for it. Find a name.\"","The room descended into controlled chaos.","Operators shouted over one another. Security personnel made calls. The blonde girl beside Rachel was typing so fast her fingers were a blur.","Ten minutes passed.","Ten minutes of black screen and rising panic and the suffocating weight of a family name that could end careers and lives with equal indifference.","Then a voice sharply cut through the noise.","\"Sir. I fixed it.\"","The Head Supervisor spun toward the speaker, a young man at the far right terminal who was staring at his screen with wide, disbelieving eyes. \"Activate instant teleportation immediately.\"","The young man hesitated. His fingers hovered over his keyboard. \"Sir, I was not able to restore the instant teleportation function. The sabotage there is too thorough. But I was able to find a weakness in the arc seal on the physical door. I exploited it and forced the arc open. That is the only thing I could do.\"","The Head Supervisor roared.","\"Call the medics to follow me!\"","He walked past everyone and headed straight into the elevator. Rachel followed and Two guards Pek Superhumans followed her. They descended in silence.","The lead guard placed his palm on the access panel.","The door opened with a puff sound.","The Head Supervisor did not wait for the guards to go first. He stepped through the arc and into the dimensional zone, and Rachel was right behind him.","They emerged into the clearing and they stopped dead in their tracks, stunned.","Dexter stood in the center of a wide, open space, his chest rising and falling ss he panted.","Blood covered him from head to toe, soaking his clothes, streaked his arms, and dripped from his fingertips onto the grass beneath his feet.","In his left hand, he held the head of a massive beast. The skull was thick, encased in plates of bone armor that gleamed dully in the pale light of the dimensional zone.","It was the head of the seventh tier armored bear. The boss beast. The alpha.","Around Dexter, spread across the clearing in every direction, were the corpses of thirty armored bears.","Some were fourth tier. Some were fifth tier. A handful were sixth tier.","All of them were dead. Sliced, apart, crushed, or simply burnt. The ground was filled with sword scars and craters.","Dexter’s teammates lay scattered behind him.","Marcos was conscious but barely, clutching his left arm, which hung from his shoulder by nothing but tendon and a thin strip of flesh.","Gregor was on his back, a long, savage claw mark carved across his chest, the wound was so deep his white bones could be seen.","Lena lay face down, as a matching claw mark running the full length of her back, her breathing shallow and irregular.","Fiona was sitting upright, which was more than could be said for the others, but her face was utterly bloodless. Her eyes were half closed and her body swayed slightly where she sat.","She had pushed her time dilation ability to its absolute limit, making her look as though she was halfway to death’s door.","Nobody spoke for a long moment.","But Rachel moved.","She walked past the Head Supervisor, past the corpses and the blood and the devastation, and she threw her arms around Dexter.","Dexter went rigid and his mind went blank.","The massive head slipped from his grip and hit the ground with a heavy, wet thud that shook the earth slightly. He stood there with his arms at his sides, unsure of what to do, as Rachel pressed her face against his blood-soaked chest.","\"Thank goodness you are alright,\" she said, her voice muffled against him. \"Thank God. Thank goodness you are alright. Are you really alright? Whose blood is this? Is this your blood? Do you need medical attention?\"","Dexter cleared his throat awkwardly. \"I do not need medical attention. It is not my blood. It is the blood of the beasts.\"","He gently tilted his head toward his fallen teammates. \"But the others are injured. They need medical attention immediately.\"","Rachel pulled back and finally looked at the ground around them. She glanced indifferently at the others injured. She didn’t care for them so it wasn’t her problem. She was only concerned about Dexter.","The Head Supervisor approached Dexter and placed a firm hand on his shoulder. \"It is good that you are alright. We apologize for what happened. The malfunction, the failure of the extraction system, all of it. We take full responsibility.\"","Dexter frowned. \"What actually hap...\"","\"What the fuck happened?\" Marcus roared from the ground, his face twisted in pain and fury. \"What the fuck actually happened? Where the hell were you people? We were almost killed in there! You said this was a controlled dungeon! This does not look fucking controlled to me! It went way out of control! I am suing you! I am telling my father to sue every single person in this fucking establishment!\"","The Head Supervisor did not flinch. \"It was not a malfunction. It was an intentional sabotage. Someone deliberately tampered with the extraction watches, the protection bubbles, and the wave progression system. We have not yet identified the responsible party, but the director himself will personally oversee the investigation. You will receive a full explanation and compensation for what you have endured.\""]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81 | Registration","paragraphs":["Immediately he heard the name Director Klein, Marcus’s mouth which opened to complain immediately snapped shut.","Everyone knew Director Klein was one of the seven Transcendants in the city.","Even Marcus understood that if the director was involved, things would move. The director’s reach was long, and his temper was legendary.","\"Medic,\" the Head Supervisor said into his earpiece. \"Get here now.\"","The medical team arrived in a flash. They poured through the arc door in organized pairs, carrying stabilized stretchers and emergency healing kits.","Healers with active healing talents moved among the injured, their hands glowing with soft, warm light as they knelt beside Marcus, Gregor, Lena, and Fiona.","Marcus was stabilized first, his severed arm carefully secured to prevent further damage. Gregor’s chest wound closed slowly under the healer’s touch.","Lena was rolled onto her side and treated with delicate precision. Fiona was simply lifted onto a stretcher and connected to an IV drip, her eyes already closed.","Dexter was guided toward the medical bay as well.","Dexter tried to wave them off, but the supervisor shook his head.","\"No arguments. You might have hidden injuries. Internal damage you can’t feel yet. We need to be certain.\"","They guided Dexter to the medical bay. Rachel stayed with him every step.","Rachel walked beside him the entire way.","The medical bay was clean and bright, a sharp contrast to the blood and carnage of the clearing. A healer directed Dexter to stand before a large pane of translucent glass mounted in the center of the room.","\"Spread your arms,\" the healer said.","Dexter complied. The glass hummed softly, and a moment later his entire body became visible through the pane as a detailed, three dimensional skeletal and muscular projection.","The healer studied the readouts for a long time, then looked at Dexter with a puzzled expression. \"You are as healthy as they come. No fractures, no internal bleeding, no tissue damage, you’re good.\"","Dexter smiled slightly. \"Alright.\"","Rachel exhaled a breath she had been holding since the clearing and hugged him again.","Dexter stood there, arms at his sides, staring at the ceiling. He had no idea what to do with this girl. He had told her, plainly and directly, that he had three wives.","Most people heard that and immediately backed off. But Rachael seemed even more attached to him.","He gently but firmly extracted himself from the hug and took a step back. \"Where do I go to get my license card?\"","Rachel stared at him for a moment. Then she erupted into laughter.","\"You almost died in there,\" she said, still laughing, \"and the first thing you are worried about is your license card?\"","Dexter shrugged. \"That is what I came here for.\"","Rachel shook her head, a wide grin still on her face. \"Alright. Let me take you to the licensing hall.\"","They left the medical bay and walked through a series of corridors that led to a spacious hall with polished floors and a high ceiling.","A single queue stretched from the service counter toward the door.","There were five people ahead of them.","Rachel waited with him this time.","She stood beside him in the line, quiet for once, her earlier panic slowly fading.","Neither of them spoke. They simply stood there, waiting.","Under 10 minutes later, it was Dexter’s turn.","He stepped up to the counter.","The receptionist was a young woman with neat auburn hair pulled into a tight bun and thin reading glasses perched on the tip of her nose.","\"Your temporary ID?\"","Dexter produced it.","She took the temporary ID card from Dexter’s hand and typed his name into the system. Her eyes moved across the screen, and then they stopped moving.","She blinked. She adjusted her glasses. She read the screen again.","\"Mr. Dexter Ashford,\" she said, her tone shifting. It seemed she saw something.","\" You have passed the entry registration exam exceptionally.\"","She looked up at him over the rims of her glasses. \"Also, your potential rating is very high. In fact, let me check the official rankings.\"","Her fingers clicked across the keyboard. A new window populated on her screen.","\"You rank number 9 of the top 10 in the official F Hero rankings. That puts you well within the upper percentile of all F rank Heroes.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow but he wasn’t surprised.","The receptionist straightened in her chair and offered a polite smile. \"Welcome, Mr. Dexter. Please head through the inner doors for your proper registration.\"","Dexter nodded and walked past the counter, through a set of frosted glass doors, and into a long corridor.","At the end of the corridor was a single room. The door was open. Inside, a woman stood waiting beside a sleek, modern terminal.","She was truly stunning as she stood there.","High cheekbones, dark hair and calm eyes.","She wore the white coat of a medical professional, but it fit her like it had been tailored specifically for her.","\"Good morning,\" she said, her voice smooth and unhurried. \"How are you?\"","\"Quite alright,\" Dexter replied.","\"Please place your hand on the scanner.\"","She gestured to a flat, translucent panel mounted on the desk beside the terminal.","Dexter placed his right palm on it. A soft blue light passed beneath his hand, and he felt a faint warmth spread through his fingers as it processed his data.","\"Mana signature is being registered,\" the doctor said, watching the screen. \"This is a unique biometric identifier tied to your internal energy. No two signatures are alike. It will be embedded into your license card and used to verify your identity at any licensed facility or checkpoint.\"","The scan completed. A detailed waveform appeared on the screen, representing the specific frequency and pattern of his mana.","\"Next, I will need a retinal scan for visual verification,\" she said, turning to a small device mounted on an adjustable arm. \"Please look straight ahead and keep your eyes open.\"","Dexter complied.","\"Now a small blood sample for genetic archiving,\" she continued, producing a sterile lancet and a glass vial. \"This is standard procedure. The sample is encrypted and stored only for identity verification in the event of disputed license use. It is not shared with any third party.\"","She pricked his fingertip, collected a few drops into the vial, and sealed it. The entire process took less than ten seconds.","\"Lastly, emergency contact information.\""]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82 | You Are The Product","paragraphs":["Dexter provided the necessary details. The doctor entered them, reviewed everything one final time, and then pressed a button on the terminal.","A moment later, a small slot beneath the desk whirred to life, and something slid out into a velvet lined tray.","The doctor picked it up and held it out to Dexter.","It was a license card. But it was not the card Dexter had expected.","Most license cards issued to new registrants were F rank, which was standard for first time examinees.","The F rank cards typically came in normal plastics. But for top 10,000, they receive theirs in Iron.","Iron cards for those in top 10,000, Bronze for those in top 1,000, Silver for top 100 and Gold for those in top 10.","This card Dexter was given was pure gold.","’ Damn. They really went all out.’","Dexter chuckled in his mind as he looked at the card, then at the doctor.","\"The card functions as identification, bank account access, dungeon authorization, mission registration, medical insurance verification, and emergency extraction identification.\"","She paused and then continued. \"The gold card is issued exclusively to top ten registrants. It grants priority access to licensed dungeons, expedited processing at all guild affiliated facilities, and a few additional privileges that will be detailed in the document packet I am about to give you. The gold card also carries Tier 3 clearance—access to classified information and restricted databases that standard bronze and silver cardholders cannot view.\"","She turned to a folder on the desk and handed him a thick, sealed envelope. \"This contains your full registration documents, a handbook of license holder privileges and restrictions, and a directory of training centers, guilds and facilities in your region.\"","\"You will also receive a monthly stipend. Bronze-ranked licensees which is top 10,000 receive 1,000 dollars. Gold, like yours, receives 100,000 dollars monthly.\" She paused, something flickering in her eyes.","\"As for Diamond cards, they are reserved for the top three and receives one million. Individuals like Aurora, for instance.\"","Dexter eyes widnened slightly when he heard the amount he would receive monthly.","It was insane.","’ Hundred thousand dollars for doing nothing? There’s definitely a catch!’","If something is for free then you are the product. It was something that had stuck with Dexter for a long while and he squinted his eyes.","\"What’s the catch?\"","The doctor smiled prettily. \"It’s actually not much. You will be requested to clear an F or E rank dungeon at least 3 times a month and also tasked with immediate response to any dungeon outbreak close to you.\"","’ As expected.’","Dexter chuckled internally. But he wasn’t worried. Since he was getting paid, he would naturally work for the 100,000 dollars. Moreover, to grow stronger, he needed money to spoil his wives and increase his strength.","The doctor continued her speech.","\"Your profile is already live on the Hero Association website,\" the doctor continued.","The doctor then did something that surprised him.","She bowed slightly.","\"Congratulations, Mr. Ashford. And welcome to the licensed ranks.\"","From that point on, the staff treated him differently. Every person he passed in the corridor on his way out offered a nod or a polite greeting.","Dexter moved through it all calmly.","He tucked the gold card into his pocket, held the envelope under his arm and stepped back into the main corridor.","The supervisor from the observation room was waiting for him. Two staff members flanked the man in step.","\"Mr. Ashford,\" the supervisor said, stepping forward. He held out an envelope, thick with documents or credits or both.","\"One hundred and fifty thousand dollars. Compensation for the failures during your examination. I know it cannot compare to nearly losing your life, but I hope you can accept it as a gesture of our sincerity.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. These people truly didn’t want him to sue them.","He sighed and took the envelope.","He needed the money, his wives’ needs, his household’s expenses, the constant drain of maintaining even a modest noble lifestyle.","\"Thank you.\"","\"When the beast corpses from the examination are processed and sold,\" the supervisor added, \"your share of the profits will be transferred by tomorrow. Standard procedure for participants, but given your... performance, it will be substantial.\"","Dexter nodded again. \"Alright. I’m in a hurry so I will take my leave.\"","The Supervisor smiled and waved as Dexter left, then his eyes turned cold as he turned back to his staff members behind him.","\"How the fuck did you two fail a simple task?\"","...","Rachel was waiting for him in the main lobby.","She had been waiting since he went in. She fell into step beside him as he walked toward the exit.","\"You got the gold card,\" she said. It was not a question. She had known he would eventually get a gold card.","Dexter nodded.","\"I knew you would,\" she said simply.","They walked through the massive front doors of the building and out into the open air. The sun was high and the day was warm.","The garage where Rachel had parked was a short walk across a wide plaza paved with pale stone.","\"Let me drive you home,\" she said. \"Or at least to the bus station. Please.\"","Dexter shook his head. \"I need to get some things first. For my wives.\"","Rachel looked at him for a moment. Then she smiled playfully.","\"You really care about them, don’t you? It really makes me wish I was one of them.\"","Her eyes brightened up as she smirked.","Dexter stared at her with a raised eyebrow.","’ What exactly does she mean?’","\"Thank you, Rachel,\" he said, and extended his hand. \"For everything today. I will see you around.\"","Rachel looked at his hand then looked at him.","\"You’re truly cruel Dexter.\"","She took his hand and shook it but didn’t let go as she tilted her head and asked.","\"Have you heard of a Finger trap?\"","Dexter was a bit caught offguard by the change in subject.","’ She’s up to something.’","He slowly nodded his head. \"Yes, I’m familiar with it.\"","She smiled brilliantly and seductively. Her perfectly set, white teeth, pink lips and pink tongue as she licked her lips made Dexters heart trickle.","\"The more you struggle...\""]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83 | 250,000 Dollars!","paragraphs":["\"The more you struggle...\"","With that she turned around and left. Her hips swaying seductively in the afternoon sun.","Dexter inhaled sharply and decisively turned away.","\"Vixen.\"","He exited the Hero Association. He didn’t even inquire about Fiona, Gregory, Lena or Marcus, he simply just left.","Once he was a comfortable distance away, he pulled out his phone and opened the map application.","The screen loaded a detailed layout of the surrounding area, his current location marked with a small blue dot. He zoomed out slightly, scanning the nearby streets and districts.","He needed to find a market. His eyes immediately landed on a location.","Stargate Central Market.","Distance: 2.3 kilometers.","Dexter nodded. ’ Its within walking distance’","Perfect.","He still needed two necklaces.","If he returned home with a gift for only Mira...","He had a feeling surviving another dungeon would somehow be easier than surviving Lyra and Selene’s jealousy.","He set off at an easy pace, his phone tucked back into his pocket, and allowed himself to take in the city as he moved through it.","The district surrounding the Hero Association building was unlike anything he had seen in the quieter parts of the city.","The buildings here were tall and modern.","Massive billboards clung to the sides of the tallest structures, advertising everything from high end relic dealerships to serum clinics to luxury fashion brands that Dexter had only ever heard about in passing.","Dexter found himself stopping more than once. He stared at a billboard for a relic manufacturer that depicted a warrior encased in a futuristic glowing combat armor, it looked very masculine and attractive.","Dexter sighed and continued walking.","He enjoyed the walk through the city, forgetting the pain he was feeling at the moment.","By the time he reached his destination, he was satisfied with the sight seeing and he stepped through the entrance of the shop.","Thw shop was massive. It was a single, large establishment that dealt primarily in relics.","The interior was spacious and dimly lit, with display cases lined up in neat rows along the floor and mounted on the walls.","Each case held items categorized by type and tier.","Simple relics like Type 1 relics occupied the front of the store, like basic mana conductors and low grade enhancement trinkets.","Further back, the items grew more complex and more expensive.","Type 3 relics sat behind reinforced glass with individual price tags that made Dexter’s eyebrows rise slightly.","The type 4 and type 5 relics were kept in a sealed section at the very back, visible only through a transparent barrier.","Dexter moved through the displays with a specific goal in mind. He was looking for a necklace.","Specifically, a necklace similar to the one he had given Mira.","He had not planned to buy matching jewelry when he gave Mira hers, but seeing the way the Lyra had looked at it, he felt like he needed to.","He searched every display case on the floor.","But nothing matched. There were necklaces, certainly. Pendants, chokers, chains adorned with small relics. But none of them was the same as the one he gave Mira.","He walked to the clerk’s desk. The clerk was a young woman with a patient expression and a name tag that read Elise.","Dexter pulled out his phone, then turned the screen toward Elise.","\"Have you seen anything like this in your inventory? Or something similar?\"","Elise leaned in, studied the image carefully, and then shook her head. \"I am sorry, sir. We do not carry anything like that. The design is quite specific. It looks like it may be a custom piece or from a specialized dealer.\"","Dexter frowned slightly, thanked her, and left the store.","He stood on the sidewalk outside and looked around.","The advantage of being this close to the Hero Association building was that the surrounding district was packed with specialty stores.","Relic shops, art galleries, fashion boutiques, serum clinics, and medicine shops lined the streets in both directions, each one competing for the attention of the licensed heroes and wealthy patrons who frequented this area.","He spotted a medicine shop two blocks down and entered it.","The woman behind the counter was middle aged her eyes scanning Dexter as he entered.","Dexter approached the counter. \"I need a month’s supply of Ice suppressant serum. The high quality version, not the standard grade.\"","The woman raised an eyebrow slightly but did not comment.","She turned to a locked cabinet behind her and retrieved a small box.","\"This is the premium grade,\" she said, placing the box on the counter. \"2000 dollars per vial. So 60,000 dollars total. However, we do offer a slight discount for full month purchases. 59,500 even.\"","Dexter’s eyebrows trembled. He bought something worth 60,000 dollars and all they removed from discount was just 500 dollars? Was the discount even needed?","With the compensation he had received and the monthly stipend for ranking in the top ten, he has about 250,000 dollars but right now 60,000 was gone already.","The cheaper suppressants were unreliable, and he was not about to compromise on something Seven needed.","\"I will take it,\" he said.","As the woman began processing the transaction, Dexter’s thoughts drifted to the pain he was feeling and trying to block out.","He had been managing it since the past days, pushing it to the back of his mind.","He contemplated on buying pain relief for the girls to relieve himself.","He was considering asking the woman for a mild pain reliever when a notification chimed softly in his mind.","DING!","A familiar notification echoed inside his mind.","═══════════════════","[Endurance Buddha Scripture has advanced]","[Second Layer Iron Bones Completed.]","[Third Stage Golden Organs Unlocked.]","Rewards:","→ +100 Strength","→ +100 Agility","→ +100 Physique","→ +100 Mana","═══════════════════","Dexter froze.","His muscles trembled as a surge of power flooded his being, within seconds, his body trembled as his strength increased even further.","His body felt light and impossibly dense at the same time, as though every cell had been replaced with something fundamentally better.","Then the sensation faded, leaving his body warm and tingling.","The pain was still there too. But it was different now. As if the Gold Organ stage had created a layer of separation between the pain and his awareness of it.","He could still feel it if he focused on it, but it no longer demanded his attention.","He looked at the woman behind the counter, who was waiting with a packaged box and a receipt. He had been standing in silence for several seconds.","He shook his head slightly. There was no need for the pain relief after all. He was used to the pain, and now, with the Golden organs active, it was even better.","He paid the thirty thousand, took the packaged box of eye suppressant serum, and left the medicine shop."]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84 | Purchasing CloudWeave Bed","paragraphs":["The jewelry store next door was larger than the relic shop he had visited earlier.","The air was different here. The display cases near the entrance held rings and earrings, but Dexter walked past them without a second glance. He moved deeper into the store, until he reached the necklace section at the far end.","He still condone find it.","Then he pulled out his phone, opened the image of Mira’s necklace again, and walked to the clerk’s desk.","The clerk was a woman also. Dexter turned the phone screen toward her.","\"I am looking for something that matches this,\" Dexter said.","The clerk studied the image on Dexter’s phone for a long time.","\"This is a type three relic, possibly type four,\" she said in a professional tone.","\"Pieces like this do not circulate through standard retail channels. They are typically commissioned by the major families. The Ashfords, the Vances, the Hargroves. When items of this caliber are produced, they are reserved for the wives and daughters of those households. You would not find one in a public shop.\"","Dexter’s frown deepened. \"What about the auction houses?\"","The clerk shook her head slowly. \"Even at auction, a piece like this would draw fierce bidding from the major families. A private individual without family backing would find it nearly impossible to secure. I am not saying it is impossible, but it would be very, very difficult.\"","Dexter was quiet for a moment.","\"Can I get an imitation?\" he asked.","The clerk’s expression tightened. She glanced toward the front of the store, then back at Dexter. \"I am not supposed to discuss that,\"","She said quietly. \"Recommending imitation goods to a customer is against store policy. I could lose my position.\"","Dexter held her gaze for a moment, then reached into his pocket. \"Two thousand. Just for the information.\"","The clerk frowned and shook her head.","\"Three thousand.\"","She shook her head again, but this time she did not step back.","She did not walk away. She stood exactly where she was, her fingers resting on the edge of the display case, her eyes flickering with something that was not quite refusal.","\"Five thousand,\" Dexter said.","The clerk was still for several seconds.","She looked at the floor, then at the ceiling, then at the front of the store where a manager was visible through the glass partition, sorting through inventory paperwork.","Then she looked back at Dexter and gave a small, slow nod.","\"There is a place,\" she said, her voice barely above a whisper. \"About an hour from here, east of the commercial district, past the old warehousing blocks. Tell them Mara sent you.\"","Dexter smiled as he nodded. \"Thank you.\"","The clerk smiled, tilting her head slightly, and said, \"You are welcome. Please come back and purchase more items if you wish. I am always here to help.\"","Dexter pursed his lips and rolled his eyes.","She was shrewd. Five thousand for a sentence, and now she was already angling for a return visit that might bring more. But she knew her business, and he could not fault her for that.","He turned and left the store without another word.","The black market was an hour away, and he fully intended to go there.","But on his way, he passed a building that caught his attention.","It was a furniture store, but not the ordinary kind. The storefront was wide and grand, with large display windows showcasing elegantly arranged room sets that looked like they belonged in a mansion rather than a retail floor.","The sign above the entrance read Celestine Home, and beneath it, in smaller script,","Furnishings for the Extraordinary.","Dexter paused. He wanted to purchase beds for the girls and himself so he went inside.","As expected, it looked really nice. A sales representative approached him with a polite smile, but Dexter waved her off and headed straight for the elevator.","\"Which floor has the beds?\" he asked as the doors closed.","\"Third floor, sir.\"","The third floor opened into a long, wide gallery lined with beds.","Dozens of them. They ranged from simple platform frames to elaborate four poster designs with canopies and carved headboards.","Each bed was made up with premium linens and arranged in its own small vignette, complete with nightstands, lamps, and accent pillows, as though inviting the customer to imagine falling asleep right there in the store.","Dexter walked the length of the gallery, scanning each option. Queen sizes, king sizes, California kings.","He sat on several of them, testing the firmness.m but it dishes reach his requirements.","Then he reached the end of the gallery and found a bed that stopped him in his tracks.","It was a king size platform bed with a low, sleek frame made from dark ironwood, a material so dense that it was rumored to be slightly resistant to mana.","The frame alone was striking, but the mattress was what commanded attention. It was thick, easily a foot and a half deep, and it had a slight iridescent quality to its surface,","Dexter sat down on the edge.","The mattress yielded beneath him like sinking into warm water.","It was soft, impossibly soft, but it did not collapse.","There was structure beneath the softness that rose up to meet his weight and distribute it evenly, so that he felt supported and cradled at the same time.","He shifted his weight, leaned back, and felt the mattress adjust to the new position without a sound.","No creaking. No springs pressing against him. Just a smooth, effortless conformity to his body.","A female assistant appeared at his side. She was tall and composed, with her hair pulled back in a neat ponytail and a tablet clutched against her chest.","\"That is the Cloudweave Sovereign,\" she said, a note of pride in her voice. \"The mattress is constructed from layered Cloudwool sheared from lunar rams, which are raised on the high altitude pastures of the northern mountain ranges. Cloudwool is naturally temperature regulating, hypoallergenic, and possesses a unique cellular structure that distributes pressure so evenly that it eliminates virtually all contact stress on the body. The inner core is made from compressed essence silk, which provides the structural support. The outer covering is woven from moon thread, which gives it that slight shimmer you are seeing.\""]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85 | Black Market","paragraphs":["Dexter head was almost exploding with all the information she was dropping.","He ignored her and simply ran his hand across the surface. It was smoother than most things he had touch.","But never smoother than Mira...","\"This bed has been extremely popular among licensed heroes,\"","The assistant continued. \"In fact, it is the same model used by Blitz, the speed star herself. She endorsed the Cloudweave line after our parent company became one of her sponsors.\"","Dexter glanced to the side and saw the advertisement mounted on the wall beside the bed.","It showed Blitz, the renowned female Ultra hero, seated on the edge of an identical Cloudweave Sovereign, her silver hair catching studio lighting, one hand resting on the mattress with an expression of casual satisfaction.","The caption beneath read, \" Even the fastest need the best rest. Cloudweave by Celestine Home.\"","Dexter was not particularly impressed by celebrity endorsements. But the bed itself was another matter. He could already imagine how the girls would react to sleeping on something like this.","They would love this bed.","\"How much?\" Dexter asked.","The assistant smiled but did not answer immediately.","She tapped something on her tablet, scrolled, tapped again, and then looked up at him with the particular expression that salespeople wore when they were about to deliver a number they knew would provoke a reaction.","\"Thirty thousand dollars,\" she said.","Dexter stared at her.","\"Thirty thousand,\" he repeated flatly.","\"Yes, sir.\"","\"For one bed.\"","\"The Cloudweave Sovereign is a premium product, sir. The materials alone...\"","\"Is it made of heavenly clouds?\" Dexter asked, his voice perfectly calm but his eyes slightly wider than usual. \"Because I genuinely do not understand why a single bed costs thirty thousand dollars.\"","The assistant covered her mouth with one hand and shook her head as though Dexter had made the most charming joke she had heard all week.","Dexter sat on the edge of the Cloudweave Sovereign and said nothing.","He was not joking. In a world where people could manipulate fire, bend the earth to their will, and tear holes in the fabric of space, it was not unreasonable to wonder whether someone with the ability to shape the sky could fashion a bed from actual clouds.","He kept the thought to himself, however, because explaining it would only prolong a conversation he did not want to have.","He calculated Two beds would cost sixty thousand. It would drain his money as he still needed to prichasw a lot of things like foodstuffs, ingredients and jewelries for the girls., but it was workable.","He made his decision.","\"I will take two,\" he said.","The assistant’s smile widened. She tapped furiously on her tablet, her earlier laughter replaced by the brisk efficiency of a closing sale. \"Excellent choice, sir. If I may ask, will you be taking them with you today, or would you like them delivered?\"","\"Delivered,\" Dexter said. \"What is the timeline?\"","\"Standard delivery is next day. However, we do offer an expedited option for an additional five thousand dollars, which would have them at your address within four hours.\"","Dexter shook his head. \"Next day is fine.\"","The assistant nodded and guided him through the purchasing process. He provided his address, confirmed the delivery details, and signed the digital receipt. The total came to exactly sixty thousand dollars.","The assistant printed a physical copy of the receipt, placed it inside a sleek Celestine Home folder along with a care guide for the Cloudwool mattress, and handed the package to him with both hands.","\"Thank you for your purchase, sir. We are certain the ladies in your life will be very pleased.\"","Dexter took the folder, tucked it under his arm alongside the medicine shop packaging, and left the store.","The walk to the black market took just under an hour. Dexter followed the directions the jewelry clerk had given him,","He found the iron door at the end of a narrow alley between two warehouses.","’I hope this isn’t some organ trafficking thing. ’","Dexter opened it and stepped inside.","What he found was not what he had expected.","He had imagined something dark. Something dangerous. An underground marketplace lit by flickering torches or bare bulbs, where shadowy figures conducted illicit business in hushed tones and everyone watched everyone else with suspicion.","What he got was a thrift market.","It was a massive complex. The interior was open and well lit by overhead fluorescent panels, with wide aisles that crisscrossed between rows of stalls and tables and makeshift display areas.","Traders sat behind their wares, calling out to passersby in the same loud, casual voices that vendors used in any open air market anywhere in the city.","Come look at this. Best price in the complex. You will not find this anywhere else, my friend.","The goods on display were where the difference lay. On a table near the entrance, a woman was selling type one relics, small trinkets and minor enchantments laid out on a faded cloth.","A few stalls down, a heavyset man with a thick beard had arranged a collection of type two weapons on a rack, each one tagged with a handwritten price card.","Further in, Dexter spotted type three items, including a set of gauntlets that faintly hummed with stored energy, and a shield that seemed to absorb the light around it.","But it was the stall near the far wall that made Dexter stop.","A man sat cross legged on the floor. His eyes were closed as though he were meditating rather than selling goods. In front of him was a blade.","It was a type 3 blade. Dexter could tell from the way the air around it seemed to bend slightly, the faint distortion that indicated a high concentration of refined mana sealed within the weapon’s structure.","Dexter was stunned, but not because of the blade.","He was stunned because the blade was sitting out in the open, unguarded, on a cloth mat on the floor of a black market, with the seller’s eyes closed and his attention clearly elsewhere.","A type 3 blade was worth a fortune. In the hands of a capable fighter, it could dramatically alter their combat capabilities.","There were people in this very complex who would kill for a weapon like that, so why exactly was he puttingvthebwepaon out there just like that?"]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86 | Purchasing Tea","paragraphs":["There were people in this very complex who would kill for a weapon like that.","Yet no one touched it. No one even approached the stall closely and their was even a wide space around the man.","People kept casting glances at the blade and then at the seated man, and then quickly moving on.","Dexter looked at the man more carefully. He was lean, with sharp features and dark hair that fell past his shoulders.","His clothes were plain.There was nothing about his appearance that immediately announced who or what he was.","But Dexter felt a faint pressure that was almost imperceptible as it distorted space around him.","’ Ultra rank hero!’","Dexter’s eyes widened slightly. He had never seen an ultra rank hero in person before but he heard they were vastly powerful compared to Meta humans and Superhumans.","And he was sitting cross legged on the floor of a black market, selling a type 3 blade with his eyes closed.","Dexter could not make sense of it. An ultra rank hero had access to the Hero Association’s most exclusive resources. They could join various guilds receive funding, equipment, and support that ordinary licensed heroes could only dream of.","They were recruited the moment their rank was confirmed, courted by factions and organizations that competed for their allegiance.","An ultra rank hero could walk into any weapon dealer in the country and receive preferential treatment, the kind that came with VIP status and unlimited credit lines.","So why was this man sitting on the floor of a black market, selling a single type 3 blade to strangers?","Dexter stood there for a long moment, watching the meditating ultra rank hero,","’ Forget it.’","Then he shook his head slightly, filed the mystery away for another time, and moved on.","He had come here for a specific reason, and staring at an ultra rank hero was not going to help him find an imitation necklace for his wives.","Dexter moved through the black market, checking stall after stall.","The first nine sellers either did not carry imitation jewelry or the quality of their work was so poor that even a casual glance would reveal the deception.","One man tried to sell him a necklace that was clearly just spray painted copper, and Dexter had to suppress the urge to drag the man by his collar to the nearest mirror.","By the tenth stall, he found what he was looking for.","The seller was a quiet woman with gray streaks in her hair and a display case that was noticeably better organized than her neighbors.","Inside, arranged on black velvet, were several pieces of imitation jewelry that actually resembled their higher tier counterparts.","They lacked the mana signature, durability, but visually, they were remarkably close.","Dexter pointed to a necklace that shared the same design elements as Mira’s. It was a type 1 necklace.","\"I will take this.\"","The woman nodded and reached into the case.","Before Dexter could breathe a sigh of relief, the trader at the neighboring stall leaned over.","He was a short man with a wide grin and eyes that darted between Dexter’s face and the wallet in his pocket with the subtlety of a hungry dog watching a steak.","\"My friend, my friend,\" the trader said, sliding around the edge of his own stall and inserting himself into the transaction with practiced ease. \"You are buying for a lady, yes? Just one necklace? No, no, no. This is not how you impress a woman. You need the full set.\"","He produced a pair of earrings from his stall and held them up to the light. They were type one, modest in quality, but they caught the fluorescent light prettily.","\"Look at this. Perfect match for the necklace. The same design language, the same finish. A woman notices these things, my friend. She sees the necklace and she thinks, where are the earrings? Where is the bracelet? You do not want her thinking you only care enough to buy one thing.\"","Dexter frowned. \"I do not need...\"","\"And this,\" the trader continued, already reaching behind him, producing an anklet with a delicate chain and a small charm at the center.","\"For the ankle. Very popular right now. All the fashionable ladies in the city are wearing them. And this bracelet, look, see the workmanship? This is not cheap garbage. This is quality type one craftsmanship.\"","The trader was relentless. Every time Dexter tried to decline, the man produced another item, held it up, explained why it was essential, why the girls would expect it, why buying just the necklace was somehow an insult to the very concept of gift giving.","He moved between his stall and the woman’s stall grabbing items from both displays and assembling them into an ever growing pile on the counter.","Dexter stood there, caught in the current of the man’s sales pitch, and realized with a distant sort of irritation that the trader was right about one thing.","He did not know what girls liked. He had no idea what they preferred, what they secretly wanted, what small things might make their day better.","He knew their personalities. But not the specifics of what brought them joy in the small, everyday sense.","By the time Dexter extracted himself from the trader’s gravitational pull, he had spent 20,000. Necklaces, earrings, anklets, bracelets, finger rings, and hairpins that the trader had slipped into the pile when Dexter was not looking.","The man had smiled the entire time, that wide, greedy grin that said he knew exactly what he was doing.","Dexter left the stall angrily.","He knew he had been manipulated. It was his own fault for not walking away sooner.","He put it behind him and walked towards where food stuffs were been sold.","The section smelled of earth and green things, cut grass and dried bark and the faint, sweet scent of flowers that had been set out in small buckets near the entrance.","Dexter moved through the herb section first.","Tea herbs lined one entire row, sorted by variety and origin.","Calming blends for sleep and relaxation sat beside energizing blends for morning routines.","Meditation aids, awareness enhancers and, aphrodisiac blends!","Dexter swallowed as he saw it but immediately removed his gaze."]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87 | Psychological Welfare","paragraphs":["Dexter’s eyes drifted across the black market as he walked, scanning the stalls and tables without any particular purpose.","Then they stopped.","The ultra rank expert was still there.","He sat in the same position as before, cross legged on the floor, eyes closed while the type three blade lay there before him.","He then checked the weapon closely and saw it was incredibly beautiful.","The sword body was very dark but it was also incredibly beautiful.","It wasn’t flashy at all, nor was it dull","It looked more like elegant.","The steel had a faint silver sheen that seemed to shift depending on the angle, like moonlight on still water.","It was, without question, designed for a woman. It wasn’t decorated with much jewels or covered in elaborate engravings. In fact, its appearance was remarkably simple. Yet that simplicity made it elegant. The slender blade, graceful guard, and perfectly balanced design gave it a quiet beauty that would undoubtedly appeal to women.","More importantly...","It was a Type-3 Relic.","A weapon powerful enough to greatly enhance its wielder in battle.","The more Dexter looked at it, the more certain he became.","The girls would absolutely love this...","Dexter paused.","He should keep walking. He had already spent far more money than he had planned to spend.","The jewelries he purchased was enough and adding more expenses would be irresponsible.","But he was like a gambler. Just one last purchase. One last 100x investment opportunity.","Dexter stood there for several seconds, warring with himself. The rational part of his mind told him to walk away. The irrational part, already calculating his rewards and the smile on his girls faces.","The irrational part won.","’I bet the price would scare me away.’","He adjusted the bags under his arm and walked toward the trader.","He stopped in front of the cloth mat and looked down at the blade. Then he looked at the man.","\"How much?\" Dexter asked.","The man did not open his eyes. His response came in a voice that was low and unhurried, carrying the particular gravity of someone who had no need to rush anything.","\"I am not selling it.\"","Dexter frowned. If you are not selling it, then what are you doing here? The question rose in his mind, but he kept it behind his teeth. Questioning an ultra rank hero’s choices seemed like a poor way to start a conversation.","\"In that case, never mind.\"","Just as he turned to leave—","\"I am not selling it,\" the man repeated, and this time his eyes opened, \"but I am exchanging it for certain items.\"","Dexter paused mid turn. He looked back at the man over his shoulder and blinked his eyes thoughtfully. Then replied.","\"What item do you wish to exchange it for?\"","\"A grade three heavenly material.\"","Dexter went still.","Heavenly materials. Heaven and earth treasures are rare treasure.","Unlike weapons, which could be used repeatedly and passed from owner to owner, heavenly materials were consumable.","They could only be used once, their power expended in a single moment of transformation or enhancement.","And because of that single use limitation, they were valued above almost everything else.","Obtaining a type three relic weapon was difficult but achievable. Enter a high grade dungeon, defeat the creatures within, and there was a chance, however small, of finding one.","But heavenly materials were different. They did not appear in dungeons with any reliability. They were found in places so dangerous that the mortality rate for expeditions was measured in percentages rather than fractions.","People died for grade three heavenly materials and here was an ultra rank hero, sitting on the floor of a black market, asking for one in exchange for a single type 3blade.","\"No one in their right mind would trade a Grade-3 Heaven and Earth Treasure for a single Type-3 weapon.\"","The man’s eyes flashed, \"Does not mean you do not have one.\"","Dexter met his gaze without flinching. \"Maybe I do. Maybe I do not.\"","The man snorted, a sound of dismissive amusement, and closed his eyes again. The conversation, as far as he was concerned, was over.","Dexter stood there for a moment, then smirked. \"Alright. It is your choice if you want to miss this opportunity. Who knows when the next one will come.\"","The man’s nostrils flared slightly. He inhaled, as though testing the air for something, then shook his head without opening his eyes. \"You are bluffing. You do not have a grade three treasure.\"","\"It is up to you whether you want to miss this opportunity or not,\" Dexter said, and this time he actually turned and started walking.","He did not look back in the slightest. Behind him, he could sense the man’s attention pressing against his back.","But Dexter simply kept walking.","\"...Fine.\"","Dexter stopped walking.","A faint smile flashed across his lips before disappearing.","When he turned around again, his expression had become completely calm.","The man was looking at him now, his eyes open and it was obvious he was frustrated.","\"What else do you want to exchange for the grade three treasure?\" Dexter asked.","The man’s jaw tightened further. \"I have one more weapon with me. I will exchange all two for the treasure.\"","Dexter shook his head reading three of his fingers. \"Three grade three weapons.\"","The man’s expression darkened as his nose flared. \"Why do you not just put a blade to my neck and steal it instead?\"","\"Three weapons or nothing,\" Dexter replied with indifference. \"I don’t need the weapons. But it seems you need the trwaure. So what’s it gonna be?\"","\"Do you want to rob me?\" The man’s voice had dropped.","Dexter sneered. \"You have no other choice. You can exchange, or I leave. Those are your options.\"","The man leaned forward slightly, and the pressure in the vicinity intensified to the point where Dexter could feel it pressing against his skin like a physical force. \"I could simply take it from you.\"","Dexter did not move. \"Do you think I am dumb enough to bring a grade 3 heavenly material into a black market, in front of an ultra rank hero, without any protection? Of course I did not bring it with me. I left it somewhere safe. This is my first time in this place. Bringing a treasure here would be asking for death, and I am not seeking death anytime soon.\""]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88 | Buying Weapons For The Girls","paragraphs":["The man’s eyes narrowed. For a long moment, the two of them stared at each other, the air between them thickened as the man glared at him.","Then the man exhaled slowly, and some of the pressure receded.","\"Fine. Three weapons. Bring me the treasure.\"","Dexter frowned slightly. He had expected more resistance. But the man accepted so easily.","\"Are you lying to me?\" Dexter asked. \"I am fairly certain no one has three type three weapons just lying around. If this is some kind of trick...\"","The man flipped his hand.","Two more weapons appeared out of nowhere, materializing in midair and dropping to the cloth mat with soft thuds. One was fiery red like flames and the other gleamed with a silver so bright it seemed to glow.","Together with the original black blade, three type three weapons now lay on the mat in front of the ultra rank hero.","Dexter was stunned.","He had been toying with the man. He had pushed for three weapons specifically because he thought the demand was unreasonable enough that the man would refuse, and refusal would have been a clean exit.","He had not expected the man to agree. He had certainly not expected the man to produce the weapons on the spot, as though pulling out three type three relics was as casual as pulling out pocket change.","But the weapons were there and also real enough.","Dexter made a decision.","\"All right,\" he said.","He flipped his hand, and a small orb appeared in his palm.","It was perhaps the size of a walnut, but it was different and looked really nice.","The surface shimmered with colors that seemed to exist outside the normal spectrum, shifting and flowing in patterns.","A grade 3 heavenly material.","The man’s eyes locked onto the orb with an intense hunger and his pupils shrank.","\"A storage relic...\"","His breathing became noticeably heavier.","So that was why...","No wonder he couldn’t smell the treasure on him. The young man has a Quantum Ring.","Dexter smiled faintly.","\"Now you know why you couldn’t smell it on me.\"","The man’s gaze darkened for a brief moment.","For the first time...","Killing intent flickered deep within his eyes.","If he eliminated Dexter now...","Both the treasure and the storage relic would become his.","However—","Dexter simply stood there smiling.","Come on.","Try to take it.","See what happens.","The man stared at Dexter for a long, tense moment. He burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha!\"","\"I nearly forgot myself.\"","\"As an Ultra-ranked hero...\"","\"...breaking my word over greed would be truly disgraceful.\"","He accepted the Grade-3 Heaven and Earth Treasure before pushing the three relics toward Dexter.","\"The deal is complete.\"","Dexter stored the three weapons inside his storage relic before smiling politely.","\"Thank you. Thank you for the treasures.\"","The man waved a dismissive hand. \"Thank you as well. It has been a long time since I encountered someone interesting in this place.\"","Dexter chuckled. \"I will take that as a compliment.\"","\"You should,\" the man said, closing his eyes again and returning to his meditative posture. \"Now leave. You have what you came for, and I have what I came for. We are done.\"","Dexter nodded and left without hesitation.","Next was the food section. Dexter filled a basket with essentials: rice, flour, cooking oil, spices, fresh vegetables, meat, eggs, milk, and butter. He added dried fruit, honey, bread, and a few things he thought the girls might enjoy. By the time he finished shopping, the basket was overflowing.","He set everything down on a bench near the edge of the marketplace and took a moment to rest. Bags and bundles surrounded him in a small mountain of purchases. Pulling out his phone, he checked his remaining balance.","There was not much left but he still had enough to manage for a few days, but nothing more.","For a moment, he considered buying a vehicle. Nothing expensive, just something in the five to ten thousand dollar range to make getting around easier for him and the girls. It would save time and spare them from relying on public transport.","But the money from the dungeon kills was not here yet.","The payment for the beasts he had killed in the examination dungeon would arrive eventually. Thirty-one Armored Bears, including a Seventh-Tier boss. The money alone would be substantial.","He could wait.","Dexter abandoned the idea of buying a vehicle for now and started the walk home, carrying as many bags as he could manage.","The change from the marketplace district to his neighborhood was gradual. The streets narrowed, the buildings became shorter and older, and the smooth pavement gave way to cracked concrete and uneven patches.","It was rough around the edges, but not dangerous.","This was a working-class neighborhood. Quiet and lived-in. Far removed from the gleaming streets surrounding the Hero Association, yet comfortable in its own way.","A few stray dogs wandered the sidewalks, sniffing lampposts and ignoring passersby.","Dexter walked past a repair shop where a mechanic worked beneath the hood of a sedan, a convenience store with a faded sign, and a laundromat with steam-covered windows.","Then he passed a bakery.","It was a small shop wedged between a pawn shop and a closed pharmacy. The display window was modest, holding a few cakes beneath glass domes and a chalkboard listing the day’s specials.","But the smell drifting from the open door was irresistible.","Warm butter, vanilla, caramelized sugar, and toasted nuts filled the air.","Dexter stopped.","The girls would definitely like sweets.","Standing on the sidewalk with his arms full of shopping bags, Dexter made up his mind.","He shifted the bags to one arm, pushed open the door with his shoulder, and stepped inside.","The warmth hit him immediately.","Soft golden light filled the bakery, reflecting off cream-colored walls and polished wooden shelves stocked with preserves, specialty flour, and bundles of dried herbs that looked more suited to an apothecary than a bakery.","But it was the display case that captured his attention.","It stretched across the entire counter, filled with pastries unlike anything Dexter had ever seen.","The bottom shelf held Cloud Biscuits, pale pastries hovering just above their trays and glowing faintly.","Baked with refined cloud wheat flour. Levitation effect lasts approximately three minutes after removal from packaging.","Beside them sat Starfruit Tarts with deep violet crusts and fillings that swirled with gold and silver like miniature galaxies."]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89 | The Bakery And Tessa","paragraphs":["Soft golden light filled the bakery, reflecting off cream-colored walls and polished wooden shelves stocked with preserves, specialty flour, and bundles of dried herbs that looked more suited to an apothecary than a bakery.","But it was the display case that captured his attention.","It stretched across the entire counter, filled with pastries unlike anything Dexter had ever seen.","The bottom shelf held Cloud Biscuits, pale pastries hovering just above their trays and glowing faintly.","Baked with refined cloud wheat flour. Levitation effect lasts approximately three minutes after removal from packaging.","Beside them sat Starfruit Tarts with deep violet crusts and fillings that swirled with gold and silver like miniature galaxies.","Nearby were Ember Rolls, their glossy surfaces glowing with a soft red warmth while wisps of steam rose from them despite being fully baked.","Infused with low-grade fire essence. Maintains ideal eating temperature for up to six hours.","The middle shelf displayed larger creations.","There was a Mooncake the size of a dinner plate, its surface patterned like lunar craters and its filling visible beneath translucent dough that shimmered like moonlight.","Next to it stood the Dewdrop Tower, a layered cake of pastel colors crowned with edible crystal clusters that scattered tiny rainbows across the glass.","The top shelf held the premium items.","Phoenix Feather Pastries rested inside a lacquered box, each one shaped like a flame-colored feather.","Produces a gentle warming sensation from throat to chest.","And beside them sat ten pastries unlike anything else in the display.","They were round and roughly the size of a fist, their golden crust threaded with a faint shimmer as though strands of light had been woven into the dough itself.","Through small openings in the top, a pale cream filling could be seen shifting between white and gold depending on the angle.","A handwritten card rested against the plate.","Celestine Dew Pastry. Family Recipe. Limited Batch.","Dexter’s eyes widened.","His mouth watered as he stared at the display case like a man who had lived on plain bread all his life and had suddenly wandered into a royal banquet hall.","\"Dexter?\"","The voice came from behind the counter.","He tore his gaze away from the pastries and looked up at the girl standing there.","She was about 15 years of age, with auburn hair tied in a messy bun dusted with flour and an apron smeared with vanilla cream. She wiped her hands on a towel and smiled at him with easy familiarity.","It took him a second to recognize her.","\"Tessa,\" he said. \"Hey. How have you been?\"","\"I’m actually doing alright,\" Tessa replied, leaning against the counter. \"Though I feel I should be asking you that question. How are you doing after the monster outbreak and the attack at your home?\"","Dexter shrugged and replied.","\"I’m quite alright.\"","Tessa nodded. \"What about your wives? Are they okay too?\"","Dexter nodded in reply. \"Yeah. They were not affected by the beasts.\"","\"I thought the damage to your place made you move away from the area. When I heard about the monsters attack, I tried seeing you but you weren’t around so I figured maybe you left the neighborhood. \"","Dexter shook his head.","\"No. The Hero Association stepped in and moved me and my wives to a hotel while the repairs were being done.\"","Tessa’s eyes widened slightly.","\"That explains the construction noises. I thought your building was being renovated.\"","\"In a way, it was.\"","She laughed.","\"Fair enough. My dad and some of the neighbors were worried about you.\"","Then a mischievous grin spread across her face.","\"Though I guess I won the bet.\"","Dexter head tilted slightly and he blinked.","\"What bet?\"","\"The neighborhood betting pool after the attack.\"","She held up five fingers.","\"Some people thought you ran away. I said you didn’t. Looks like I just made five thousand dollars.\"","Dexter stared at her.","The neighbors had started a betting pool on whether he had fled.","Not whether he was safe or whether he needed help, it was whether he had run.","\"The audacity of my neighbors,\" Dexter muttered.","Tessa laughed.","\"What can I say? They’re quite entertaining when you get to know them.\"","A reluctant chuckle escaped him.","\"Well, congratulations on the win.\"","Then he glanced back toward the display case.","\"So, what’s good here?\"","Tessa immediately pointed toward the top shelf.","\"The Celestine Dew Pastries. Family recipe.\"","Her expression brightened as she spoke.","\"The dough uses sun wheat flour grown on the eastern mountain slopes, and the filling is made with dew nectar harvested from dawnflowers. The ingredients are difficult to get, so we only make a small batch each day.\"","She pointed at the porcelain plate.","\"And that’s the last batch.\"","Dexter looked at the pastries.","There were exactly ten left.","\"I’ll take all ten.\"","Tessa froze.","\"All ten?\"","\"All ten.\"","Lyra always ate more than everyone else, and if there were not enough to go around, she would be the first to notice.","Besides, if they tasted even half as good as they looked, everyone would want seconds.","Ten was not excessive.","Tessa laughed and reached for a pastry box.","\"You really don’t do things halfway, do you? Most people buy one or two. You walk in and buy the entire batch.\"","With care, she placed each pastry into its own compartment before tying the box shut with a ribbon.","Dexter watched quietly as the scent of bread, vanilla, and warm sugar filled the air around him.","For a brief moment, despite the bags digging into his arms and the lingering ache in his body, everything felt peaceful.","Tessa set the box on the counter.","\"There you go. Ten Celestine Dew Pastries.\"","She smiled.","\"Tell me what the girls think.\"","\"I will.\"","Dexter picked up the box carefully.","\"Thanks, Tessa.\"","⸻","Tessa rested her elbows on the counter.","\"So, how’s training to becoming a hero going?\"","Dexter shifted the bags in his arms.","\"Pretty well.\"","\"Pretty well,\" she repeated.","Then she tilted her head.","\"That’s funny, because I can’t sense you anymore.\"","Dexter’s expression remained calm, but his attention sharpened.","\"It’s strange,\" Tessa continued. \"Before, I could always sense and feel your strength.\"","She tapped the counter.","\"Now there’s nothing much. It’s like you’re not even here.\""]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90 | Being Followed","paragraphs":["Dexter’s strength had grown tremendously after improving his bloodline to Ancient Grade and also advancing to Gold Organs, the second stage of the Eternal Endurance Buddha Scripture.","Though he had not tested his limits yet, he estimated that his raw physical power was comparable to a 9th-tier superhuman, perhaps even peak knight tier.","Yet Tessa said she couldn’t sense him much.","She shouldn’t have been able to sense him at all. The Ancient Grade Chaos Flame Demon bloodline made sure of that.","Being part demon, one advantage was concealment. He gained the ability to conceal his energy waves from leaking out, yet Tessa said she couldn’t sense him much, meaning her strength had definitely surpassed Ultra rank.","Dexter kept his expression neutral.","An ultra-rank hero at her age should have been impossible. She looked no older than sixteen.","Reaching superhuman status took years of training, and advancing to ultra-human required even more talent, resources, and dedication. Most ultra-rank heroes were at least in their forties or fifties.","Yet the evidence was difficult to ignore.","Dexter filed the thought away.","\"Where is your dad?\" he asked, changing the subject.","Tessa straightened. \"He went out for an errand. He should be back tonight.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Greet him for me when he returns.\" He had never seen her dad, but he knew she wasn’t lying about him.","\"Alright,\" she said with a small smile.","Dexter turned to leave, then remembered something.","\"The old woman who sits in front of our building,\" he said. \"Was she one of the people who placed the bet?\"","Tessa’s smile became wry.","\"Old lady Lucy? Yes.\"","\"What did she bet?\"","\"Against you. Everyone did. I was the only one who bet that you wouldn’t run.\"","Dexter was silent for a moment before laughing.","\"Then I suppose I should thank you for defending my honor, lady Tessa.\"","Tessa waved a hand.","\"No need. I already got my reward. I can buy many things with 5000 dollars.\"","Dexter chuckled.","Several customers had entered the bakery during their conversation, and the staff was attending to them.","\"I’ll see you later,\" he said.","\"Come back soon.\"","Dexter pushed open the door and stepped into the afternoon air. The scent of fresh pastries faded behind him, replaced by the familiar smells of the neighborhood. Adjusting the bags in his arms, he started walking.","After about fifteen meters, he stopped.","Nothing had changed. The street remained quiet, with a few stray dogs wandering near a distant lamppost.","Yet something felt wrong.","It wasn’t a sound or a sight. It was a faint pressure at the edge of his awareness—the unsettling feeling of being watched.","And it was moving.","Someone was following him.","Whoever it was moved without sound or presence, blending into the surroundings so perfectly that they seemed part of the air itself.","Dexter continued walking, pretending not to notice.","A thief?","Unlikely.","Thieves were not this skilled, nor did they carry this subtle sense of danger. Well, not if you’re Batman’s parents.","Dexter turned into a narrow alley between two buildings. The afternoon sun barely reached inside, leaving the passage cool and shadowed.","There, he stopped.","Setting the bags against the wall, he slipped into the deepest shadow and waited.","Five seconds, ten seconds. Twenty.","But nothing.","No footsteps. No movement.","Frowning, Dexter unsheathed his blade as he focused hard, pouring mana into his eyes and activating his enhanced hearing talent; he extended his senses, stretching them to the max.","Even then, he couldn’t find a trace of the person.","Either the person was hiding without using energy, or their concealment was beyond his ability to detect.","He calmed his nerves and sheathed back his blade.","\"You can come out now. I already know you’re following me.\"","Silence.","No response.","A thread of doubt crept into his mind.","He had barely slept in days due to the pain of sharing his wife’s pain, so he resorted to cultivation.","Maybe it was the exhaustion from that, and he was imagining it.","Maybe the pressure was lingering tension from the dungeon.","Exhaling slowly, he turned toward the bags.","However, it was at that moment that l the air shifted.","There was no flash of light or burst of energy.","One moment the space ahead was empty.","The next, it wasn’t.","A woman stepped out of nowhere as though emerging through an invisible curtain.","She wore a dark cloak that covered her from neck to ankle.","The fabric seemed to absorb light, making her appear almost like a living shadow. Her hood hid most of her face, though Dexter caught a glimpse of dark, practical clothing beneath.","She stood three meters away from Dexter, observing him as she said nothing.","The pressure Dexter had sensed since leaving the bakery exploded in intensity.","It wasn’t killing intent or harmful intent. It was just a curious interest.","Dexter’s mind rapidly spun—an Ultra human.","At the very least, maybe even stronger.","An ultra-human expert had been following him.","The woman smiled, an amused expression on her face.","\"Relax,\" she said calmly. \"I’m not here to kill you. If I wanted you dead, I could have killed you the moment you left the Hero Association.\"","Dexter didn’t lower his guard immediately, but her words sank in.","Since the Hero Association.","She had followed him through the streets, the black market, the shopping district, his neighborhood, and even the bakery. Yet he had never sensed her.","She was right. If she had intended to kill him, he would already be dead.","After a moment, Dexter pocketed the Type 3 hidden weapons.","The Flame Demon transformation retreated into its sealed state, no longer on the verge of exploding. He took a slow breath and forced himself to relax.","\"Who are you?\" he asked.","The woman lowered her hood, revealing long violet hair and matching violet eyes. She looked about his age, but with softer skin and a pretty figure.","\"You don’t know who I am?\" she asked.","Dexter studied her face. It seemed familiar.","Then he remembered. He slapped his palm and smiled.","\"You’re that old man’s wife,\" he said. \"The one I saw on the hotel balcony.\"","\"Eh—!?\"","The lady was greatly stunned, and she actually choked on her own spit."]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91 | Spar With Me","paragraphs":["\"What the hell is running through your head?\" she huffed and glared at him","Dexter rubbed the back of his head and chuckled embarrassedly. \"I had no idea. That was why I said it. I did not know who you were.\"","The girl rolled her eyes with the most sass Dexter had ever seen. \"I am his granddaughter, you idiot. That old geezer is almost five hundred years old. There is no way I am his wife.\"","Dexter nodded his head. \"Right. Granddaughter, not wife.\"","But he was a bit surprised to hear that the old man was 500 years old. The old man still looked energetic, even more energetic than him, and he was nearly five centuries old. That explained a great deal about his presence and his power.","But then he remembered that this was the granddaughter the old man had used as a wager back then. Luckily for the old man, Dexter had rejected the marriage for his granddaughter as part of the wager; otherwise, it would have been something else.","’But what exactly is she doing here?’","Calming her nerves, the girl’s expression turned serious, and she stepped closer.","Her eyes glinted as she stared at him up and down as though she could see through him, and then her gaze settled on the base of his neck.","Her eyes suddenly brightened, and she stared intently at his neck, muttering.","\"The old geezer really did give you the necklace.\"","Dexter blinked and unconsciously touched the necklace on his neck. ’Was she here for this?’","She looked at Dexter’s eyes and then said slowly.","\"Can I have the necklace back?\"","Dexter frowned. His hand moved unconsciously to his neck, where the necklace the old man had given him rested against his collarbone.","\"Does the old man want it back?\"","The girl tilted her head and slowly shook her head. \"No. He said you won it fair and square. But you do not deserve to wear that key.\"","Dexter’s frown deepened. \"The old man gave it to me. He knows perfectly well whether I deserve it or not. It is not your place to decide if I’m worthy of it or not.\"","If she had asked properly, he might have shrugged and given her the necklace. He didn’t know what it was, and she was the granddaughter of the old man.","But the way she asked irritated Dexter instead.","The girl’s face changed, and her eyes narrowed.","For a split second, the color of her eyes changed from violent to pure gold.","At the same split second, a wave of heat gushed outward like a volcano erupting.","And for that same split second, the hair on Dexter’s neck stood on end, and he felt a surge of something immense and terrifying brush against his awareness.","She held his gaze for a second, but Dexter felt it was an hour.","But just as she was about to do something, she shook her head, the gold fading from her eyes as they returned to their usual violet, and let out a deep breath.","Dexter sighed in relief. If they had truly battled here, it would be an insane battle, and Dexter had no idea who would come out on top, but he knew she would at least lose a layer of skin.","The lady rolled her eyes indifferently as she asked a question.","\"How did you manage to learn Grand Cosmos?\"","Dexter inhaled deeply and raised an eyebrow. \"Was it really that difficult?\"","The girl’s eyelid trembled. Dexter truly knows how to press her button.","Her eye twitched. \"You have no idea what you are talking about.\"","Dexter frowned. \"I’m positive I do since I learnt the technique fully.\"","The girl inhaled deeply, her chest rising and falling as she visibly tried to calm herself. Dexter could practically see her blood pressure rising.","He was not entirely sure why his responses were aggravating her so much, but he was not going to change them to make her feel better.","\"The key would only cause you endless trouble. You should give it to someone who knows how to protect it.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"You, me, and your grandfather are the only ones who know I have it. I won’t say anything, and I’m pretty sure your grandfather won’t either. That only leaves you. As long as you don’t say anything, I will be fine.\"","The girl gritted her teeth as she heard Dexter’s response.","\"How about you tell me what this is and I will consider giving you or not.\" Dexter smiled deviously.","The girl glanced at him with her white eyes. \"Even if I told you, you wouldn’t understand.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"It was worth a try.\"","He then waved at her. \"Alright. Enough chat. I need to go home.\"","He was walking when he realized the girl was walking with him.","Dexter frowned. \"What do you want now?\"","\"Until I get my hands on the necklace, you are not leaving my sight.\" The girl suddenly smiled as she cracked her neck and stretched, making her large breasts pop out even more.","’ What the hell is this girl talking about? Am I about to have my own personal stalker?’","\"Do what you wish.\" With indifference in his tone, he replied.","The girl raised an eyebrow and smirked.","\"Don’t think I won’t follow you to meet your wives.\"","Dexter’s face changed slightly. But he wasn’t worried because he had the Tier 4 protection.","\"What would it take to leave me alone?\" He sighed.","The girl’s eyes lit up. \"Give me the —\"","She wasn’t able to talk for long when Dexter cut her off. \"Impossible, ask for another thing.","The girl glared at him for a second then spoke.","\"Do something for me.\"","\"What?\" Dexter asked.","\"Spar with me.\"","Dexter blinked. Then he chuckled. \"That is funny. You want me to spar with you.\"","The girl glared at him. \"Spar with me, and I will leave you alone.\"","Dexter’s chuckle faded, replaced by a flat look. \"You are an ultra rank. Possibly higher. How exactly is that supposed to be a fair fight? I’m not egoistic enough to think I can battle across realms.\"","[A/N: 100 GT Milestone Reached, 10 Chapters Mass Release will be released in 48 hours]"]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92 | 200,000 $ For A Spar","paragraphs":["Dexter frowned. \"What do you want now?\"","\"Until I get my hands on the necklace, you are not leaving my sight.\" The girl suddenly smiled as she cracked her neck and stretched, making her large breasts pop out even more.","’What the hell is this girl talking about? Am I about to have my own personal stalker?’","\"Do what you wish.\" With indifference in his tone, he replied.","The girl raised an eyebrow and smirked.","\"Don’t think I won’t follow you to meet your wives.\"","Dexter’s face changed slightly. But he wasn’t worried because he had the Tier 4 protection.","\"What would it take to leave me alone?\" He sighed.","The girl’s eyes lit up. \"Give me the —\"","She wasn’t able to talk for long when Dexter cut her off. \"Impossible, ask for another thing.","The girl glared at him for a second then spoke.","\"Do something for me.\"","\"What?\" Dexter asked.","\"Spar with me.\"","Dexter blinked. Then he chuckled. \"That is funny. You want me to spar with you.\"","The girl glared at him. \"Spar with me, and I will leave you alone.\"","Dexter’s chuckle faded, replaced by a flat look. \"You are an ultra rank. Possibly higher. How exactly is that supposed to be a fair fight? I’m not egoistic enough to think I can battle across realms.\"","The girl shook her head, and a small smile returned to her face. \"Relax. I will suppress my power down to your level. I will spar with you at the same strength. What do you say?\"","Dexter considered it. Part of him was genuinely curious. He had never fought an ultra rank before. He had never even been in the same room as one until today, and now he had encountered two or possibly three in a single afternoon.","The opportunity to experience what it was like to face someone at that level, even with their power suppressed to match his own, was tempting. He wanted to witness the power of an Ultra.","But then he shook his head and pushed the urge down. There was no logical reason to accept. He had nothing to gain from the spar itself, and the risk, however small with her power suppressed, was still present.","He had better things to do than indulge the strange whims of a five hundred year old man’s granddaughter.","\"There is no need,\" he said. \"I see no reason to spar with you. If I agree, you leave me alone. If I do not agree, what? You follow me forever? At some point, you will get bored and leave regardless.\"","The girl frowned, clearly not expecting his refusal.","She had probably assumed that the offer itself would be enough, that the chance to spar with an ultra rank would be too tempting for any young fighter to pass up.","She did not understand that Dexter did not operate on the same assumptions as other people his age.","\"How about I give you twenty thousand dollars?\" she asked.","Dexter frowned. \"Twenty thousand dollars to spar with you?\"","But he shook his head. \"No.\"","The girl’s frown deepened. She thought he was being difficult. Unreasonable. \"Everybody has a price,\" she said.","\"Not me.\"","\"Twenty thousand.\"","Dexter shook his head.","\"Thirty thousand.\"","He shook his head again.","\"Forty thousand.\"","No.","\"Fifty thousand.\"","No.","\"Seventy thousand.\"","Dexter was unmoved.","The girl smiled. \"Eighty thousand.\"","Dexter shook his head slowly. \"Do not bother.\"","\"Two hundred thousand.\"","\"6565436786 Starsoul Bank\"","The girl was stunned. She had thought Dexter was a man of pride and honor, expecting him to refuse, but he actually caved in.","Her lips curled as she glanced at him with a glint in her eyes.","\"The two hundred thousand is for when you win. I never said when I was going to give it to you. You asked me the condition for sparring, and I told you two hundred thousand. You agreed. You never asked if I was going to give it to you beforehand or whether it was conditional on winning.\"","Dexter was startled. That was true. He looked at the girl; a faint smile was on his lips and a hint of amusement in his eyes. \"That is true. It is actually not your fault. I should have asked for clarification.\"","\"When are we doing this?\" he asked.","\"Anytime you are ready,\" the girl replied.","Dexter thought for a moment. \"I am ready right now.\"","The girl frowned and looked at him, then at the bags of food and items scattered on the ground behind him. \"You are serious. What about all your food? It will go bad.\"","Dexter shook his head. \"If I go home, it will take a while for me to come back out. So we do it now, or we do it tomorrow.\"","The girl paused, considering. Then she nodded. \"Tomorrow is fine by me. So long as you keep your promise.\"","Dexter nodded. \"I do not like to break promises. I try to keep them when they are within my power.\"","The girl gave him one last look, something unreadable in her violet eyes. Then she turned around.","In a single step, she vanished.","Not walked away. Not moved quickly. Vanished. One moment she was there, and the next moment the space where she had been standing was empty. No sound. No displacement of air. No trace that she had ever been there at all.","Dexter stood in the corridor for a long moment, staring at the space.","\"Ultra rank,\" he muttered to himself. \"They have the power of teleportation. Teleportation to anywhere within their line of sight. That is one of the signature abilities of the ultra rank. Unlike superhumans, whose visible capabilities are limited to...\"","He trailed off and shook his head. He was talking to himself in an alleyway about power classifications. That was a sign that he needed to go home and rest.","He turned back, picked up the bags of food and items and the box of pastries, and continued walking toward his apartment.","...","The house was quiet when Dexter pushed open the door. He felt something was a bit off compared to when he left, and he frowned.","\"Did something happen to the girls?\"","He quickly set the bags down just outside the entrance and quickly entered inside.","What he saw stunned him."]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93 | Back At Home [1st GT & Gift Bonus - s]","paragraphs":["An extremely massive mansion lay within an ever stretching estate that radiated wealth and power.","Deep within the mansion was a massive room with toys and figurines of superheroes lined the shelves in countless rows.","And at the center of it all sat a thirteen years old, hunched over a desk, his pen moving steadily across paper as he did his assignments.","Soft music played in the background. The kids head bobbed rhythmically to the beat, completely absorbed in his work, oblivious to the world around him.","It was at that moment something happened.","The space itself seemed to fracture, the void rippling like disturbed water until it tore open.","From within that shifting void, a figure emerged and he stepped silently into the room, appearing directly behind the boy.","The kid didn’t seem to notice him as he continued bobbing his head to the music, writing his assignments, lost in his own world.","The man, however, did not advance further as his eyes glinted when he stared at the back of the youths head.","Suddenly —","THUD!","His knees hit the ground as he fell on his knees, bowed his head to stare at the ground as his body trembled violently like a kid caught stealing meat from the pot at midnight.","It was a shocking sight!","An ultra-rank expert actually kneeling on the ground, trembling before a thirteen-year-old boy as though he were a god.","He said nothing, it was as though he did not dare.","The boy continued working on his assignment as minutes passed.","Ten, twenty, then thirty.","For nearly half an hour, the man remained face-down on the floor, motionless except for his trembling body, waiting. The boy’s pen never stopped. His head never ceased its nodding to the music.","Finally, the youth yawned and stretched lazily then he set his pen down.","His eyes lifted from the assignment, but he did not turn to the man. Instead, he reached toward the speaker beside him and adjusted the music, changing the track with a casual flick of his fingers.","Suddenly, he spoke in a childish, almost playful tone.","\"You failed.\"","The words hung in the air like a death sentence.","The man’s face drained of color instantly. Sweat erupted across his brow, his body pressing harder into the floor as though the weight of those two words had physically crushed him.","\"Voss,\" the boy continued, his voice still carrying that unsettling youthful lightness. \"You truly disappointed me.\"","Without hesitation, Ross threw himself onto the floor, prostrating so deeply that his forehead struck the polished marble.","\"I... I deserve punishment, Sire,\" Ross said, his voice trembling.","Despite being an Ultra-Rank expert capable of making countless people kneel with a glance...","His breathing turned ragged. An ultra-rank expert, reduced to a trembling wreck by a child’s words.","It was a shocking sight.","The boy ignored him. He bobbed his head to the new track playing through the speaker,","His hands flying as he pretend rap to follow the music. The Ultra rank expert didn’t dare to live as he waited patiently.","The youth finally stopped fake rappinb and he chuckled as he said in an amused tone.","\"Think Voss, and give me a reason why you failed. You have only ten words to save your filthy life.\"","Ross slowly lifted himself from the floor but did not stand fully. He remained on his knees, head bowed, as he reached into his clothing and produced a phone.","The phone screen was cracked and pathetic.","He quickly played a video and spoke with trembling tone.","\"Here’s my reason, Sire.\"","He stretched out his hands towards the kid. The kid turned with a raised eye brow and took the phone from his hand.","He played it the video.","The recording showed an unclear figure using a single flaming strike killing a dark cloth man and then using flame breathe to kill another man.","The image wasn’t clear, the resolution poor and low quality but the events were unmistakable.","The figure who was Dexter had killed the assassins one after the other.","The boy’s eyes finally left the screen.","He turned to look at Ross for the first time.","...","Dexter pushed open the front door and stepped inside. Almost immediately, he stopped.","Something was wrong.","The moment Dexter stepped through the front door, he stopped.","\"...Hmm?\"","A faint smell lingered in the air and Dexter immediately recognized it was smoke.","The smoke had been cleared but the smell of burnt stuffs could still be smelt.","Dexter sniffed the air before frowning.","Someone tried cooking...","His first thought was that the girls must have gotten hungry while he was away.","\"I’m home,\" he called out.","Receiving no reply, he walked into the living room and the sight that greeted him made him pause.","The three girls were seated on the couch, Selene, and Lyra while Mira was seated in her wheelchair, beside them.","They weren’t watching television nor were they cultivating.","They were just sitting there, side by side, staring directly at him.","The three girls stared at him without blinking, It was as though they had been waiting for him.","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"You guys need something for me?\" he asked, his tone casual despite the strangeness of the scene.","Mira said nothing. Her expression remained flat, unreadable.","It was Selene who spoke first.","\"Yes,\" she muttered in a small voice. \"We were waiting for you.\"","Dexter blinked, puzzled by them suddenly caring about him and replied. \"I’m alright. The licensing went really well with no accident.\" Of course he was lying through his teeth.","Changing the subject. \"Did you girls cook something?\" he asked with concern.","\"Were you hungry? You should have just asked me to make something for you.\"","Mira rolled her eyes.","\"We tried to cook something for you, obviously we failed.\" she said flatly, falling at him with the corner of her eye.","Dexter stared at her.","They tried to cook something... for him?","He was stunned. The girls had been distant and guarded toward him. He had always been the one taking care of them.","Cooking, cleaning, buying supplies and making sure they were comfortable.","He had never expected them to try doing something for him. The fact that they had attempted to do something for him felt strange and surprising.","[A/N: Special thanks to reader \"LocopickleRICK\" for his Magic Castle Gift!!!","It will really help for the competition the book is participating in]","[100 GT = 10 Chapters Mass Release]","[Magic Castle = 5 Chapters Mass Release]","[Author owe the readers approximately 14 Chapters with this ( Will be released in 24 hours)]","[Thank you all for the gifts and support, really appreciate it. A real motivation to keep pushing! ╰(* ́)`*)╯♡╰(* ́)`*)╯♡(╹◡╹)♡]"]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94 | Suspicion [2nd GT & Gift Mass Release]","paragraphs":["The fact that they had attempted to do something for him felt strange and surprising.","His gaze softened slightly.","\"Are you sure?\" Dexter asked slowly. \"If you were hungry, you just needed to ask. I would have made something for you.\"","Mira shook her head. \"No. We. wanted to make something special for you.\"","Dexter fell quiet. The idea sat strangely in his mind.","Why would they make something for him?","He was the one taking care of them, providing shelter, food, protection.","They had never once tried to reciprocate. The gesture, while seemingly innocent, didn’t add up.","He looked at the three of them seated on the couch, his eyes narrowing with suspicion as he glared at Mira.","She must be the mastermind behind it. While the system said Lyra was the devious and two faced one, he felt like Mira was the true prankster.","Mira rolled her eyes even harder.","\"Why are you looking at us suspiciously?\" she said. \"You’re the suspicious one.\"","Dexter frowned. \"Suspicious about what?\"","Selene spoke again, her voice still quiet. However its tone had changed.","\"What do you know about second awakening?\"","The question landed like a stone dropped into still water.","Dexter’s expression tightened as his mind raced. Did one of them finally awaken?","He knew Mira had already awakened but the other two, Selene and Lyra, hadn’t awakened yet. Had one of them finally manifested the second ability?","\"I have no idea what you’re talking about,\" Dexter lied smoothly.","Instantly, Selene’s head snapped toward him. \"You’re lying,\" she said quietly. \"Your heartbeat skipped a beat just now.\"","Dexter feigned shock, his eyes widening as he looked between the girls.","\"Wait—the two of you awakened a second ability as well?\" He turned to Mira. \"You already awakened the Spectral arms ability. But what about you two?\"","He turned to Selene. \"Selene, you said you heard my heart skip a beat. What did you mean by that?\"","A small smile crept onto Selene’s face. She replied in a quiet, gentle tone.","\"I can finally see things now.\"","Dexter’s eyes popped open in exaggerated surprise. \"You can see?\"","Selene shook her head. \"Not really. I can’t see colors or details. But I can see through vibrations. I can see the outlines. It’s not true sight, but...\" She paused, her smile growing faintly. \"I can see.\"","Dexter nodded warmly. \"Congratulations. Even if it’s not the same as true sight, it’s still better than nothing.\"","Selene’s expression flickered with something like gratitude, perhaps—but she remained quiet, her nature keeping her words to herself.","Dexter then turned to Lyra.","\"Lyra, what did you—\"","’I awakened telepathy.’","The voice resonated inside his mind again—clear, soft, unmistakable. Lyra’s voice.","’I can hear the surface level thought thoughts of other people. And if they open their mind to me, I can speak to them also.’","Dexter clutched his chest in mock astonishment. \"That’s incredible,\" he said, his voice dripping with theatrical disbelief.","Then, recovering, he stroked his chin thoughtfully. \"Maybe it’s because your body realized what it had lost. Your body compensated, and awakened a new one to replace it.\"","Mira scoffed loudly as she gestured around at the three of them, with her chin.","\"Do you think we’re idiots? Countless people lose their abilities, but they don’t magically awaken a talent that perfectly bypasses their specific disability. Lyra can’t speak, so she gets telepathy. Selene is blind, so she gets echolocation. I can’t move, so I get spectral arms. There is no such thing as a coincidence this perfect.\"","Mira’s crimson eyes locked onto him. \"The only thing linking the three of us together is you, Dexter.\"","The three girls stared at him, suspicion etched deeply into their faces.","Dexter stared back at them for a long moment and when it seemed he was about to crack, he burst out laughing.","\"Wait—wait.\" He held up a hand, trying to contain his laughter. \"Are you three seriously telling me you believe I have the ability to grant other people talents?\"","The girls glanced at each other but didn’t respond.","Because they realized how ridiculous it sounded.","No one in the world had the ability to grant talents. The idea was absurd and they knew it. Mira, despite her stubborn nature, knew it.","And yet...","Dexter was the only person in their lives. The only constant. The only variable that had entered their world before these awakenings began. He was the only suspicious person they could point to. But accusing someone of granting abilities was like accusing them of controlling the reality.","Mira’s mouth tightened. She wanted to argue, but even she couldn’t rationalize it.","Dexter grinned sheepishly and waved his hand dismissively.","\"I’m really happy,\" he said lightly, \"that the three of you managed to awaken abilities that can assist you. That’s all that matters, right?\"","Then, seemingly as an afterthought, he turned toward Lyra and spoke aloud while projecting his thought to her at the same time.","\"Lyra, your voice is incredibly sweet. Like a thousand sirens calling out at the same time. Its’s really nice and soothing.\"","Mira smirked. \"Greedy pervert.\"","A faint blush crept across Lyra’s cheeks. Her voice fluttered softly in Dexter’s mind.","’Thank you.’","Dexter chuckled, then turned to Mira with a teasing grin. \"Are you jealous? If you are, just beg me and I’ll compliment you too.\"","Mira sneered. \"As if I’d need your compliments.\"","Dexter shrugged dramatically. \"Alright. Suit yourself.\" He paused, then leaned in with a sly smile. \"Jealous brat.\"","\"I am not jealous,\" Mira shot back immediately.","Her quick response only made Dexter’s smile widen.","\"Sure you aren’t.\"","Mira rolled her eyes, refusing to continue the argument.","\"Anyway, I got you girls something.\"","He walked back to the entrance of the house, where he had dropped several bags earlier when he first arrived. He scooped them up and carried them into the living room, setting them down on the floor in front of the couch.","From the first bag, he pulled out a massive egg the size of a watermelon. It was the ancient egg he got from the system.","[A/N: Special thanks to reader \"LocopickleRICK\" for his Magic Castle Gift!!!","It will really help for the competition the book is participating in]","[100 GT = 10 Chapters Mass Release]","[Magic Castle = 10 Chapters Mass Release]","[Author owe the readers approximately 13 Chapters (Will be released within 24 hours)]"]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95 | The Ancient Eggs [3rd GT & Gift]","paragraphs":["The egg shell wasn’t smooth like an ordinary bird’s egg. Instead, it was covered with overlapping scales that resembled the scales of an ancient dragon. Tiny cracks ran across its surface, giving it an ancient and mysterious appearance.","Dexter held it up for the girls to see.","\"This,\" he announced proudly, \"is the egg of an ancient beast.\"","Mira stared at it. Then she looked at Dexter.","\"You got scammed again,\" she said flatly.","Dexter’s rolled his eyes. \"You can’t scam a scammer. I’ve been in the business since I was 13, of course I know if I’m been scammed.\"","Life in the Ashford family hadn’t been kind. He had to scam a few kind souls just to survive.","Lyra and Selene were faintly curious.","They was the first time they were curious about anything other than the second awakening ever since Dexter had met them.","Selene’s vibration-sense picked up the egg’s outline and Lyra curiously looked at it.","The egg sat in Dexter’s hands like a relic from another era.","Mira, however, wasn’t impressed. \"You should probably go collect your money from whoever sold you this,\" she said, her voice dripping with skepticism.","Dexter shook his head slowly. \"Do you want it or not?\"","He began to pull the egg away, as if to take it back.","Before he could move more than a few inches, two glowing Mana arms glowing faintly with pale light. shot out from Mira’s side and snatched the egg from his hands.","Dexter smirked. \"I thought you said it was a scam.\"","Mira said nothing. Her spectral arm gently carried the egg toward her and settled it carefully onto her lap.","While her expression remained neutral, but the fact that she had claimed it so quickly spoke volumes.","Selene and Lyra immediately moved closer, drawn by curiosity. They reached out and touched the egg’s surface.","As they touched it, their expressions changed when they realized they couldn’t see through the egg with their mana but the egg was actively sucking any mana they provided like a sponge.","The egg didn’t feel like a fake.","Mira felt it too. But she said nothing. She simply held the egg in her lap and stared at it.","\"I heard it will hatch if one cultivates beside it. With the three of you cultivating by it, it would be faster than me cultivating with it. \"","Dexter watched them for a moment, smiling faintly, then reached into the bag again.","\"That’s not all I got for you.\"","He pulled out three weapons.","They had been wrapped casually in a grocery bag and bundled together like ordinary purchases. But the moment he unwrapped them, it was clear they were anything but ordinary.","The first was a beautiful black sword that seemed even darker than the shadows.","The second was a silver sword and the third was crimson sword.","He handed the black sword to Lyra.","\"This one’s yours.\"","Then he passed the silver one to Selene.","\"And this belongs to you.\"","Finally, he gently laid the crimson sword across Mira’s lap.","Mira stared at it before slowly looking back at him.","\"You do remember that I’m paralyzed... right?\"","Dexter shrugged unconcerned.","\"When you become more proficient with your spectral arms,\" he said calmly, \"you’ll be able to wield it. This weapon has a fire attribute. Once your control improves, it should complement your abilities perfectly.\"","Mira opened her mouth to argue, but Dexter had already turned away.","He faced Lyra next.","\"The relic weapon has shadow attributes and will enhance your shadow abilities and amplify your overall talents.\"","Lyra’s reached out and took the weapon, her fingers curling around its dark surface.","Then Dexter turned to Selene.","She was already looking at him—or rather, looking in his direction. Her new echolocation ability painted the world in shapes and outlines, vibrations forming a three-dimensional map of everything around her.","She could see him now, not in color, but in form.","Dexter held up the silver weapon, letting her sense its outline through vibration.","\"And this one,\" he said, \"is for you.\"","Suddenly, Mira noticed something.","\"You bought three Type 3 weapons?\" Her tone was a bit high.","Dexter nodded casually. \"Yeah. Got them at a discount, too. Really great deal.\"","The room went quiet.","Relic weapons were supposed to be rare and expensive, not the kind of thing an ordinary house husband could just walk into a store and buy three of, discount or no discount.","And yet, Dexter had done exactly that.","Mira’s eyes narrowed, a knowing smile crept onto her face.","\"Now I know,\" she said. \"There are people backing you up.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"I never said its true.\"","\"You never denied it either,\" Mira countered.","Dexter simply laughed at her observation, offering neither confirmation nor denial. Then he reached into the bag again.","This time, he pulled out two necklaces.","He had already given Mira one before, so he had purchased two similar ones for Lyra and Selene. He didn’t want the other two girls feeling left out or jealous.","He handed the necklaces to Lyra and Selene.","The two girls hesitated, wanting to refuse, but the necklaces were genuinely stunning.","They glanced at Mira, at the way her necklace sat against her neck, how perfectly it complemented her, how astonishingly beautiful it looked against her skin.","Mira noticed them looking. Her smirk returned.","\"I see,\" she said, her voice dripping with implication. \"You forcefully gave me a collar. Now you’ve gotten two similar ones for them.\" She tilted her head, her eyes boring into Dexter.","\"Why? Are you branding us as your property?\"","Dexter was momentarily stunned. Then he rolled his eyes.","\"I know exactly what you’re doing. Nice try though.\"","Mira’s smirk didn’t falter, but she didn’t push further.","Dexter reached into the bags one final time and began pulling out the rest of the jewelry he had purchased.","Anklets, bracelets, earrings. He had even bought gold mirrors for the girls.","One by one, he laid them out on the center table, dragging it closer to the couch so they could see everything clearly."]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96 | S-so Warm! [4th GT]","paragraphs":["The jewelry was dazzling.","Selene and Lyra stared at the display, slightly overwhelmed. But rather than reaching for the jewelry, they simply took the necklaces Dexter had handed them, stood up from the couch, and walked to the bedroom without a word.","They didn’t take anything else. They didn’t say thank you. They didn’t say anything at all.","Dexter watched them go, noting the shift in their demeanor. Their mood had soured visibly and the warmth and curiosity from moments ago had evaporated as they appeared more distant.","’Weren’t we just making progress?’","Mira smirked from her wheelchair, watching Dexter’s expression shift as realization dawned on him.","\"You think you’re trying too hard. \" she said, indifferently.","Dexter blinked, then sighed. \"The vendor forced me to buy all of this,\" he muttered. \"I just wanted to get a few things, and the vendor practically shoved the rest at me.\"","Mira shrugged. \"Do what you want.\"","Her spectral arm extended slowly, trembling slightly with the effort, and gripped the wheel of her chair. She began rolling herself forward toward the bedroom. She didn’t ask Dexter to push her even though she could barely control the Mana arms.","Dexter watched her go, her wheelchair creaking slowly across the floor. He opened his mouth as if to offer assistance, then thought better of it and closed it.","He simply stood there as the last of the three girls disappeared into the bedroom.","He shrugged to himself and turned toward the kitchen.","The moment he stepped inside, the source of the smoke became apparent.","The girls had attempted to make noodles and somehow, impossibly, they had burnt even that.","Dexter chuckled in amusement. The fact that they had tried to cook for him was really nice.","But it also meant he had work to do.","He sighed and rolled up his sleeves.","As he cleaned the kitchen, scrubbing the burnt pot, wiping down the counters, clearing the smoke, then he noticed that the food he had cooked that morning for the girls had also run out. They had eaten everything, or rather Lyra had eaten everything.","So he pulled out the ingredients he had purchased earlier, spread everything across the counter and set to work.","He didn’t use the Diamond rice this time. He already planned on using them once a day.","So he made spaghetti, incorporated with heavenly materials like the cosmic star origin Necter and other herbs that elevated it beyond a simple meal.","Moreover, he used his Heavenly Flame: Emperor Void Flames to make the dish.","The pure white flames cooked the food rapidly.","By the time he finished, a massive pot of steaming plates of beautifully crafted spaghetti sat on the counter.","[Name: MoonFire Pasta]","[Grade: 2 Arcane Meal]","[Effect: Restores 25% of stamina and 15% of mana over five minutes. Increases mana recovery by 10% for the next 30 minutes.]","[Special Effect: Moonfire Warmth — Grants immunity to cold environments below 0°C and increases Fire-attribute spell power by 5% for 20 minutes.]","The aroma filled the kitchen—rich, savory, inviting.","He looked up.","Selene was standing in the doorway of the bedroom, staring directly at him.","He chuckled and thought she was staring at him.","\"Are you hungry?\" But she didn’t answer and stared at his chest instead, reluctance and hesitation on her face.","Beside her stood Lyra. But Lyra wasn’t looking at Dexter. Her gaze was locked firmly on the food, her attention captured entirely by the plates of spaghetti on the counter.","Two girls. Two very different stares. And Dexter stood between them, spatula in hand, wondering what either of them was thinking.","Dexter raised an eyebrow, looking between the two girls standing in the doorway.","\"Are you girls hungry? Do you want to eat?\" He glanced at the clock on the wall. \"It’s still afternoon and a bit early for dinner. But if you want, I can give you a portion of what I made.\"","Lyra nodded immediately. Her mouth was already watering, with her eyes fixed on the steaming plates of spaghetti.","Dexter could feel her voice echoing in his mind","’Give me. Give me. Give me. Give me.’","Over and over, like a hungry child begging for treats.","Dexter chuckled. \"So cute,\" he said—not in his mind, but out loud.","Lyra froze. Her neck flushed a deep crimson that crept up to her ears. But the embarrassment lasted only a fraction of a second before the pull of the food overpowered it.","She remained rooted in place, eyes locked on the plates, waiting with barely contained patience as Dexter scooped a generous portion onto a plate and handed it to her.","Lyra immediately took it and disappeared.","Selene, however, hadn’t moved.","She was still standing there, her white eyes fixed on Dexter.","Dexter frowned slightly and met her gaze spoke gently.","\"You can tell me if you need something. I’ll get it for you. Do you also want a portion of the food?\"","She slowly shook her head.","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"Then what is it?\"","She hesitated. Her lips parted, then closed. Then parted again.","\"I...\" Her voice was barely audible. \"Can I touch you?\"","Dexter blinked.","Touch him?","This was the girl who had always avoided contact, kept her distance, always shied away from him but now she was asking to touch him?","He chuckled at the irony. \"Sure,\" he said. \"You can—\"","He hadn’t even finished the sentence before her hands shot out and grabbed his arm.","She held on to his left arm tightly.","Her fingers wrapped around his forearm and locked there, squeezing as though she feared he might vanish at any moment.","She closed her eyes, pressing herself closer, and took in the warmth radiating from his skin.","\"So warm,\" she whispered unconsciously, her voice soft and dreamy. She sighed a gentle, contented sound that came out like the purr of a kitten. \"So warm. Very warm.\"","Dexter smiled. She was really beautiful. Her white eyes, her delicate features, the way her expression softened when she let her guard down.","It was so stunning it blew Dexter’s mind away for a split second before he recovered."]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97 | Sorting Out Rewards [5th GT]","paragraphs":["Selene held on to his left arm tightly.","Her fingers wrapped around his forearm and locked there, squeezing as though she feared he might vanish at any moment.","She closed her eyes, pressing herself closer, and took in the warmth radiating from his skin.","\"So warm,\" she whispered unconsciously, her voice soft and dreamy. She sighed a gentle, contented sound that came out like the purr of a kitten. \"So warm. Very warm.\"","Dexter smiled. She was really beautiful. Her white eyes, her delicate features, the way her expression softened when she let her guard down.","It was so stunning it blew Dexter’s mind away for a split second before he recovered.","But as she held onto his arm, he noticed something else.","Her body was cold, deeply, unnaturally cold. The kind of cold that seeped through fabric and skin and settled into bone. It crawled up his arm and shot straight down his spine, making him shudder involuntarily. No wonder she had wanted warmth. Her body was practically radiating frost.","Although he shared her pain, he didn’t share her discomfort.","’Should I activate it?’","Dexter pondered a while but then shrugged and activated Flame Will within his body.","His blood heated instantly as it almost turned into molten magma in his body. But with the Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline, he was resistant to the heat.","The change was immediate and dramatic. Heat poured off his skin in waves, turning his arm into a furnace.","\"Mmmh...\"","Selene moaned unconsciously as her grip tightened and her fingers dug in harder, clutching his arm like a child gripping a teddy bear.","She pressed herself against him, absorbing every bit of warmth she could, and purred and moaned continuously and unconsciously as she simply held on, eyes closed, drinking in the heat like a flower turning toward the sun.","They stood there for ten minutes.","Dexter finally leaned down and whispered.","\"Should we head to the living room?\"","Selene didn’t respond. Her eyes remained closed. Her body continued absorbing the heat, and she gave no indication that she had heard him at all.","Dexter sighed.","He began walking slowly, toward the living room. Selene didn’t let go. She shuffled along beside him, her arms still wrapped around his, her eyes still closed, her body still pressed against his side.","When they reached the living room, he settled onto the couch. Selene sat beside him, still hugging his arm, her head gradually drifting down until it rested against his shoulder.","Dexter reached for the remote with his free hand and turned on the television.","The screen flickered to life. He scrolled through the channels—news, news, more news. He hadn’t purchased any subscription packages yet, so the available options were limited to free broadcasts. Everything was either news or mind-numbingly boring.","He kept flipping.","Then he landed on something unexpected.","A telenovela.","The episode was already in progress.","Two characters arguing passionately on screen, their dramatic confrontation underscored by swelling music and tight camera angles. Within moments, Dexter was hooked.","The plot twists came fast and furious, each one more outrageous than the last.","Beside him, Selene’s eyes were still closed. But through her echolocation, she could feel his heart rate spiking up sis she ended up listening to the drama on the tv.","Within minutes, she was as captivated as Dexter was. Her expression shifted with every scene and her eyes widening at shocking reveals.","Sometimes, she would even shake her head shaking slowly when someone did something spectacularly stupid. Occasionally, a small smile would creep onto her face when a character displayed unexpected cleverness.","Dexter didn’t notice any of this. He was too absorbed in the drama unfolding on screen to realize that the girl attached to his arm had quietly become his viewing or better still, his ompanion.","They sat for an hour.","When the episode ended, Dexter sat back, slightly dazed.","\"That was...\" he murmured. \"That was really good.\"","Then he noticed something.","The temperature in the room had dropped.","A cold, biting fury radiated from Selene, it was directed squarely at the television.","Dexter’s eyes traveled downward.","The wooden TV stand beneath the television was frozen.","A layer of frost had crept across its surface. The cold had spread to the wall behind it.","Dexter’s eyes widened.","\"Wait, wait, wait—\" He held up his hands. \"The TV—let’s not break the TV.\"","He lunged for the remote and switched off the television.","He let out a breath he didn’t realize he’d been holding, then turned to Selene.","\"So,\" he said, his voice careful and measured. \"You like telenovelas?\"","Selene blinked.","Her eyes focused—as though she were waking from a dream. She looked down at her hands, still wrapped around Dexter’s arm. She looked at the frost-covered TV stand. She looked at the ice crawling up the wall.","The realization hit her all at once.","She immediately released his arm instantly, as though it had burned her. A deep blush erupted across her cheeks. It was so vivid against her pale skin. She stumbled backward, turned, and fled the room like a rabbit being pursued by the predator as she disappeared down the hallway toward the bedroom.","Dexter stood there, arm suddenly cold and empty.","He touched his nose, a crooked smile spreading across his face.","\"After you used me, now you’re abandoning me.\"","He stood there for a moment longer, shaking his head softly. Then he turned off the lights in the living room and headed to his own room.","It was time to cultivate.","And more importantly, it was time to sort out his previous rewards.","[1. Professional Rank Promotion: Great Grandmaster Foodsmith (Early Stage) ➔ Great Grandmaster Foodsmith (Middle Stage)]","[2. Special Physical Constitution: Heavenly Gastronomy Body]","[3. Elemental Evolution: Alchemist Flame ➔ 9th Heavenly Flame: Emperor Void Flame]","[4. Raw Materials: 1,000kg of Premium Diamond Rice]","[5. Rare Liquids: 100kg of Cosmic Star Origin Nectar]","[6. Premium Alcohol: 100kg of Burning Sun Lava Wine]","[7. Talent Evolution: Mana Affinity (SS-Rank) ➔ Mana Affinity (SSS-Rank)]"]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98 | Heaven Gastronomy Body [6th]","paragraphs":["[1. Professional Rank Promotion: Great Grandmaster Foodsmith (Early Stage) ➔ Great Grandmaster Foodsmith (Middle Stage)]","[2. Special Physical Constitution: Heavenly Gastronomy Body]","[3. Elemental Evolution: Alchemist Flame ➔ 9th Heavenly Flame: Emperor Void Flame]","[4. Raw Materials: 1,000kg of Premium Diamond Rice]","[5. Rare Liquids: 100kg of Cosmic Star Origin Nectar]","[6. Premium Alcohol: 100kg of Burning Sun Lava Wine]","[7. Talent Evolution: Mana Affinity (SS-Rank) ➔ Mana Affinity (SSS-Rank)]","...","[Name: Heavenly Gastronomy Body]","[Grade: Divine Constitution]","[Description:","A legendary physique said to have been created by the Heavenly God of Cuisine. Every ingredient consumed is perfectly refined, allowing the body to absorb 100% of its nutritional, spiritual, and magical essence while eliminating all impurities.","Unlike ordinary physiques that merely strengthen the body, the Heavenly Gastronomy Body transforms every meal into cultivation. The rarer and more powerful the ingredients, the greater the evolution of the user’s body.]","[Passive Abilities]","• Cooking Efficiency: +200%","• Alchemy Success Rate: +200%","• Fire Attribute Damage: +200%","• Infinite Nutrient Absorption","Absorbs 100% of all nutrients, mana, spiritual essence, and life force contained within food.","• Gourmet Evolution","Every first-time consumption of a rare ingredient permanently increases one or more attributes.","• Arcane Metabolism","Magical meals grant twice their original effects and their duration is increased by 100%.","• Monster Cuisine","The flesh of magical beasts, dragons, demons, and divine creatures can be safely consumed regardless of toxicity.","• Culinary Insight","Instantly understands the quality, freshness, rarity, grade, and hidden effects of any ingredient upon sight.","• Divine Appetite","The body instinctively craves ingredients capable of triggering future evolutions.","[Current Evolution Stage]","Heavenly Gastronomy Body (Awakened)","...","[Name: Emperor Void Flame]","[Classification: 9th Heavenly Flame]","[Grade: Divine]","[Description:","One of the Nine Heavenly Flames in the world. The Emperor Void Flame burns not only matter but souls and even strong enough, can burn even mana, curses, and even fragments of space itself. It possesses intelligence and recognizes only a single master.]","[Abilities]","• Absolute Incineration","Burns nearly anything regardless of elemental resistance.","• Void Devour","Consumes other flames and permanently strengthens itself.","• Heavenly Refinement","Raises the success rate of forging, alchemy, cooking, and enchantments by 500%","• Soul Flame","Damages both the physical body and the soul simultaneously.","• Emperor’s Dominion","All flames of lower rank become suppressed within a large radius.","• Flame Regeneration","The user rapidly regenerates stamina, mana, and injuries while surrounded by the Emperor Void Flame.","• World Scorch","Creates a domain where everything within is gradually consumed by divine void fire.","[Passive Effects]","• Fire Resistance: ∞","• Poison Resistance: 100%","• Heat Resistance: Absolute","• Cooking Efficiency: +500%","• Alchemy Success Rate: +300%","• Fire Attribute Damage: +1000%","• Mana Consumption of Fire Skills: -70%","...","Dexter was quite satisfied with the physique and also the heavenly flames. With them, failing to cook headed meals would be impossible.","In fact, if he knowingly wanted to cook ordinary meals, it would automatically be Arcane meals, making it physically impossible for Dexter to cook ordinary meals.","’ Sigh, it’s so lonely at the top.’","As a Great Grandmaster food Amith, barely anyone in the entire Stargate city could rival his cooking ability!","’ Maybe I should become a chef and sell my food for money.’","The more he thought about it, the more the idea expanded in his head and he smiled. \"Perfect. I will start after the sparring battle.\"","As for the heavenly flames, he wondered if that’s the reason Selene clung to him. Since it could melt anything in the world, does it mean it could melt the Eternal Winter Ice that was afflicting her?","He would find a time to test this theory. He simply needed to wait for her to come to him. She was like a rabbit after all.","He then began pondering other things.","Why hadn’t he gotten his rewards yet from the system?","But he figured out that probably because the beds hadn’t arrived yet so the system couldn’t calculate his rewards based on what the girls hadn’t seen and reacted to yet.","Dexter returned to his room feeling deeply satisfied. The power coursing through his veins was a constant reminder of how far he had come in such a short time.","However, rather than resting, he immediately sat cross-legged on his airbed and closed his eyes, intending to use the remaining hours of the afternoon to cultivate.","He had barely begun circulating the Limitless Grand Cosmos Scripture when a sudden, sharp warning flared at the back of his mind.","It was his Frost Sense.","Selene.","Her internal cold energy was spiking rapidly which meant she was about to have a seizure.","Dexter’s eyes snapped open instantly. He lunged toward the pile of groceries and supply bags he had left beside his bed, until his fingers closed around the ice-suppressing serum.","Gripping the syringe tightly, Dexter activated Flame Burst.","\"BOOM!\"","A violent explosion of heat erupted beneath his feet. The air in his small bedroom distorted wildly as his body became a blur of crimson light.","He vanished from his room, leaving behind a scorch mark on the floorboards and a wave of displaced air that sent his bedsheets flying.","The lady’s room was dim as the curtains were half-drawn. The three wives were arranged in a loose circle.","Mira sat in her wheelchair near the bedside, facing the mattress.","Lyra and Selene sat cross-legged on the bed, and resting at the center of their triangle was the massive, dragon-scaled ancient beast egg as they cultivated around it.","\"Bam!\"","Dexter burst through the girls’ bedroom without knocking.","The sudden commotion drew their attention. Mira cracked one eye open, glanced at him with indifference, and then closed it again, resuming her meditation without a word.","Lyra peered at him curiously through her type 2 AI smart glasses wondering why he came and if he brought something with him.","While Selene simply raised her slender pale arm, presenting it to Dexter.","\"I’m sorry for barging in,\" Dexter said quickly as he stepped toward the bed.","He lined the syringe up against Selene’s exposed wrist and pressed the plunger, injecting the warm, thick serum directly into her bloodstream."]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99 | Dinner’s Ready","paragraphs":["The moment the needle pierced her skin, Dexter felt the pain instead of Selene feeling the sharp prick of the needle, because ikf the Ring of Shared Burdens.","As the serum entered her system, Selene inhaled deeply.","The violent tremors that had begun to ripple through her body slowly subsided and her breathing steadied, the dangerous buildup of frost within her body began to recede.","Unconsciously, her cold fingers wrapped tightly around Dexter’s forearm, pulling it closer to her body as she sought out the comforting warmth radiating from his Flame Demon bloodline.","Dexter administered the full dose and carefully withdrew the empty syringe. But Selene still didn’t let go.","He stood there in an increasingly awkward position. He was hunched slightly over the bed, one arm trapped in Selene’s surprisingly strong grip.","Mira sat mere feet away with her eyes closed, though there was a fault smirk at the corner of her lips,","Meanwhile, Lyra kept glancing curiously at Dexter.","’This foodie.’","Dexter could tell immediately what Lyra wanted. He made a mental note to buy a variety of snacks the next time he went out, something she could munch on whenever she felt hungry between meals.","That way, she wouldn’t have to wait for him to cook every time her bottomless stomach demanded attention.","After a few more minutes of standing there like a human radiator, Dexter gently tapped Selene’s hand.","\"Selene,\" he whispered. \"It’s done. You can let go now.\"","Her eyes fluttered open. For a brief, disoriented moment, she seemed confused about why Dexter was saying to let go.","Then she immediately realized she had been holding him all these time.","\"I- sorry.\"","Her pale cheeks flushed and she immediately released his arm as if his skin were burning hot.","She quickly pulled her hand back to her lap and lowered her head, unable to meet his gaze.","Dexter chuckled softly, pocketed the empty syringe, and turned to leave. As he reached the doorway, he paused and glanced back at the three girls.","Then he quietly closed the door behind him and returned to his room.","***","Sitting back down on his bed, Dexter reached into his system storage and pulled out three shimmering crystals.","They were the Bloodline Evolution Stones, the rewards he had received from the system quite some time ago.","In the chaos and emotional turbulence of the past few days, he had nearly forgotten they existed.","A Bloodline Evolution Stone was a priceless treasure.","According to the system, it could grant an entirely new bloodline to someone who possessed none, or it could evolve an existing bloodline by one full grade.","With these stones, the girls could potentially awaken bloodlines that would drastically increase their overall strength, accelerate their healing, and amplify their existing talents.","He had three stones. One for each wife.","The question was how to give them. If he simply handed the crystals over, the girls would immediately bombard him with questions about where he obtained such impossibly rare treasures. They were already suspicious of him after the second awakenings. Handing them bloodline stones would only add fuel to that fire.","He would need to find a subtle way to deliver them, perhaps integrating them into their meals, or slipping them into their bodies while they slept.","For now, he placed the three stones carefully back into his storage ring and closed his eyes.","It was time to cultivate.","Dexter sank deep into meditation and the two blazing Star Nodes within his inner universe began to spin, generating a powerful gravitational force that reached outward into the physical world.","Across the hallway, the three girls resumed their own cultivation of the Grand Cosmos Scripture.","Mira’s five awakened Star Nodes hummed with power. Selene’s four nodes pulsed steadily. And Lyra’s two nodes rotated along.","As the four of them cultivated simultaneously, something extraordinary began to happen.","Invisible currents of mana started flowing through the entire house.","But as the minutes passed and their absorption rates climbed, the flow intensified dramatically.","The mana in the surrounding neighborhood began to drift toward the bungalow.","The phenomenon was identical to what had occurred the day before.","A Mana Hurricane.","There was no wind. No physical force moved through the house. Yet the window curtains billowed outward as if caught in a violent gale.","Outside, anyone with even a basic sensitivity to mana would have felt it if it weren’t for the protective barrier.","Dexter didn’t fully understand the phenomenon himself. He knew it was a byproduct of their cultivation, but he didn’t realize the true significance.","Three girls with S-Rank mana affinity and one man with an SSS-Rank affinity, all cultivating simultaneously using a 7th-Tier technique and 9th tier technique.","It was like placing four massive vacuum tubes in a single small room and turning them all on at maximum power.","Dexter cultivated through the afternoon and deep into the evening.","\"RIIIIIING!\"","He only stopped when the alarm on his phone rang out, breaking his meditation.","He had meticulously set alarms for every meal, as well as an alarm every four to five hours specifically to take Mira to the restroom.","It was a necessary schedule, given her paralysis.","Rising from his bed, he walked to the girls’ bedroom door and knocked twice.","Come in, ’ a soft, melodic voice echoed directly inside his mind.","Dexter chuckled. Even after hearing it a few times, Lyra’s telepathic voice was endearingly cute.","\"It’s dinner time already,\" Dexter projected back, leaning against the doorframe. \"You guys should come and—\"","He hadn’t even finished the sentence before the door snapped open. Lyra’s face popped out, her eyes wide and sparkling with hunger.","Dexter let out a laugh and pointed toward the kitchen. She didn’t need to be told twice; she practically teleported toward the dining table.","Feeling Lyra move away, Selene opened her eyes.","\"Dinner is ready,\" Dexter told her softly. He then looked toward Mira. \"Dinner is ready, Mira.\"","Selene nodded and stood up. She glanced between Dexter and Mira’s wheelchair, but Dexter simply shrugged. \"I’ll take her. You go ahead.\""]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100 | Hope!","paragraphs":["Selene opened her eyes.","\"Dinner is ready,\" Dexter told her softly. He then looked toward Mira. \"Dinner is ready, Mira.\"","Selene nodded and stood up. She glanced between Dexter and Mira’s wheelchair, but Dexter simply shrugged. \"I’ll take her. You go ahead.\"","Selene nodded and left the room. Mira kept her eyes closed as Dexter stepped behind her wheelchair.","\"I’m cultivating,\" Mira stated flatly, her voice carrying a hint of annoyance at being interrupted.","Dexter chuckled, unlocking the wheels. \"Okay, do something about it then.\"","Mira cracked one eye open to glare at him, but seeing his amused smile, she simply closed her eyes again and conceded.","Instead of heading straight to the kitchen, Dexter wheeled her into the bathroom. For the first time since they had moved in, she was wearing trousers instead of a dress, which made the process slightly different. With practiced efficiency, Dexter removed her trousers and panties, lifting her carefully and placing her on the toilet.","Both of them remained silent. Even after doing this countless times, a faint flush still crept up Mira’s pale cheeks.","Dexter’s neck was also slightly red, but his face remained perfectly indifferent.","\"Call me when you’re done,\" he said, stepping outside the bathroom to wait.","He listened for the rush of water, waiting thirty seconds after the sound faded before stepping back inside. He dressed Mira, flushed the toilet, and lifted her back into her wheelchair.","Pushing her out to the dining table, he found Lyra and Selene already waiting.","Dexter hadn’t dished out the food yet. Lyra was staring at the covered pots with ravenous intensity, while Selene sat with her eyes closed.","She no longer needed to keep her eyes open to see; her Echolocation talent painted a perfect three-dimensional map of her surroundings through sound and vibration.","Dexter served the meals. He placed a portion in front of Selene, and her hand immediately snapped out, accurately finding the fork without needing any guidance.","\"Nice!\"","Dexter smiled at her progress.","Next, he placed three extra portions in front of Lyra, who instantly dove into her food.","The moment the first forkful of pasta entered her mouth, she sighed exaggeratedly, her eyes fluttering shut as the heavenly taste burst across her taste buds.","She swallowed and immediately shoved another bite in, sighing in contentment again.","Finally, Dexter placed the plate in front of Mira. He picked up the fork, about to feed her as usual, but Mira shook her head.","\"Let me try feeding myself,\" she said quietly.","Dexter raised an eyebrow, frowning slightly. \"You aren’t really proficient with the arms yet.\"","\"If I don’t try, how will I become proficient?\" Mira countered, meeting his gaze stubbornly.","Dexter shrugged. \"As long as the food doesn’t spill.\"","Mira rolled her eyes. Two glowing orange spectral arms materialized behind her shoulders.","Selene watched curiously, while Lyra couldn’t care less, her mind was entirely devoted to devouring her pasta.","Mira controlled one of the spectral arms. It reached down, clumsily wrapping translucent fingers around the iron fork.","It lifted the pasta, trembling slightly from the uneven mana distribution. Mira opened her mouth, leaning forward to receive the bite.","\"Snap.\"","The iron fork instantly shattered into tiny pieces, crushed to dust by her inability to regulate the spectral arm’s strength. The pasta tumbled down, staining her clean clothes.","Mira froze, her eyes unblinking but she was stubbornly refusing to be humiliated.","Dexter didn’t say a word.","He simply stood up, walked to the drawer, brought out ten more forks, and set them on the table beside her plate.","Then, he sat back down, picked up his own fork, and continued eating as if destroying cutlery was a perfectly normal dinner event.","Mira glanced at him, her heart skipping a beat.","A warm, unfamiliar feeling trickled into her chest as she knew Dexter was actually considering her feelings and didn’t want to embarrass her.","Swallowing her pride, she grabbed another fork with her spectral arm and tried again.","It took her seven attempts. Six crushed forks and stained napkins later, she finally managed to regulate the pressure, guiding a neat bite of pasta into her mouth.","Dexter looked up, gave her a thumbs-up, and smiled. \"Nice.\"","Mira rolled her eyes, though a tiny, reluctant smile tugged at her lips.","She continued to feed herself. It was incredibly slow.","But thanks to the properties of his Grade-Two cooking, the meal never lost its heat or its taste, remaining perfectly warm as if freshly cooked even after hours on the plate.","It took an hour and half for Mira to finish her dinner, but by the end of it, her proficiency with the spectral arms had increased drastically.","Dexter was genuinely happy; she could finally feed herself.","After dinner, the girls went to freshen up. When Dexter offered to help Mira bathe, she shook her head.","\"I don’t need to bathe twice a day,\" she muttered. \"Once is enough. I’ll bathe tomorrow.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"Alright.\"","He wished the girls goodnight and retreated to his room to cultivate.","He suddenly remembered he was in pain as the Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture tempered his organs.","The chronic pain absorbed from the girls was a constant, agonizing companion, but the scripture was slowly converting that suffering into raw strength.","To bear it, he forced himself into a deep meditative trance. He mediated for five solid hours before exhaustion finally pulled him into a dreamless sleep.","***","Later that night, inside the girls’ bedroom, the room was silent.","Mira was lying at the edge of the bed. Her eyes were open, staring blankly at the ceiling as she silently cultivated the Grand Cosmos Scripture.","Suddenly, she felt it.","A phantom sensation. She had felt them countless times over the past three years the cruel, psychological torture of thinking she could move her limbs, only to realize it was just a phantom sensation from her severed nerves.","But this time, it felt... different. More real.","Out of curiosity, Mira shifted her gaze to the corner of her eye, looking down at her right hand resting on the mattress.","Suddenly, her expression changed as her breathing froze.","She could see something moving and that something was actually her index finger!","It wasn’t a phantom sensation but was real instead! And she was actually moving her finger!","Without knowing, tears fell down her eyes and rolled down the side of her head, soaking into the pillow.","She didn’t sniffle or make a sound, as if terrified that if she acknowledged it too loudly, the miracle would vanish. She just lay there, crying silently as a wave of desperate, long-abandoned hope crashed over her like a tide!"]}]);
